window.HC_ARTICLES = {"getting-started":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Logging in to Your Account","blurb":"Your Admin Portal is the command center for everything in R-Link Studio — managing your rooms, team, billing, and settings. This guide walks you through accessing it for the first time and getting oriented.","html":"<p>Your Admin Portal is the command center for everything in R-Link Studio — managing your rooms, team, billing, and settings. This guide walks you through accessing it for the first time and getting oriented.</p>","text":"Your Admin Portal is the command center for everything in R-Link Studio — managing your rooms, team, billing, and settings. This guide walks you through accessing it for the first time and getting oriented.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Resetting Your Password","blurb":"Locked out of your Admin Portal? Reset your own password from the login screen using a 6-digit code sent to your email — no support ticket needed. This guide walks through the whole flow.","html":"<p>Locked out of your Admin Portal? Reset your own password from the login screen using a 6-digit code sent to your email — no support ticket needed. This guide walks through the whole flow.</p><div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">1</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Click \"Forgot Password?\" on the login screen</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">On the <a href=\"https://studio.r-link.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><code>studio.r-link.com</code></a> login page, click <strong>Forgot Password?</strong> beneath the password field.</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">2</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Enter your email address</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Type the email address on your R-Link account and click <strong>Send Reset Link</strong>.</div>\n            <div class=\"real-screenshot\"><div class=\"src-img-placeholder\" data-alt=\"Reset Password Enter Your Email\"><span><svg width=\"40\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg></span><span>Screenshot: Reset Password Enter Your Email</span></div></div>\n            <p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Reset Password screen — enter your email to receive a reset link</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">3</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Check your email for the reset link or code</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">If an account exists with that address, you'll receive a <strong>6-digit reset code</strong> shortly. Click the link in the email, or click <strong>Enter Reset Code</strong> and type the code on the reset page.</div>\n            <div class=\"real-screenshot\"><div class=\"src-img-placeholder\" data-alt=\"Reset Password Check Your Email for a Reset Link\"><span><svg width=\"40\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg></span><span>Screenshot: Reset Password Check Your Email for a Reset Link</span></div></div>\n            <p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Confirmation that the reset email is on its way — use the link or the 6-digit code</p>\n            <div class=\"callout note\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">📬</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">No email after a few minutes?</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">Check your spam and junk folders, and confirm you entered the address your account was created with. Still nothing? Contact the R-Link support team at <strong>support@r-link.com</strong>.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">4</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Set a new password</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">On the <strong>Set a New Password</strong> screen, enter your email address, the <strong>6-digit code</strong> from your email, then your new password and confirm it. Passwords must be <strong>at least 10 characters</strong>. Click <strong>Reset Password</strong>, then use <strong>Back to Login</strong> to sign in with your new credentials.</div>\n            <div class=\"real-screenshot\"><div class=\"src-img-placeholder\" data-alt=\"Set a New Password Enter Code and Choose Password\"><span><svg width=\"40\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg></span><span>Screenshot: Set a New Password Enter Code and Choose Password</span></div></div>\n            <p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Enter the 6-digit code from your email and choose a new password</p>\n            <div class=\"callout note\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">🔄</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">Code expired or lost?</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">Click <strong>Request a new code</strong> at the bottom of the form to have a fresh 6-digit code emailed to you.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"callout tip\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">💡</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">Already know your current password?</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">You don't need the reset flow — you can change it from inside the Admin Portal. See <strong>Changing Your Password</strong> in Account &amp; Billing.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>","text":"Locked out of your Admin Portal? Reset your own password from the login screen using a 6-digit code sent to your email — no support ticket needed. This guide walks through the whole flow. Step-by-step 1 Click \"Forgot Password?\" on the login screen On the studio.r-link.com login page, click Forgot Password? beneath the password field. 2 Enter your email address Type the email address on your R-Link account and click Send Reset Link . Screenshot: Reset Password Enter Your Email ↑ The Reset Password screen — enter your email to receive a reset link 3 Check your email for the reset link or code If an account exists with that address, you'll receive a 6-digit reset code shortly. Click the link in the email, or click Enter Reset Code and type the code on the reset page. Screenshot: Reset Password Check Your Email for a Reset Link ↑ Confirmation that the reset email is on its way — use the link or the 6-digit code 📬 No email after a few minutes? Check your spam and junk folders, and confirm you entered the address your account was created with. Still nothing? Contact the R-Link support team at support@r-link.com . 4 Set a new password On the Set a New Password screen, enter your email address, the 6-digit code from your email, then your new password and confirm it. Passwords must be at least 10 characters . Click Reset Password , then use Back to Login to sign in with your new credentials. Screenshot: Set a New Password Enter Code and Choose Password ↑ Enter the 6-digit code from your email and choose a new password 🔄 Code expired or lost? Click Request a new code at the bottom of the form to have a fresh 6-digit code emailed to you. 💡 Already know your current password? You don't need the reset flow — you can change it from inside the Admin Portal. See Changing Your Password in Account &amp; Billing.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"User Profile","blurb":"Your Profile tab is your personal R-Link Studio identity — display name, photo, phone, timezone, and your password. This guide covers both sections.","html":"<p>Your Profile tab is your personal R-Link Studio identity — display name, photo, phone, timezone, and your password. This guide covers both sections.</p>\n      <div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">1</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Open Settings</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">In your Admin Portal, click <strong>Settings</strong> in the left sidebar (under the <strong>Account</strong> section). Settings is organized into tabs across the top — <strong>Profile</strong>, <strong>Account</strong>, <strong>Team &amp; Users</strong>, <strong>Integrations</strong>, and <strong>AI Suite</strong>. This guide covers the <strong>Profile</strong> tab, where your personal identity and password live.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">2</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Profile</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Profile</strong> tab — this is your personal R-Link Studio identity. At the top, upload a profile <strong>photo</strong> (a square JPG or PNG, max 3&nbsp;MB). Under <strong>Personal Information</strong> you can edit your <strong>Display Name</strong>, <strong>Phone</strong>, and <strong>Timezone</strong>. When you're done, click <strong>Save Changes</strong>.</p>\n            <div class=\"real-screenshot\">\n              <div class=\"src-img-placeholder\" data-alt=\"R-Link Studio Profile Settings page\"><span><svg width=\"40\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg></span><span>Screenshot: Profile tab</span></div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Profile tab — your personal R-Link Studio identity</p>\n            <div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:12px;\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">Your email is your sign-in identity</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">The email field is locked because it's tied to how you sign in. To change it, contact our support team.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">3</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Password</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Still on the <strong>Profile</strong> tab, scroll to the <strong>Password</strong> section. Enter your <strong>Current Password</strong>, then your <strong>New Password</strong> (at least 10 characters), and re-enter it under <strong>Confirm Password</strong>. Click <strong>Update Password</strong> to save.</p>\n            <div class=\"callout tip\" style=\"margin-top:12px;\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">💡</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">Locked out instead?</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">This section is for changing your password while you're signed in. If you can't log in at all, see <a href=\"#getting-started/art-1\">Resetting Your Password</a>.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"art-divider\"></div>\n\n      <div class=\"helpful\">\n        <p>Was this article helpful?</p>\n        <div class=\"helpful-btns\">\n          <button class=\"hbtn yes\" onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button>\n          <button class=\"hbtn\" onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","text":"Your Profile tab is your personal R-Link Studio identity — display name, photo, phone, timezone, and your password. This guide covers both sections. Step-by-step 1 Open Settings In your Admin Portal, click Settings in the left sidebar (under the Account section). Settings is organized into tabs across the top — Profile , Account , Team &amp; Users , Integrations , and AI Suite . This guide covers the Profile tab, where your personal identity and password live. 2 Profile Open the Profile tab — this is your personal R-Link Studio identity. At the top, upload a profile photo (a square JPG or PNG, max 3&nbsp;MB). Under Personal Information you can edit your Display Name , Phone , and Timezone . When you're done, click Save Changes . Screenshot: Profile tab ↑ The Profile tab — your personal R-Link Studio identity 📌 Your email is your sign-in identity The email field is locked because it's tied to how you sign in. To change it, contact our support team. 3 Password Still on the Profile tab, scroll to the Password section. Enter your Current Password , then your New Password (at least 10 characters), and re-enter it under Confirm Password . Click Update Password to save. 💡 Locked out instead? This section is for changing your password while you're signed in. If you can't log in at all, see Resetting Your Password . Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Dashboard Overview","blurb":"The Dashboard is the first thing you see after logging in. Here's a tour of the sidebar, the top bar, the quick-start actions, and the panels that track what's live, scheduled and recorded.","html":"<p>The Dashboard is the first thing you see after logging in. Here's a tour of the sidebar, the top bar, the quick-start actions, and the panels that track what's live, scheduled and recorded.</p>\n      <p class=\"step-desc\" style=\"margin-bottom:20px\">The Dashboard is the first thing you see after logging in. It gives you a live picture of your account — what's running, what's scheduled, and where everything lives.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"real-screenshot\">\n              <div class=\"src-img-placeholder\" data-alt=\"Admin Dashboard Overview\"><span><svg width=\"40\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg></span><span>Screenshot: Admin Dashboard</span></div>\n            </div>\n      <p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Admin Dashboard — your landing view after logging in</p>\n\n      <div class=\"steps\" style=\"margin-top:28px\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">What's on the page</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">1</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Left sidebar navigation</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Everything in R-Link Studio is reachable from the left sidebar, grouped into three sections. <strong>Workspace</strong> holds <strong>Dashboard</strong>, <strong>Sessions</strong>, <strong>Recordings</strong>, <strong>Rooms</strong>, and <strong>Studio Assets</strong>. <strong>Grow</strong> holds <strong>Monetize</strong>, <strong>Branding</strong>, <strong>Analytics</strong>, and <strong>Affiliate</strong>. <strong>Account</strong> holds <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong>, <strong>Settings</strong>, and <strong>Support</strong>. Use the <strong>«</strong> button at the top to collapse the sidebar into icons.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">2</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Your organization and plan</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">The card at the top of the sidebar shows your organization name and current plan. Your own account sits at the bottom of the sidebar with your name and sign-in email. For usage counts and plan changes, open <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong>.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">3</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Top bar, search and notifications</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">The breadcrumb on the left tells you where you are. The search box in the middle searches sessions, rooms and leads — press <strong>⌘K</strong> to jump straight to it. On the right, a counter shows how many rooms are live, the bell icon holds your notifications, and <strong>Go Live</strong> (shortcut <strong>G</strong>) starts a session immediately.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">4</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Quick start — Start a meeting or Schedule</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">The welcome panel carries the two actions you'll use most. <strong>Start a meeting</strong> takes you live in a room right away. <strong>Schedule</strong> opens the scheduling flow for a future meeting or webinar. A status pill above them tells you when your studio is warmed up and ready.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">5</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Live Now</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">The panel on the right tracks rooms that are live this moment. When nothing is running it reads <strong>No live rooms yet</strong>; the moment you go live, it starts showing active rooms.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">6</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Summary cards</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Four cards summarize your account at a glance: <strong>Today</strong> (sessions scheduled for today), <strong>Upcoming</strong> (sessions still ahead), <strong>Total Rooms</strong>, and <strong>Recordings</strong>. Each card shows a trend line alongside the count.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">7</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Upcoming &amp; Live, and Recent leads</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Below the cards, <strong>Upcoming &amp; Live</strong> lists your next sessions so you can start or edit them without leaving the page. <strong>Recent leads</strong> shows the latest registrations captured by your events. Both have a <strong>View all</strong> link through to the full list.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:22px;\">\n        <div class=\"callout-icon\">🧭</div>\n        <div class=\"callout-body\">\n          <div class=\"callout-title\">Where to find each feature</div>\n          <div class=\"callout-text\">Scheduled meetings and webinars live under <strong>Sessions</strong>. Saved recordings are under <strong>Recordings</strong>. Rooms and their URLs are under <strong>Rooms</strong>. Logos and backgrounds are under <strong>Branding</strong> and <strong>Studio Assets</strong>. Invoices, plan and usage are under <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong>. Profile, organization and team settings are under <strong>Settings</strong>.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"art-divider\"></div>\n\n      <div class=\"helpful\">\n        <p>Was this article helpful?</p>\n        <div class=\"helpful-btns\">\n          <button class=\"hbtn yes\" onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button>\n          <button class=\"hbtn\" onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","text":"The Dashboard is the first thing you see after logging in. Here's a tour of the sidebar, the top bar, the quick-start actions, and the panels that track what's live, scheduled and recorded. The Dashboard is the first thing you see after logging in. It gives you a live picture of your account — what's running, what's scheduled, and where everything lives. Screenshot: Admin Dashboard ↑ The Admin Dashboard — your landing view after logging in What's on the page 1 Left sidebar navigation Everything in R-Link Studio is reachable from the left sidebar, grouped into three sections. Workspace holds Dashboard , Sessions , Recordings , Rooms , and Studio Assets . Grow holds Monetize , Branding , Analytics , and Affiliate . Account holds Billing &amp; Usage , Settings , and Support . Use the « button at the top to collapse the sidebar into icons. 2 Your organization and plan The card at the top of the sidebar shows your organization name and current plan. Your own account sits at the bottom of the sidebar with your name and sign-in email. For usage counts and plan changes, open Billing &amp; Usage . 3 Top bar, search and notifications The breadcrumb on the left tells you where you are. The search box in the middle searches sessions, rooms and leads — press ⌘K to jump straight to it. On the right, a counter shows how many rooms are live, the bell icon holds your notifications, and Go Live (shortcut G ) starts a session immediately. 4 Quick start — Start a meeting or Schedule The welcome panel carries the two actions you'll use most. Start a meeting takes you live in a room right away. Schedule opens the scheduling flow for a future meeting or webinar. A status pill above them tells you when your studio is warmed up and ready. 5 Live Now The panel on the right tracks rooms that are live this moment. When nothing is running it reads No live rooms yet ; the moment you go live, it starts showing active rooms. 6 Summary cards Four cards summarize your account at a glance: Today (sessions scheduled for today), Upcoming (sessions still ahead), Total Rooms , and Recordings . Each card shows a trend line alongside the count. 7 Upcoming &amp; Live, and Recent leads Below the cards, Upcoming &amp; Live lists your next sessions so you can start or edit them without leaving the page. Recent leads shows the latest registrations captured by your events. Both have a View all link through to the full list. 🧭 Where to find each feature Scheduled meetings and webinars live under Sessions . Saved recordings are under Recordings . Rooms and their URLs are under Rooms . Logos and backgrounds are under Branding and Studio Assets . Invoices, plan and usage are under Billing &amp; Usage . Profile, organization and team settings are under Settings . Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-4","title":"Account Settings","blurb":"The Account tab holds your organization's details — name, owner, regional defaults, legal and privacy information, and the Danger Zone.","html":"<p>The Account tab holds your organization's details — name, owner, regional defaults, legal and privacy information, and the Danger Zone.</p>\n      <div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">1</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Open the Account tab</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">In your Admin Portal, click <strong>Settings</strong> in the left sidebar (under the <strong>Account</strong> section), then open the <strong>Account</strong> tab. This tab holds your organization's details, as distinct from your personal <a href=\"#getting-started/art-2\">User Profile</a>.</p>\n            <div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:12px;\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">🔗</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">Looking for Google Calendar?</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">Calendar connections now live under the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. See the dedicated Integrations guide to connect Google Calendar.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">2</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Organization Details</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Under <strong>Organization Details</strong> you can set your <strong>Company / Organization Name</strong>, <strong>Owner / Admin Name</strong>, and an optional <strong>Phone</strong> number.</p>\n            <div class=\"real-screenshot\">\n              <div class=\"src-img-placeholder\" data-alt=\"R-Link Studio Account Settings page\"><span><svg width=\"40\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg></span><span>Screenshot: Account tab</span></div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Account tab — manage your organization's basic information</p>\n            <div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:12px;\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">🔒</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">Owner email is locked</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">The Contact Email is locked to the sign-in identity. Contact support to change it.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">3</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Regional Settings</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Below Organization Details, the <strong>Regional Settings</strong> section lets you choose your <strong>Timezone</strong> and <strong>Default Locale / Language</strong>. These set the defaults for your whole organization. Click <strong>Save Changes</strong> when you're finished.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">4</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Legal &amp; Privacy</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">Further down the Account tab, <strong>Legal &amp; Privacy</strong> collects your organization's legal and privacy information.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\">\n          <div class=\"step-num\">5</div>\n          <div class=\"step-body\">\n            <h3 class=\"step-title\">Danger Zone</h3>\n            <p class=\"step-desc\">The <strong>Danger Zone</strong> sits at the bottom of the Account tab and holds destructive, account-level actions.</p>\n            <div class=\"callout warning\" style=\"margin-top:12px;\">\n              <div class=\"callout-icon\">⚠</div>\n              <div class=\"callout-body\">\n                <div class=\"callout-title\">These actions can't be undone</div>\n                <div class=\"callout-text\">Anything in the Danger Zone affects your whole organization. Read each confirmation prompt carefully before continuing, and contact <strong>support@r-link.com</strong> if you're unsure.</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"art-divider\"></div>\n\n      <div class=\"helpful\">\n        <p>Was this article helpful?</p>\n        <div class=\"helpful-btns\">\n          <button class=\"hbtn yes\" onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button>\n          <button class=\"hbtn\" onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","text":"The Account tab holds your organization's details — name, owner, regional defaults, legal and privacy information, and the Danger Zone. Step-by-step 1 Open the Account tab In your Admin Portal, click Settings in the left sidebar (under the Account section), then open the Account tab. This tab holds your organization's details, as distinct from your personal User Profile . 🔗 Looking for Google Calendar? Calendar connections now live under the Integrations tab. See the dedicated Integrations guide to connect Google Calendar. 2 Organization Details Under Organization Details you can set your Company / Organization Name , Owner / Admin Name , and an optional Phone number. Screenshot: Account tab ↑ The Account tab — manage your organization's basic information 🔒 Owner email is locked The Contact Email is locked to the sign-in identity. Contact support to change it. 3 Regional Settings Below Organization Details, the Regional Settings section lets you choose your Timezone and Default Locale / Language . These set the defaults for your whole organization. Click Save Changes when you're finished. 4 Legal &amp; Privacy Further down the Account tab, Legal &amp; Privacy collects your organization's legal and privacy information. 5 Danger Zone The Danger Zone sits at the bottom of the Account tab and holds destructive, account-level actions. ⚠ These actions can't be undone Anything in the Danger Zone affects your whole organization. Read each confirmation prompt carefully before continuing, and contact support@r-link.com if you're unsure. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-5","title":"Setting Up Your Room","blurb":"Before you go live, take a few minutes to set up your room. A well-configured room means a smoother, more professional experience for you and everyone who joins.","html":"<p>Before you go live, take a few minutes to set up your room. A well-configured room means a smoother, more professional experience for you and everyone who joins.</p>","text":"Before you go live, take a few minutes to set up your room. A well-configured room means a smoother, more professional experience for you and everyone who joins.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-6","title":"Starting Your First Meeting","blurb":"Ready to host your first live session? This guide walks you through launching a meeting in R-Link Studio — from your dashboard all the way to welcoming your first participant into the room.","html":"<p>Ready to host your first live session? This guide walks you through launching a meeting in R-Link Studio — from your dashboard all the way to welcoming your first participant into the room.</p>","text":"Ready to host your first live session? This guide walks you through launching a meeting in R-Link Studio — from your dashboard all the way to welcoming your first participant into the room.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-7","title":"Your Room URL","blurb":"Every room in R-Link Studio has its own unique URL — your direct link for participants to join. Understanding how your Room URL works makes it easier to share, promote, and manage your sessions.","html":"<p>Every room in R-Link Studio has its own unique URL — your direct link for participants to join. Understanding how your Room URL works makes it easier to share, promote, and manage your sessions.</p>","text":"Every room in R-Link Studio has its own unique URL — your direct link for participants to join. Understanding how your Room URL works makes it easier to share, promote, and manage your sessions.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-8","title":"The Pre-Launch Check","blurb":"Before you enter the live studio, R-Link Studio takes you through the Pre-Launch Check — a quick configuration screen where you set up your camera, microphone, name, and how you're joining. Think of it as your pre-flight checklist before going live.","html":"<p>Before you enter the live studio, R-Link Studio takes you through the Pre-Launch Check — a quick configuration screen where you set up your camera, microphone, name, and how you're joining. Think of it as your pre-flight checklist before going live.</p>","text":"Before you enter the live studio, R-Link Studio takes you through the Pre-Launch Check — a quick configuration screen where you set up your camera, microphone, name, and how you're joining. Think of it as your pre-flight checklist before going live.","headings":[]}],"best-practices":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Meetings vs Webinars — Which One Do I Need?","blurb":"R-Link Studio gives you two powerful ways to connect with your audience — Meetings and Webinars. They look similar on the surface but are built for very different purposes. This article helps you choose the right one before you start.","html":"<p>R-Link Studio gives you two powerful ways to connect with your audience — Meetings and Webinars. They look similar on the surface but are built for very different purposes. This article helps you choose the right one before you start.</p>","text":"R-Link Studio gives you two powerful ways to connect with your audience — Meetings and Webinars. They look similar on the surface but are built for very different purposes. This article helps you choose the right one before you start.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Understanding Your Plan — Basic vs Business","blurb":"R-Link Studio has two plans — Basic and Business . Throughout this Help Center you'll see features tagged as Basic or Business Only. This article is your single reference for understanding exactly what each plan includes — so you always know what you have access to.","html":"<p>R-Link Studio has two plans — Basic and Business . Throughout this Help Center you'll see features tagged as Basic or Business Only. This article is your single reference for understanding exactly what each plan includes — so you always know what you have access to.</p>","text":"R-Link Studio has two plans — Basic and Business . Throughout this Help Center you'll see features tagged as Basic or Business Only. This article is your single reference for understanding exactly what each plan includes — so you always know what you have access to.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Starting Simultaneous Meetings — Scaling Your Reach Across Multiple Rooms","blurb":"Run two or more live meetings at the same time across separate rooms. A strategic playbook for Business plan teams scaling their reach.","html":"<p>Simultaneous meetings let you run two or more live sessions at the same time across separate rooms. This is a strategic capability available on the Business plan — and used well, it can multiply your reach without multiplying your stress.</p>","text":"Simultaneous meetings let you run two or more live sessions at the same time across separate rooms. This is a strategic capability available on the Business plan — and used well, it can multiply your reach without multiplying your stress.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Webinar Launch Strategy — Planning Your Event From Start to Finish","blurb":"A successful webinar isn't just pressing 'go live'. Planning, registration, and day-of execution all matter. A practical playbook for Business plan teams running webinars that fill seats and hold attention.","html":"<p>A successful webinar isn't just about pressing the \"go live\" button. Planning, registration strategy, and day-of execution all matter. This guide walks you through how to set up and run your webinar so attendees show up, stay engaged, and get value.</p>","text":"A successful webinar isn't just about pressing the \"go live\" button. Planning, registration strategy, and day-of execution all matter. This guide walks you through how to set up and run your webinar so attendees show up, stay engaged, and get value.","headings":[]}],"hosting":[{"id":"art-0","title":"The Studio Interface","blurb":"Once you click Start Meeting, you are live inside R-Link Studio. This article walks you through every part of the studio interface, so you know exactly what each area does before you go live.","html":"<div></div>\n      <div>\n        <a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span>\n        <a href=\"#\">Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</a><span>›</span>\n        <span>The Studio Interface</span>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</div>\n        <h1>The Studio Interface</h1>\n        <div>\n          <span>All Plans</span>\n          <span>Business — AI Notes, All Elements</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 5 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>✓ Beginner</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>Once you click <strong>Start Meeting</strong>, you're live inside R-Link Studio. This article walks you through every part of the studio interface — so you know exactly what each area does before your first session.</p>\n        <div>\n          <div>📌</div>\n          <div>\n            <div>Basic vs Business — What's Different in the Studio</div>\n            <div>\n              Both plans give you access to the full studio interface. However, some features within each area are plan-specific:<br><br>\n              <strong>Top Navigation Bar</strong> — <strong>AI Notes</strong> (Notetaker + Translation) is available on Business Plan only.<br><br>\n              <strong>Left Panel (Elements)</strong> — Basic includes the 5 Core Elements: Image / File, Video, Audio, Sound Effect, and Presentation. Business unlocks all Elements: Links, Banners, Polls, Website Overlays, Prompter, and more.<br><br>\n              <strong>Meeting Control Bar</strong> — Core controls are available on all plans. Some advanced options may be Business only.<br><br>\n              Not sure which plan you're on? See <a href=\"#best-practices/art-1\">Understanding Your Plan</a>.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>Overview</div>\n\n        <div><div>1</div><div>\n          <div>Studio Areas</div>\n          <div>The R-Link Studio interface is built around five main areas. Each is covered in detail in the steps below.</div>\n          \n          <p>↑ The R-Link Studio interface — Stage, Top Navigation Bar, Meeting Control Bar, Left Panel, Right Panel</p>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Stage</div><div>The large video area in the centre where participant videos and shared content appear.</div></div><div><div>Top Navigation Bar</div><div>Runs across the top — Rewards, Record, AI Notes, and your profile avatar.</div></div><div><div>Meeting Control Bar</div><div>Runs along the bottom — microphone, camera, screen share, and session controls.</div></div><div><div>Left Panel</div><div>Studio Controls — Views and Elements for managing stage layout and visual assets.</div></div><div><div>Right Panel</div><div>Chat, Attendees, Reactions, Branding, and Tools tabs.</div></div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n        \n        <div><div>2</div><div>\n          <div>The Meeting Control Bar</div>\n          <div>The <strong>Meeting Control Bar</strong> runs along the bottom of the studio throughout your session. Use the reference below to identify each control.</div>\n          \n          <p>↑ The Meeting Control Bar — Business Plan view. Basic Plan may show fewer options.</p>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-0-185.png\" alt=\"The Meeting Control Bar — all controls along the bottom of the studio\"></div>\n          <div>\n              <div>\n                <div>Meeting Control Bar — Overview</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>\n                <div><div>🎙️ 📹 🔊 Audio &amp; Video</div><div>Mute/unmute your mic, toggle your camera, and select your audio output device.</div></div>\n                <div><div>🖥️ Screen Share</div><div>Share your entire screen, a specific app window, or a browser tab with attendees.</div></div>\n                <div><div>😊 ♡ Reactions</div><div>Send emoji reactions and engagement signals during the session.</div></div>\n                <div><div>⊞ 👤 👥 Session</div><div>Switch layouts, invite participants, and manage Breakout Rooms.</div></div>\n                <div><div>CC 📄 ⚙️ Tools</div><div>Enable Closed Captions, access notes, and adjust session settings.</div></div>\n                <div><div>🚪 Leave / End</div><div>Leave the session or end it for all participants.</div></div>\n              </div>\n              <div>\n                <span>For a full icon-by-icon breakdown, see</span>\n                <a onclick=\"showArticle(1)\" href=\"#\">Using the Meeting Controls →</a>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>3</div><div>\n          <div>The Top Navigation Bar</div>\n          <div>The top bar runs across the top of the studio. Use the reference below to see what each control does.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-0-186.jpg\" alt=\"Top Navigation Bar\"></div>\n          <p>↑ The Top Navigation Bar — Rewards, Record, AI Notes, and your profile</p>\n          <div><div><div>Top Navigation Bar — Icon Reference</div></div><div><div><div>Rewards</div><div>Displays your current R-Link token balance in real time.</div></div><div><div>Record</div><div>Start or stop recording your session. A red indicator shows when recording is active.</div></div><div><div>AI Notes <span>Business Plan</span></div><div>Toggle the AI Notetaker on or off. Captures Smart Summary, Action Items, Decisions, and Insights.</div></div><div><div>Profile Avatar</div><div>Access your account settings from within the active session.</div></div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n        <div><div>4</div><div>\n          <div>The Left Panel — Studio Controls</div>\n          <div>Click <strong>Studio Controls</strong> on the left to expand the panel. Use the reference below to see what each section does.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-0-187.jpg\" alt=\"Left Panel — Studio Controls\"></div>\n          <p>↑ The Left Panel — Studio Controls showing Views and Elements</p>\n          <div><div><div>Left Panel — Studio Controls Reference</div></div><div><div><div>Collapse / Expand</div><div>Click the toggle to collapse the panel and give your stage more space.</div></div><div><div>Views</div><div>Switch between stage layouts — Grid View, Spotlight, Speaker View, and more.</div></div><div><div>Core Elements (Basic)</div><div>Access the 5 Core Elements — Image / File, Video, Audio, Sound Effect, and Presentation — from your library.</div></div><div><div>Elements <span>Business Plan</span></div><div>Unlocks all Elements — Links, Banners, Polls, Overlays, Prompter, and more.</div></div><div><div>Shared Libraries</div><div>Access element libraries shared with your account by other team members.</div></div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n        <div><div>5</div><div>\n          <div>The Right Panel</div>\n          <div>The Right Panel gives you access to communication, engagement, and session tools. Click any tab at the bottom to switch views.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-0-188.jpg\" alt=\"Right Panel\"></div>\n          <p>↑ The Right Panel — Chat open, with Attendees, Reactions, Branding and Tools tabs at the bottom</p>\n          <div><div><div>Right Panel — Tab Reference</div></div><div><div><div>Chat</div><div>Send and receive messages. Includes AI Assistant and group chat options.</div></div><div><div>Attendees</div><div>View and manage everyone — admit, mute, spotlight, or remove participants.</div></div><div><div>Reactions</div><div>See live emoji reactions from participants in real time.</div></div><div><div>Branding <span>Business Plan</span></div><div>Customise session appearance — Banner Styles, Colors, Background, Media, QR.</div></div><div><div>Tools</div><div>Enable Whiteboard, AI Translations (Business), AI Notetaker (Business), and Breakout Rooms.</div></div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n      <div></div>\n      <div>\n        <p>Was this article helpful?</p>\n        <div>\n          <button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button>\n          <button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n                <div>\n            <div>Previous Category</div>\n            <div>Getting Started</div>\n          </div>\n        </a>\n        <a onclick=\"showArticle(2)\" href=\"#\">\n          <div>›</div>\n          <div>\n            <div>Next Article</div>\n            <div>Break Out Rooms</div>\n          </div>\n        </a>\n      ","text":"Help Center › Hosting &amp; Studio Controls › The Studio Interface Hosting &amp; Studio Controls The Studio Interface All Plans Business — AI Notes, All Elements 5 min read Updated April 2026 ✓ Beginner Once you click Start Meeting , you're live inside R-Link Studio. This article walks you through every part of the studio interface — so you know exactly what each area does before your first session. 📌 Basic vs Business — What's Different in the Studio Both plans give you access to the full studio interface. However, some features within each area are plan-specific: Top Navigation Bar — AI Notes (Notetaker + Translation) is available on Business Plan only. Left Panel (Elements) — Basic includes the 5 Core Elements: Image / File, Video, Audio, Sound Effect, and Presentation. Business unlocks all Elements: Links, Banners, Polls, Website Overlays, Prompter, and more. Meeting Control Bar — Core controls are available on all plans. Some advanced options may be Business only. Not sure which plan you're on? See Understanding Your Plan . Overview 1 Studio Areas The R-Link Studio interface is built around five main areas. Each is covered in detail in the steps below. ↑ The R-Link Studio interface — Stage, Top Navigation Bar, Meeting Control Bar, Left Panel, Right Panel Details Stage The large video area in the centre where participant videos and shared content appear. Top Navigation Bar Runs across the top — Rewards, Record, AI Notes, and your profile avatar. Meeting Control Bar Runs along the bottom — microphone, camera, screen share, and session controls. Left Panel Studio Controls — Views and Elements for managing stage layout and visual assets. Right Panel Chat, Attendees, Reactions, Branding, and Tools tabs. 2 The Meeting Control Bar The Meeting Control Bar runs along the bottom of the studio throughout your session. Use the reference below to identify each control. ↑ The Meeting Control Bar — Business Plan view. Basic Plan may show fewer options. Meeting Control Bar — Overview 🎙️ 📹 🔊 Audio &amp; Video Mute/unmute your mic, toggle your camera, and select your audio output device. 🖥️ Screen Share Share your entire screen, a specific app window, or a browser tab with attendees. 😊 ♡ Reactions Send emoji reactions and engagement signals during the session. ⊞ 👤 👥 Session Switch layouts, invite participants, and manage Breakout Rooms. CC 📄 ⚙️ Tools Enable Closed Captions, access notes, and adjust session settings. 🚪 Leave / End Leave the session or end it for all participants. For a full icon-by-icon breakdown, see Using the Meeting Controls → 3 The Top Navigation Bar The top bar runs across the top of the studio. Use the reference below to see what each control does. ↑ The Top Navigation Bar — Rewards, Record, AI Notes, and your profile Top Navigation Bar — Icon Reference Rewards Displays your current R-Link token balance in real time. Record Start or stop recording your session. A red indicator shows when recording is active. AI Notes Business Plan Toggle the AI Notetaker on or off. Captures Smart Summary, Action Items, Decisions, and Insights. Profile Avatar Access your account settings from within the active session. 4 The Left Panel — Studio Controls Click Studio Controls on the left to expand the panel. Use the reference below to see what each section does. ↑ The Left Panel — Studio Controls showing Views and Elements Left Panel — Studio Controls Reference Collapse / Expand Click the toggle to collapse the panel and give your stage more space. Views Switch between stage layouts — Grid View, Spotlight, Speaker View, and more. Core Elements (Basic) Access the 5 Core Elements — Image / File, Video, Audio, Sound Effect, and Presentation — from your library. Elements Business Plan Unlocks all Elements — Links, Banners, Polls, Overlays, Prompter, and more. Shared Libraries Access element libraries shared with your account by other team members. 5 The Right Panel The Right Panel gives you access to communication, engagement, and session tools. Click any tab at the bottom to switch views. ↑ The Right Panel — Chat open, with Attendees, Reactions, Branding and Tools tabs at the bottom Right Panel — Tab Reference Chat Send and receive messages. Includes AI Assistant and group chat options. Attendees View and manage everyone — admit, mute, spotlight, or remove participants. Reactions See live emoji reactions from participants in real time. Branding Business Plan Customise session appearance — Banner Styles, Colors, Background, Media, QR. Tools Enable Whiteboard, AI Translations (Business), AI Notetaker (Business), and Breakout Rooms. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No Previous Category Getting Started › Next Article Break Out Rooms","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Using the Meeting Controls","blurb":"The Meeting Control Bar runs along the bottom of the studio throughout your session. This article walks through every control — what it does, when to use it, and where to go for more detail.","html":"\n      <div>\n        <a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span>\n        <a href=\"#\">Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</a><span>›</span>\n        <span>Using the Meeting Controls</span>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</div>\n        <h1>Using the Meeting Controls</h1>\n        <div>\n          <span>All Plans</span>\n          <span>Business — AI Notes</span>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 4 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>✓ Beginner</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>The <strong>Meeting Control Bar</strong> runs along the bottom of the studio throughout your session. This article walks through every control — what it does, when to use it, and where to go for more detail.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>Overview</div>\n\n        <!-- Toolbar screenshot  -->\n        <div>\n          <img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-1-189.jpg\" alt=\"Meeting Control Bar\">\n        </div>\n        <p>↑ The Meeting Control Bar — Business Plan view</p>\n        \n\n                <div>\n          <div>\n            <div></div>\n            <div>Control</div>\n            <div>Deep Dive</div>\n          </div>\n          <div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>🎙️</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Microphone</strong>\n                <div>Mute and unmute yourself. Click <strong>^</strong> to select your microphone device.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>🔊</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Speaker Output</strong>\n                <div>Click <strong>^</strong> to select your audio output device.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>📹</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Camera</strong>\n                <div>Turn your video on or off. Click <strong>^</strong> to select your camera device.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>🖥️</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Screen Share</strong>\n                <div>Share your screen, an app window, or a browser tab.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>\n                <a onclick=\"showArticle(5)\" href=\"#\">Learn More →</a>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>😊</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Reactions</strong>\n                <div>Send emoji reactions visible to all participants.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>👤</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Invite</strong>\n                <div>Copy your room link to share with participants.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>👥</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Participants</strong>\n                <div>Open the attendee list — admit, mute, spotlight, or remove.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>\n                <a onclick=\"showArticle(3)\" href=\"#\">Learn More →</a>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>🚪</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Breakout Rooms</strong>\n                <div>Split participants into smaller groups mid-session.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>\n                <a onclick=\"showArticle(2)\" href=\"#\">Learn More →</a>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>💬</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Chat</strong>\n                <div>Open the chat panel from the Right Panel — not the control bar.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>\n                <a onclick=\"showArticle(4)\" href=\"#\">Learn More →</a>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>CC</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Closed Captions</strong>\n                <div>Toggle live captions on or off for participants.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>⚙️</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Settings</strong>\n                <div>Access in-session settings and configuration options.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <div>🔴</div>\n              <div>\n                <strong>Leave / End Meeting</strong>\n                <div>Exit the session or end it for all participants. Red button — bottom right.</div>\n              </div>\n              <div>—</div>\n            </div>\n\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div>\n          <div>💡</div>\n          <div>\n            <div>Tip</div>\n            <div>The controls with an <strong>^</strong> arrow next to them have a device selector — click the caret to switch between your connected microphones, speakers, or cameras without leaving the session.</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <div></div>\n      <div>\n        <p>Was this article helpful?</p>\n        <div>\n          <button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button>\n          <button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n                <div><div>Previous</div><div>The Studio Interface</div></div>\n        </a>\n        <a onclick=\"showArticle(2)\" href=\"#\">\n          <div>›</div>\n          <div><div>Next Article</div><div>Break Out Rooms</div></div>\n        </a>\n      \n    ","text":"Help Center › Hosting &amp; Studio Controls › Using the Meeting Controls Hosting &amp; Studio Controls Using the Meeting Controls All Plans Business — AI Notes 4 min read Updated April 2026 ✓ Beginner The Meeting Control Bar runs along the bottom of the studio throughout your session. This article walks through every control — what it does, when to use it, and where to go for more detail. Overview ↑ The Meeting Control Bar — Business Plan view Control Deep Dive 🎙️ Microphone Mute and unmute yourself. Click ^ to select your microphone device. — 🔊 Speaker Output Click ^ to select your audio output device. — 📹 Camera Turn your video on or off. Click ^ to select your camera device. — 🖥️ Screen Share Share your screen, an app window, or a browser tab. Learn More → 😊 Reactions Send emoji reactions visible to all participants. — 👤 Invite Copy your room link to share with participants. — 👥 Participants Open the attendee list — admit, mute, spotlight, or remove. Learn More → 🚪 Breakout Rooms Split participants into smaller groups mid-session. Learn More → 💬 Chat Open the chat panel from the Right Panel — not the control bar. Learn More → CC Closed Captions Toggle live captions on or off for participants. — ⚙️ Settings Access in-session settings and configuration options. — 🔴 Leave / End Meeting Exit the session or end it for all participants. Red button — bottom right. — 💡 Tip The controls with an ^ arrow next to them have a device selector — click the caret to switch between your connected microphones, speakers, or cameras without leaving the session. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No Previous The Studio Interface › Next Article Break Out Rooms","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Break Out Rooms","blurb":"Break Out Rooms let you split participants into smaller, separate groups during a live session — perfect for workshops, group activities, or team discussions.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</a><span>›</span><span>Break Out Rooms</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</div>\n        <h1>Break Out Rooms</h1>\n        <div><span>All Plans</span><span>Business — Multiple Rooms</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 4 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>✓ Intermediate</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>Break Out Rooms let you split participants into smaller, separate groups during a live session — perfect for workshops, group activities, or team discussions.</p>\n        <div><div>📌</div><div><div>Basic vs Business</div><div><strong>Basic Plan</strong> includes 1 Breakout Room. <strong>Business Plan</strong> unlocks multiple rooms simultaneously.</div></div></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>Step-by-Step</div>\n\n        <div><div>1</div><div>\n          <div>Open Break Out Rooms</div>\n          <div>Open the <strong>Right Panel</strong>, click the <strong>Tools</strong> tab, toggle <strong>Breakout Rooms</strong> on, then click <strong>Manage Rooms</strong>.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-2-191.jpg\" alt=\"Opening Breakout Rooms\"></div>\n          <p>↑ Tools panel — toggle Breakout Rooms on, then click Manage Rooms</p>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Right Panel</div><div>Click the wrench icon at the bottom right of the studio to open the Tools tab.</div></div><div><div>Breakout Rooms toggle</div><div>Toggle on to activate. An <strong>+ Add Room</strong> button and <strong>Manage Rooms</strong> button will appear.</div></div><div><div>Manage Rooms</div><div>Opens the full Breakout Rooms modal with Setup, Manage, and Settings tabs.</div></div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n        <div><div>2</div><div>\n          <div>Set Up Your Rooms</div>\n          <div>In the <strong>Setup</strong> tab, create your rooms, name them, and assign participants before opening.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-2-192.jpg\" alt=\"Breakout Rooms Setup tab\"></div>\n          <p>↑ Setup tab — create and name rooms, assign participants, then click Open Rooms</p>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>+ Add Room</div><div>Creates a new breakout room. Click the room name to rename it.</div></div><div><div>Drag participants</div><div>Drag unassigned participants from the left column into any room.</div></div><div><div>Auto-assign</div><div>Distributes participants evenly across all rooms automatically.</div></div><div><div>Clear All</div><div>Removes all room assignments so you can start over.</div></div><div><div>Open Rooms</div><div>Launches all rooms. Participants receive a prompt to join their assigned room.</div></div></div></div>\n          <div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>Use <strong>Auto-assign</strong> when you have a large group and room assignments don't need to be specific.</div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n        <div><div>3</div><div>\n          <div>Manage Active Rooms</div>\n          <div>Once rooms are open, the modal switches to the <strong>Manage</strong> tab — monitor rooms, join them, broadcast messages, and respond to requests.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-2-193.jpg\" alt=\"Breakout Rooms Manage tab\"></div>\n          <p>↑ Manage tab — Active Rooms with timers, Broadcast Message, and Help Requests</p>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Active Rooms</div><div>Shows each room with a participant count, live timer countdown, and a <strong>Join Room</strong> button.</div></div><div><div>Timer</div><div>Set or adjust the remaining time per room using the dropdown (e.g. 15 min).</div></div><div><div>Broadcast Message</div><div>Type a message, select <strong>All Rooms</strong> or specific rooms, then click <strong>Send to All</strong>.</div></div><div><div>Help Requests</div><div>Participants unassigned to a room can request to be assigned from here. Click <strong>Join</strong> to bring them in.</div></div><div><div>End All Rooms</div><div>Red button — closes all rooms and returns everyone to the main session.</div></div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n        <div><div>4</div><div>\n          <div>Adjust Settings</div>\n          <div>Click the <strong>Settings</strong> tab to configure timing and end notifications for your breakout session.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-2-194.jpg\" alt=\"Breakout Rooms Settings tab\"></div>\n          <p>↑ Settings tab — Session Timer, Individual room timers, Auto-close, and End Notification</p>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Session Timer</div><div>Toggle on to set a time limit. Drag the slider to set the default duration (default: 15 minutes).</div></div><div><div>Individual room timers</div><div>Toggle on to set different time limits per room instead of a shared duration.</div></div><div><div>Auto-close when timer ends</div><div>Rooms close automatically and participants return to the main session when time is up.</div></div><div><div>End Notification</div><div>Notifies participants before the session ends. Set the lead time using the dropdown (e.g. 1 minute before).</div></div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n        <div><div>5</div><div>\n          <div>End All Rooms</div>\n          <div>Click the red <strong>End All Rooms</strong> button in the <strong>Manage</strong> or <strong>Settings</strong> tab to close all rooms and bring everyone back to the main session.</div>\n          <div><div>⚠️</div><div><div>Heads up</div><div><strong>End All Rooms</strong> immediately closes every room. Make sure groups have wrapped up before ending.</div></div></div>\n        </div></div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button></div></div>\n    ","text":"Help Center › Hosting &amp; Studio Controls › Break Out Rooms Hosting &amp; Studio Controls Break Out Rooms All Plans Business — Multiple Rooms 4 min read Updated April 2026 ✓ Intermediate Break Out Rooms let you split participants into smaller, separate groups during a live session — perfect for workshops, group activities, or team discussions. 📌 Basic vs Business Basic Plan includes 1 Breakout Room. Business Plan unlocks multiple rooms simultaneously. Step-by-Step 1 Open Break Out Rooms Open the Right Panel , click the Tools tab, toggle Breakout Rooms on, then click Manage Rooms . ↑ Tools panel — toggle Breakout Rooms on, then click Manage Rooms Details Right Panel Click the wrench icon at the bottom right of the studio to open the Tools tab. Breakout Rooms toggle Toggle on to activate. An + Add Room button and Manage Rooms button will appear. Manage Rooms Opens the full Breakout Rooms modal with Setup, Manage, and Settings tabs. 2 Set Up Your Rooms In the Setup tab, create your rooms, name them, and assign participants before opening. ↑ Setup tab — create and name rooms, assign participants, then click Open Rooms Details + Add Room Creates a new breakout room. Click the room name to rename it. Drag participants Drag unassigned participants from the left column into any room. Auto-assign Distributes participants evenly across all rooms automatically. Clear All Removes all room assignments so you can start over. Open Rooms Launches all rooms. Participants receive a prompt to join their assigned room. 💡 Tip Use Auto-assign when you have a large group and room assignments don't need to be specific. 3 Manage Active Rooms Once rooms are open, the modal switches to the Manage tab — monitor rooms, join them, broadcast messages, and respond to requests. ↑ Manage tab — Active Rooms with timers, Broadcast Message, and Help Requests Details Active Rooms Shows each room with a participant count, live timer countdown, and a Join Room button. Timer Set or adjust the remaining time per room using the dropdown (e.g. 15 min). Broadcast Message Type a message, select All Rooms or specific rooms, then click Send to All . Help Requests Participants unassigned to a room can request to be assigned from here. Click Join to bring them in. End All Rooms Red button — closes all rooms and returns everyone to the main session. 4 Adjust Settings Click the Settings tab to configure timing and end notifications for your breakout session. ↑ Settings tab — Session Timer, Individual room timers, Auto-close, and End Notification Details Session Timer Toggle on to set a time limit. Drag the slider to set the default duration (default: 15 minutes). Individual room timers Toggle on to set different time limits per room instead of a shared duration. Auto-close when timer ends Rooms close automatically and participants return to the main session when time is up. End Notification Notifies participants before the session ends. Set the lead time using the dropdown (e.g. 1 minute before). 5 End All Rooms Click the red End All Rooms button in the Manage or Settings tab to close all rooms and bring everyone back to the main session. ⚠️ Heads up End All Rooms immediately closes every room. Make sure groups have wrapped up before ending. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Managing Your Attendees","blurb":"Manage all participants in your session — admit from the Waiting Room, mute, spotlight, or remove.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</a><span>›</span><span>Managing Your Attendees</span></div>\n<div>\n        <div><span></span> Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</div>\n        <h1>Managing Your Attendees</h1>\n        <div><span>All Plans</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 3 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>✓ Beginner</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>Manage all participants in your session — admit from the Waiting Room, mute, spotlight, or remove.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>Step-by-Step</div>\n        \n        <div><div>1</div><div>\n          <div>Open the Attendees Panel</div>\n          <div>During a live session, click the <strong>Attendees</strong> tab in the Right Panel to view everyone in the room.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-3-195.png\" alt=\"Open the Attendees Panel — Attendees tab showing Hosts &amp; Co-Hosts and participant list\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Right Panel</div><div>Click the people icon in the right panel tab bar to open the Attendees view.</div></div><div><div>Participant list</div><div>Shows all connected participants including their name and connection status.</div></div><div><div>Waiting Room</div><div>If Waiting Room is enabled, pending participants appear here first for you to admit or deny.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>2</div><div>\n          <div>Admit or Deny from Waiting Room</div>\n          <div>If you have the <strong>Waiting Room</strong> enabled, participants will appear here before entering the session.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-3-196.png\" alt=\"Waiting Room — Admit All, Deny All, and per-participant admit/deny controls\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details — Waiting Room Controls</div></div><div><div>⚙️ <strong>Before your session:</strong> The Waiting Room must be turned on in your <strong>Room Settings</strong> before it will hold participants. You can configure this from your dashboard before going live.</div><div><div>Bulk Controls</div></div><div><div>Admit All</div><div>Green button — admits every participant currently waiting at once.</div></div><div><div>Deny All</div><div>Red button — removes every participant currently waiting without admitting them.</div></div><div><div>Per-Participant Controls</div></div><div><div>Chat icon (💬)</div><div>Opens a private chat with that individual while they wait. Both the host and the waiting participant can message each other — useful for a quick check-in before admitting.</div></div><div><div>✓ (green check)</div><div>Admits this individual participant into the main session.</div></div><div><div>✗ (red ×)</div><div>Denies this individual participant and removes them from the Waiting Room.</div></div><div><div>⚙ Gear Icon — Waiting Room Settings</div></div><div><div>Enable Waiting Room</div><div>Toggle on/off. When enabled, participants must wait for a host to admit them. Can also be configured in Room Settings before the session starts.</div></div><div><div>Auto-admit registered users</div><div>Toggle on/off. Registered attendees skip the Waiting Room and join automatically.</div></div><div><div>Custom Welcome Message <span>Business Plan</span></div><div>Text shown to participants while they wait (up to 200 characters). Use this to set expectations or greet attendees.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>3</div><div>\n          <div>Manage Individual Participants</div>\n          <div>Hover over any participant in the list to reveal management options.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-3-197.png\" alt=\"Participant options menu — Request to unmute, Make Presenter, Spotlight, Shadow ban, Make Co-Host, Remove from meeting\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details — ⋮ Menu options</div></div><div><div><div>Request to unmute</div><div>Sends the participant a prompt asking them to unmute their microphone.</div></div><div><div>Request to enable camera</div><div>Sends the participant a prompt asking them to turn on their camera.</div></div><div><div>Adjust volume</div><div>Drag the slider to raise or lower the volume of this participant for everyone (default 100%).</div></div><div><div>Make Presenter</div><div>Grants this participant presenter-level access to share their screen and use Elements.</div></div><div><div>Spotlight</div><div>Pins the participant to the main stage so everyone sees them prominently.</div></div><div><div>Shadow ban</div><div>Silently removes the participant's visibility from other attendees without notifying them.</div></div><div><div>Make Co-Host</div><div>Elevates this participant to Co-Host, giving them host-level controls for the session.</div></div><div><div>Assign Category</div><div>Tags the participant with a category label (e.g. VIP, Speaker) for organisational purposes.</div></div><div><div>Remove from meeting</div><div>Removes the participant from the session. They will need the room link to re-join.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button></div></div>\n          ","text":"Help Center › Hosting &amp; Studio Controls › Managing Your Attendees Hosting &amp; Studio Controls Managing Your Attendees All Plans 3 min read Updated April 2026 ✓ Beginner Manage all participants in your session — admit from the Waiting Room, mute, spotlight, or remove. Step-by-Step 1 Open the Attendees Panel During a live session, click the Attendees tab in the Right Panel to view everyone in the room. Details Right Panel Click the people icon in the right panel tab bar to open the Attendees view. Participant list Shows all connected participants including their name and connection status. Waiting Room If Waiting Room is enabled, pending participants appear here first for you to admit or deny. 2 Admit or Deny from Waiting Room If you have the Waiting Room enabled, participants will appear here before entering the session. Details — Waiting Room Controls ⚙️ Before your session: The Waiting Room must be turned on in your Room Settings before it will hold participants. You can configure this from your dashboard before going live. Bulk Controls Admit All Green button — admits every participant currently waiting at once. Deny All Red button — removes every participant currently waiting without admitting them. Per-Participant Controls Chat icon (💬) Opens a private chat with that individual while they wait. Both the host and the waiting participant can message each other — useful for a quick check-in before admitting. ✓ (green check) Admits this individual participant into the main session. ✗ (red ×) Denies this individual participant and removes them from the Waiting Room. ⚙ Gear Icon — Waiting Room Settings Enable Waiting Room Toggle on/off. When enabled, participants must wait for a host to admit them. Can also be configured in Room Settings before the session starts. Auto-admit registered users Toggle on/off. Registered attendees skip the Waiting Room and join automatically. Custom Welcome Message Business Plan Text shown to participants while they wait (up to 200 characters). Use this to set expectations or greet attendees. 3 Manage Individual Participants Hover over any participant in the list to reveal management options. Details — ⋮ Menu options Request to unmute Sends the participant a prompt asking them to unmute their microphone. Request to enable camera Sends the participant a prompt asking them to turn on their camera. Adjust volume Drag the slider to raise or lower the volume of this participant for everyone (default 100%). Make Presenter Grants this participant presenter-level access to share their screen and use Elements. Spotlight Pins the participant to the main stage so everyone sees them prominently. Shadow ban Silently removes the participant's visibility from other attendees without notifying them. Make Co-Host Elevates this participant to Co-Host, giving them host-level controls for the session. Assign Category Tags the participant with a category label (e.g. VIP, Speaker) for organisational purposes. Remove from meeting Removes the participant from the session. They will need the room link to re-join. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-4","title":"Managing Chats","blurb":"Use the Chat panel to communicate with participants, create group chats, and export the conversation.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</a><span>›</span><span>Managing Chats</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</div>\n        <h1>Managing Chats</h1>\n        <div><span>All Plans</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 3 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>✓ Beginner</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>Use the Chat panel to communicate with participants, create group chats, and export the conversation.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>Step-by-Step</div>\n        \n        <div><div>1</div><div>\n          <div>Open the Chat Panel</div>\n          <div>Click the <strong>Chat</strong> tab in the Right Panel to open the chat during a live session.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-4-198.png\" alt=\"Chat panel open — showing group messages and participant list\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Everyone</div><div>The default chat group — messages are visible to all participants.</div></div><div><div>New chat</div><div>Create a private group chat with specific participants.</div></div><div><div>AI Assistant</div><div>Ask questions or get help from the AI directly within the chat panel.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>2</div><div>\n          <div>Send a Message</div>\n          <div>Type your message in the <strong>Type a message...</strong> field at the bottom of the panel and press send.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-4-199.png\" alt=\"Chat input area — message box with emoji, attachment, and image options\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Emoji</div><div>Click the emoji icon to add reactions or emoji to your message.</div></div><div><div>Attachment</div><div>Click the paperclip icon to attach a file to the chat.</div></div><div><div>Image</div><div>Click the image icon to send an image directly in the chat.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>3</div><div>\n          <div>Export Chat</div>\n          <div>After the session, export the chat log for your records.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-4-200.png\" alt=\"Export chat option — Export button highlighted in the Chat panel toolbar\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Export</div><div>Click the Export button at the top of the chat panel to download the full chat log.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button></div></div>\n          ","text":"Help Center › Hosting &amp; Studio Controls › Managing Chats Hosting &amp; Studio Controls Managing Chats All Plans 3 min read Updated April 2026 ✓ Beginner Use the Chat panel to communicate with participants, create group chats, and export the conversation. Step-by-Step 1 Open the Chat Panel Click the Chat tab in the Right Panel to open the chat during a live session. Details Everyone The default chat group — messages are visible to all participants. New chat Create a private group chat with specific participants. AI Assistant Ask questions or get help from the AI directly within the chat panel. 2 Send a Message Type your message in the Type a message... field at the bottom of the panel and press send. Details Emoji Click the emoji icon to add reactions or emoji to your message. Attachment Click the paperclip icon to attach a file to the chat. Image Click the image icon to send an image directly in the chat. 3 Export Chat After the session, export the chat log for your records. Details Export Click the Export button at the top of the chat panel to download the full chat log. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-5","title":"Screen Sharing & Presentations","blurb":"Share your screen, broadcast system audio, and stop sharing when done.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</a><span>›</span><span>Screen Sharing &amp; Presentations</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</div>\n        <h1>Screen Sharing &amp; Presentations</h1>\n        <div><span>All Plans</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 3 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>✓ Beginner</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>Share your screen, broadcast system audio, and stop sharing when done.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>Step-by-Step</div>\n        \n        <div><div>1</div><div>\n          <div>Start Screen Sharing</div>\n          <div>Click the <strong>Screen Share</strong> icon in the Meeting Control Bar to begin sharing.</div>\n          <div><p>Option 1 — Meeting Control Bar</p><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-5-201.png\" alt=\"Start Screen Sharing — Share Options dropdown from the Meeting Control Bar\"><p>Option 2 — Top Navigation Bar</p><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-5-202.png\" alt=\"Start Screen Sharing — Share button in the Top Navigation Bar and browser share dialog\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Entire Screen</div><div>Shares your full desktop — everything visible on your monitor.</div></div><div><div>Application Window</div><div>Shares only a specific open application without showing the rest of your screen.</div></div><div><div>Browser Tab</div><div>Shares a single browser tab. Best for presenting websites or web-based content.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>2</div><div>\n          <div>Share System Audio</div>\n          \n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-5-203.png\" alt=\"Share System Audio — Also share tab audio toggle highlighted in browser share dialog\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>+ Add Element</div><div>Click in the Left Panel to upload a new presentation file.</div></div><div><div>Supported formats</div><div>PDF, PPT, PPTX. Files are converted to slides automatically.</div></div><div><div>Add to Stage</div><div>Click on any element to push it live onto the stage for all participants to see.</div></div><div><div>Remove from Stage</div><div>Click the element again or use the stage controls to remove it.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>3</div><div>\n          <div>Stop Sharing</div>\n          <div>Click the <strong>Stop Presenting</strong> button at the bottom of the video screen to end your screen share. The floating <strong>Stop Sharing</strong> bar — visible only to the <strong>Host</strong> and <strong>Co-Host</strong> — will also stop the current screen share.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-5-204.png\" alt=\"Stop Sharing — Stop Presenting button and Stop sharing bar shown during an active screen share\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Screen Share icon</div><div>When active, the icon appears highlighted. Click it to stop the share immediately.</div></div><div><div>Elements</div><div>To remove a shared element from the stage, click it in the Elements panel to deactivate it.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button></div></div>\n          \n\n    ","text":"Help Center › Hosting &amp; Studio Controls › Screen Sharing &amp; Presentations Hosting &amp; Studio Controls Screen Sharing &amp; Presentations All Plans 3 min read Updated April 2026 ✓ Beginner Share your screen, broadcast system audio, and stop sharing when done. Step-by-Step 1 Start Screen Sharing Click the Screen Share icon in the Meeting Control Bar to begin sharing. Option 1 — Meeting Control Bar Option 2 — Top Navigation Bar Details Entire Screen Shares your full desktop — everything visible on your monitor. Application Window Shares only a specific open application without showing the rest of your screen. Browser Tab Shares a single browser tab. Best for presenting websites or web-based content. 2 Share System Audio Details + Add Element Click in the Left Panel to upload a new presentation file. Supported formats PDF, PPT, PPTX. Files are converted to slides automatically. Add to Stage Click on any element to push it live onto the stage for all participants to see. Remove from Stage Click the element again or use the stage controls to remove it. 3 Stop Sharing Click the Stop Presenting button at the bottom of the video screen to end your screen share. The floating Stop Sharing bar — visible only to the Host and Co-Host — will also stop the current screen share. Details Screen Share icon When active, the icon appears highlighted. Click it to stop the share immediately. Elements To remove a shared element from the stage, click it in the Elements panel to deactivate it. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-6","title":"Recording Your Meeting","blurb":"Record your session and access the recording in your Admin Portal after the call.","html":"\n          <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</a><span>›</span><span>Recording Your Meeting</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Hosting &amp; Studio Controls</div>\n        <h1>Recording Your Meeting</h1>\n        <div><span>All Plans</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 4 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>✓ Beginner</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>Record your session and access the recording in your Admin Portal after the call.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>Step-by-Step</div>\n        \n        <div><div>1</div><div>\n          <div>Start Recording</div>\n          <div>Click the <strong>Record</strong> button in the <strong>Top Navigation Bar</strong> to start recording your session.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-6-205.png\" alt=\"Record button in the Top Navigation Bar — highlighted with green arrow\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Record button</div><div>Located in the Top Navigation Bar. A red indicator will appear when recording is active.</div></div><div><div>Who is recorded</div><div>The full studio session is recorded — stage video, audio, and shared elements.</div></div><div><div>Notification</div><div>Participants are notified when a recording starts.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        \n        <div><div>2</div><div>\n          <div>Recording Started</div>\n          <div>Once recording begins, a <strong>red recording indicator</strong> and live timer appear in the Top Navigation Bar confirming the session is being captured.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-6-206.png\" alt=\"Recording Started — red recording indicator and live timer shown in the Top Navigation Bar\"></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>3</div><div>\n          <div>Pause or Stop Recording</div>\n          <div>Click the <strong>Record</strong> button in the Top Navigation Bar to <strong>Pause</strong> or <strong>Stop</strong> the recording. Pausing lets you resume later; stopping saves the recording automatically.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-6-207.png\" alt=\"Pause or Stop Recording — Stop and Pause buttons highlighted in the Top Navigation Bar\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Stop</div><div>Click the active Record button to stop. Processing begins immediately.</div></div><div><div>Processing time</div><div>Recordings may take a few minutes to process after the session ends.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n        <div><div>4</div><div>\n          <div>Access Your Recordings</div>\n          <div>Find all your recordings in the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> under the Recordings section.</div>\n          <div><img src=\"assets/img/hosting-studio-controls-art-6-208.png\" alt=\"Access Your Recordings — Recordings section in the Admin Panel showing recorded sessions\"></div>\n          <div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Admin Portal</div><div>Log in at <a href=\"https://studio.r-link.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">studio.r-link.com</a> and navigate to the Recordings section.</div></div><div><div>Download</div><div>Click the download icon next to any recording to save it locally.</div></div><div><div>Share</div><div>Copy the recording link to share with participants who missed the session.</div></div><div><div>Delete</div><div>Remove recordings you no longer need from your library.</div></div></div></div>\n          \n        </div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button></div></div>\n          \n\n    \n  \n    \n  ","text":"Help Center › Hosting &amp; Studio Controls › Recording Your Meeting Hosting &amp; Studio Controls Recording Your Meeting All Plans 4 min read Updated April 2026 ✓ Beginner Record your session and access the recording in your Admin Portal after the call. Step-by-Step 1 Start Recording Click the Record button in the Top Navigation Bar to start recording your session. Details Record button Located in the Top Navigation Bar. A red indicator will appear when recording is active. Who is recorded The full studio session is recorded — stage video, audio, and shared elements. Notification Participants are notified when a recording starts. 2 Recording Started Once recording begins, a red recording indicator and live timer appear in the Top Navigation Bar confirming the session is being captured. 3 Pause or Stop Recording Click the Record button in the Top Navigation Bar to Pause or Stop the recording. Pausing lets you resume later; stopping saves the recording automatically. Details Stop Click the active Record button to stop. Processing begins immediately. Processing time Recordings may take a few minutes to process after the session ends. 4 Access Your Recordings Find all your recordings in the Admin Portal under the Recordings section. Details Admin Portal Log in at studio.r-link.com and navigate to the Recordings section. Download Click the download icon next to any recording to save it locally. Share Copy the recording link to share with participants who missed the session. Delete Remove recordings you no longer need from your library. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-7","title":"The Waiting Room","blurb":"Hold people outside your session until you let them in — turning the Waiting Room on, admitting or denying arrivals, and what participants see while they wait.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Waiting Room and Lobby</div><div class=\"callout-text\">These are the same feature. The studio top bar uses the shorter label <strong>Lobby</strong> — it shows <strong>Lobby On</strong> while the Waiting Room is enabled. Everywhere else, including Room Settings, it is called the <strong>Waiting Room</strong>.</div></div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-wr-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Turn the Waiting Room On</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">The Waiting Room holds people outside your session until a host lets them in. Turn it on ahead of time in <strong>Room Settings</strong> from your dashboard, or mid-session from the <strong>gear icon</strong> in the Attendees panel. While it is on, the studio top bar shows <strong>Lobby On</strong>.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Where to turn it on</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Room Settings</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Set it as a default for the room so every session starts with the Waiting Room on.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Attendees panel → gear</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Toggle <strong>Enable Waiting Room</strong> on or off while you are live.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Top bar → Lobby</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Shows <strong>Lobby On</strong> when enabled. Click it to see who is waiting.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Screenshot pending</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Send a screenshot of Room Settings with the Waiting Room toggle and we will add it here.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-wr-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">See Who Is Waiting</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Attendees</strong> tab in the Right Panel, or click <strong>Lobby</strong> in the top bar. Anyone who has arrived but not been let in is listed separately from your connected participants, so you can see at a glance who is waiting.</div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Screenshot pending</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Send a screenshot of the Attendees panel with people in the Waiting Room and we will add it here.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-wr-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Admit or Deny</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Admit people one at a time, or clear the whole queue at once. You can also message someone privately before letting them in — handy for confirming who they are.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Bulk controls</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Admit All</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Green button — admits everyone currently waiting.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Deny All</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Red button — removes everyone currently waiting without admitting them.</div></div></div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Per-participant controls</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Chat icon</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Opens a private chat with that person while they wait. Both of you can message — useful for a quick check-in before admitting.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">✓ Green check</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Admits that person into the session.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">✗ Red ×</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Denies that person and removes them from the Waiting Room.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"callout tip\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">💡</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Late arrivals</div><div class=\"callout-text\">The Waiting Room keeps working after your session starts. People who join late wait there until you admit them, so you are never interrupted mid-sentence.</div></div></div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Screenshot pending</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Send a screenshot of the Waiting Room list with Admit All and Deny All and we will add it here.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-wr-3\"><div class=\"step-num\">4</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Waiting Room Settings</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click the <strong>gear icon</strong> in the Attendees panel to change how the Waiting Room behaves during your session.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Settings</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Enable Waiting Room</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Toggle on or off. When on, participants must be admitted by a host.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Auto-admit registered users</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Registered attendees skip the Waiting Room and join automatically — useful for webinars where everyone signed up in advance.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Custom Welcome Message <span style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:20px;background:rgba(245,158,11,0.1);color:#b45309;border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.3);\">Business Plan</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Text shown to people while they wait, up to 200 characters. Use it to set expectations or greet attendees.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Screenshot pending</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Send a screenshot of the Waiting Room settings panel and we will add it here.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-wr-4\"><div class=\"step-num\">5</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">What Participants See</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Someone arriving at a session with the Waiting Room on lands on a holding screen instead of the stage. They can see your custom welcome message if you have set one, and they can reply if you message them. They join the stage the moment you admit them.</div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">🔒</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Who can admit</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Only the host and co-hosts can admit or deny people. Guests and attendees never see the Waiting Room queue.</div></div></div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Screenshot pending</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Send a screenshot of the participant-side waiting screen and we will add it here.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>\n    ","text":"Step-by-step 📌 Waiting Room and Lobby These are the same feature. The studio top bar uses the shorter label Lobby — it shows Lobby On while the Waiting Room is enabled. Everywhere else, including Room Settings, it is called the Waiting Room . 1 Turn the Waiting Room On The Waiting Room holds people outside your session until a host lets them in. Turn it on ahead of time in Room Settings from your dashboard, or mid-session from the gear icon in the Attendees panel. While it is on, the studio top bar shows Lobby On . Where to turn it on Room Settings Set it as a default for the room so every session starts with the Waiting Room on. Attendees panel → gear Toggle Enable Waiting Room on or off while you are live. Top bar → Lobby Shows Lobby On when enabled. Click it to see who is waiting. 📌 Screenshot pending Send a screenshot of Room Settings with the Waiting Room toggle and we will add it here. 2 See Who Is Waiting Open the Attendees tab in the Right Panel, or click Lobby in the top bar. Anyone who has arrived but not been let in is listed separately from your connected participants, so you can see at a glance who is waiting. 📌 Screenshot pending Send a screenshot of the Attendees panel with people in the Waiting Room and we will add it here. 3 Admit or Deny Admit people one at a time, or clear the whole queue at once. You can also message someone privately before letting them in — handy for confirming who they are. Bulk controls Admit All Green button — admits everyone currently waiting. Deny All Red button — removes everyone currently waiting without admitting them. Per-participant controls Chat icon Opens a private chat with that person while they wait. Both of you can message — useful for a quick check-in before admitting. ✓ Green check Admits that person into the session. ✗ Red × Denies that person and removes them from the Waiting Room. 💡 Late arrivals The Waiting Room keeps working after your session starts. People who join late wait there until you admit them, so you are never interrupted mid-sentence. 📌 Screenshot pending Send a screenshot of the Waiting Room list with Admit All and Deny All and we will add it here. 4 Waiting Room Settings Click the gear icon in the Attendees panel to change how the Waiting Room behaves during your session. Settings Enable Waiting Room Toggle on or off. When on, participants must be admitted by a host. Auto-admit registered users Registered attendees skip the Waiting Room and join automatically — useful for webinars where everyone signed up in advance. Custom Welcome Message Business Plan Text shown to people while they wait, up to 200 characters. Use it to set expectations or greet attendees. 📌 Screenshot pending Send a screenshot of the Waiting Room settings panel and we will add it here. 5 What Participants See Someone arriving at a session with the Waiting Room on lands on a holding screen instead of the stage. They can see your custom welcome message if you have set one, and they can reply if you message them. They join the stage the moment you admit them. 🔒 Who can admit Only the host and co-hosts can admit or deny people. Guests and attendees never see the Waiting Room queue. 📌 Screenshot pending Send a screenshot of the participant-side waiting screen and we will add it here.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-8","title":"Rally Rewards","blurb":"Earn digital rewards for hosting, inviting, and attending sessions.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Coming soon</div>\n        <div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:4px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">🚧</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">This article is coming soon</div><div class=\"callout-text\">We are writing up Rally Rewards in full. In the meantime, the Rally Rewards panel is documented as part of the meeting controls.</div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-7-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">What Rally Rewards Will Cover</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Rally Rewards are digital rewards you earn for hosting, inviting, and attending sessions. This article will walk through earning, tracking, and withdrawing them.</div>\n            <div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Planned sections</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">My Rewards</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Your balance, its USD equivalent, and progress toward the withdrawal threshold.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Badges</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Badges earned for hosting, inviting, and attending sessions.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Calculator</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Estimate what you would earn from a given number of events or invites.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Withdrawals</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">How the $100 minimum works and how to withdraw.</div></div></div></div>\n            <div style=\"background:rgba(99,102,241,0.05);border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 16px;margin-top:16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">For the in-session panel, see</span><a href=\"#hosting/art-1\" style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#7c3aed;text-decoration:none;\">Using the Meeting Controls →</a></div>\n          </div></div>\n      </div>\n    ","text":"Coming soon 🚧 This article is coming soon We are writing up Rally Rewards in full. In the meantime, the Rally Rewards panel is documented as part of the meeting controls. 1 What Rally Rewards Will Cover Rally Rewards are digital rewards you earn for hosting, inviting, and attending sessions. This article will walk through earning, tracking, and withdrawing them. Planned sections My Rewards Your balance, its USD equivalent, and progress toward the withdrawal threshold. Badges Badges earned for hosting, inviting, and attending sessions. Calculator Estimate what you would earn from a given number of events or invites. Withdrawals How the $100 minimum works and how to withdraw. For the in-session panel, see Using the Meeting Controls →","headings":[],"soon":true}],"meetings":[{"id":"art-a","title":"Scheduling a Meeting","blurb":"Create a meeting from the Sessions page — title, room, time, invitees, recording, and registration.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Where Scheduling Lives</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\"><strong>Sessions</strong> is the master control for scheduled meetings, webinars, and live events. Open it from the left sidebar — the page opens on <strong>Upcoming Sessions</strong>, with counts for total, this week, live now, and drafts.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Meetings vs Webinars</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Meetings suit smaller collaborative sessions where everyone can interact. For broadcast-style events with registration, schedule a <strong>Webinar</strong> instead.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Open the Schedule Menu</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Schedule</strong> at the top right of the Upcoming Sessions panel and pick <strong>Meeting</strong> from the dropdown. The same menu also creates Webinars and Live Streams.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-sessions-schedule.png\" alt=\"The Sessions page with the Schedule dropdown open showing Meeting, Webinar and Live Stream\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Sessions → Schedule → Meeting. Calendar and List toggle how the sessions below are displayed.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Fill In the Meeting Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The Schedule Meeting dialog opens with <strong>Session Type</strong> already set to Meeting.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-schedule-dialog.png\" alt=\"The Schedule Meeting dialog with title, description, room, date, duration, timezone and invitees\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:620px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Schedule Meeting dialog. Required fields are marked with an asterisk.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">MEETING FIELDS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Session Type</td><td>Meeting, Webinar, or Live Stream. Leave it on <strong>Meeting</strong>.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Title <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>What attendees see. Up to 100 characters.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Description</td><td>Optional context, up to 500 characters.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Room</td><td>Which of your rooms the meeting runs in.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Start Date &amp; Time <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>Pick a date and time, or use a quick chip: <strong>Next hour</strong>, <strong>Tonight 7pm</strong>, <strong>Tomorrow 9am</strong>, <strong>Tomorrow 2pm</strong>.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Duration <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>How long the meeting is scheduled to run.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Timezone</td><td>The timezone the start time is set in. Check this before inviting people in other regions.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Invitees</td><td>Add an email and an optional name, then <strong>+</strong> to add them to the list. Repeat for each person.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Set Recording and Registration</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Two toggles sit at the bottom of the dialog, both off by default.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">OPTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Enable recording</td><td>Records the session. Leave off if you do not need a recording.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Require registration</td><td>Attendees must register before they can join, which gives you a registrant list.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Recording Still Starts Manually</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Enabling recording here prepares the session for it. You still press <strong>Record</strong> in the Meeting Control Bar once you are in the room.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Create the Meeting</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Create Meeting</strong>. The meeting appears in your Upcoming Sessions list with its date, time, and room, ready to start when the time comes.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Check the Timezone Chip</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>The quick chips use your own timezone. If most of your invitees are elsewhere, set the timezone first and the chips will still land where you expect.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s6\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">6</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find It Again in Sessions</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once created, the meeting appears in the <strong>Sessions</strong> list with its type, date, time, and room. This is where you go back to change anything.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-sessions-list.png\" alt=\"The Sessions list showing a scheduled Weekly Team Sync meeting with Join and Manage buttons\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ A scheduled meeting in the Sessions list. <strong>Manage</strong> opens its details for editing; <strong>Join</strong> starts it.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">FINDING A SESSION</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Search</td><td>Search sessions by name.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>All Types</td><td>Filter to meetings, webinars, or live streams.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Upcoming</td><td>Switch between upcoming and past sessions.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>List / Grid</td><td>Toggle how sessions are laid out.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Calendar</td><td>See everything on a calendar instead of a list.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Editing a Meeting</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Click <strong>Manage</strong> on the session to change the title, room, time, invitees, or toggles. See <strong>Editing a Scheduled Meeting</strong> for the full walkthrough.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Where Scheduling Lives Sessions is the master control for scheduled meetings, webinars, and live events. Open it from the left sidebar — the page opens on Upcoming Sessions , with counts for total, this week, live now, and drafts. Meetings vs Webinars Meetings suit smaller collaborative sessions where everyone can interact. For broadcast-style events with registration, schedule a Webinar instead. 2 Open the Schedule Menu Click Schedule at the top right of the Upcoming Sessions panel and pick Meeting from the dropdown. The same menu also creates Webinars and Live Streams. ↑ Sessions → Schedule → Meeting. Calendar and List toggle how the sessions below are displayed. 3 Fill In the Meeting Details The Schedule Meeting dialog opens with Session Type already set to Meeting. ↑ The Schedule Meeting dialog. Required fields are marked with an asterisk. MEETING FIELDS Session Type Meeting, Webinar, or Live Stream. Leave it on Meeting . Title Required What attendees see. Up to 100 characters. Description Optional context, up to 500 characters. Room Which of your rooms the meeting runs in. Start Date &amp; Time Required Pick a date and time, or use a quick chip: Next hour , Tonight 7pm , Tomorrow 9am , Tomorrow 2pm . Duration Required How long the meeting is scheduled to run. Timezone The timezone the start time is set in. Check this before inviting people in other regions. Invitees Add an email and an optional name, then + to add them to the list. Repeat for each person. 4 Set Recording and Registration Two toggles sit at the bottom of the dialog, both off by default. OPTIONS Enable recording Records the session. Leave off if you do not need a recording. Require registration Attendees must register before they can join, which gives you a registrant list. Recording Still Starts Manually Enabling recording here prepares the session for it. You still press Record in the Meeting Control Bar once you are in the room. 5 Create the Meeting Click Create Meeting . The meeting appears in your Upcoming Sessions list with its date, time, and room, ready to start when the time comes. Pro Tip — Check the Timezone Chip The quick chips use your own timezone. If most of your invitees are elsewhere, set the timezone first and the chips will still land where you expect. 6 Find It Again in Sessions Once created, the meeting appears in the Sessions list with its type, date, time, and room. This is where you go back to change anything. ↑ A scheduled meeting in the Sessions list. Manage opens its details for editing; Join starts it. FINDING A SESSION Search Search sessions by name. All Types Filter to meetings, webinars, or live streams. Upcoming Switch between upcoming and past sessions. List / Grid Toggle how sessions are laid out. Calendar See everything on a calendar instead of a list. Editing a Meeting Click Manage on the session to change the title, room, time, invitees, or toggles. See Editing a Scheduled Meeting for the full walkthrough. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-b","title":"Editing a Scheduled Meeting","blurb":"Open a scheduled meeting from Sessions → Manage to change its title, time, room, recording, and invitees.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Open the Session</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Find the meeting in <strong>Sessions</strong> and click <strong>Manage</strong>. Everything about the meeting can be changed from there, right up until it starts.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-sessions-list.png\" alt=\"The Sessions list with a scheduled meeting and its Join and Manage buttons\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Sessions → Manage on the meeting you want to change.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">The Manage Panel</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The panel opens with the meeting name, its type and timing at the top, and <strong>Join</strong> and <strong>Copy Link</strong> right below. The settings are grouped into collapsible sections.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-manage-dialog.png\" alt=\"The Manage panel for a meeting showing Details and Schedule expanded and four collapsed sections\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:620px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Manage panel. Details and Schedule are open by default.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SECTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Details</td><td>Title and description.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Schedule</td><td>Start date and time, duration, and timezone. End time is calculated for you.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Room &amp; access</td><td>Which room the meeting runs in and who can get in.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Recording &amp; engagement</td><td>Recording and the engagement options for the session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Hosts &amp; invitees</td><td>Who is hosting and who has been invited.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Advanced &amp; danger zone</td><td>Less common settings, plus cancelling or deleting the meeting.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Change the Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Under <strong>Details</strong>, edit the <strong>Title</strong> and <strong>Description</strong>. The title is what invitees see in their invitation and in the session list.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Reschedule It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Under <strong>Schedule</strong>, set a new <strong>Start</strong> date and time and adjust <strong>Duration (minutes)</strong>. The <strong>End</strong> fields update automatically from start plus duration.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Check the Timezone</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>The timezone field controls how the time is interpreted. Change the timezone and the same clock time means a different moment — confirm both together before saving.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Manage Room, Recording, and Invitees</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Expand <strong>Room &amp; access</strong> to move the meeting to a different room or change who can join. <strong>Recording &amp; engagement</strong> holds the recording setting. <strong>Hosts &amp; invitees</strong> is where you add or remove people.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Copy Link Before You Move Rooms</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>If you have already shared the meeting link, check it still points where you expect after changing rooms. <strong>Copy Link</strong> at the top of the panel always gives you the current one.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s6\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">6</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Save Your Changes</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Save changes</strong> at the bottom of the panel. The status line to the left reads <strong>All changes saved</strong> once it is done. <strong>Close</strong> dismisses the panel.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Cancelling a Meeting</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>To cancel or delete a meeting, open <strong>Advanced &amp; danger zone</strong> at the bottom of the panel. Deletion cannot be undone, and invitees are not notified automatically.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Open the Session Find the meeting in Sessions and click Manage . Everything about the meeting can be changed from there, right up until it starts. ↑ Sessions → Manage on the meeting you want to change. 2 The Manage Panel The panel opens with the meeting name, its type and timing at the top, and Join and Copy Link right below. The settings are grouped into collapsible sections. ↑ The Manage panel. Details and Schedule are open by default. SECTIONS Details Title and description. Schedule Start date and time, duration, and timezone. End time is calculated for you. Room &amp; access Which room the meeting runs in and who can get in. Recording &amp; engagement Recording and the engagement options for the session. Hosts &amp; invitees Who is hosting and who has been invited. Advanced &amp; danger zone Less common settings, plus cancelling or deleting the meeting. 3 Change the Details Under Details , edit the Title and Description . The title is what invitees see in their invitation and in the session list. 4 Reschedule It Under Schedule , set a new Start date and time and adjust Duration (minutes) . The End fields update automatically from start plus duration. Check the Timezone The timezone field controls how the time is interpreted. Change the timezone and the same clock time means a different moment — confirm both together before saving. 5 Manage Room, Recording, and Invitees Expand Room &amp; access to move the meeting to a different room or change who can join. Recording &amp; engagement holds the recording setting. Hosts &amp; invitees is where you add or remove people. Pro Tip — Copy Link Before You Move Rooms If you have already shared the meeting link, check it still points where you expect after changing rooms. Copy Link at the top of the panel always gives you the current one. 6 Save Your Changes Click Save changes at the bottom of the panel. The status line to the left reads All changes saved once it is done. Close dismisses the panel. Cancelling a Meeting To cancel or delete a meeting, open Advanced &amp; danger zone at the bottom of the panel. Deletion cannot be undone, and invitees are not notified automatically. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-c","title":"Starting Your Meeting","blurb":"Start from the Dashboard, the Go Live launcher, or a room card — all three lead to the Pre-Launch Check.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Three Ways to Start</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Every route leads to the same place — the <strong>Pre-Launch Check</strong>, where you set your name, pick your devices, and choose how you are joining. Use whichever is closest to hand.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHERE TO START FROM</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Dashboard</td><td><strong>Start a meeting</strong> on the Dashboard hero — the fastest route.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Go Live launcher</td><td>The <strong>Go Live</strong> button in the top bar, or the <strong>G</strong> shortcut.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Rooms</td><td><strong>Launch</strong> on a specific room card when the meeting belongs to that room.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Sessions</td><td><strong>Start</strong> on a scheduled meeting in the Sessions list.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">From the Dashboard</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">On the Dashboard, the hero panel carries <strong>Start a meeting</strong> and <strong>Schedule</strong>. Click <strong>Start a meeting</strong> to go straight into a session now.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-start-dashboard.png\" alt=\"The Studio Dashboard with Start a meeting and Schedule buttons in the hero panel\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Dashboard → Start a meeting. The Live Now panel on the right starts pulsing once you are on air.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">From the Go Live Launcher</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Go Live</strong> in the top bar (or press <strong>G</strong>) to open the session launcher. It asks what you are doing and offers three paths.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-launch-session.png\" alt=\"The Launch a Session modal with Start a meeting, Host a webinar and Go live options\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The launcher. Each option has a keyboard shortcut: M, W, and L.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">LAUNCHER OPTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Start a meeting <span style=\"opacity:.6\">M</span></td><td>Face-to-face, right now.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Host a webinar <span style=\"opacity:.6\">W</span></td><td>Opens the studio for a presentation to a large audience.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Go live <span style=\"opacity:.6\">L</span></td><td>Stream out to your connected destinations.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Enter someone else's room</td><td>Type a host's room name or paste a room link. Tick <strong>Join as a guest</strong> for the attendee view with no host controls.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">From the Rooms Tab</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">If the meeting belongs to a particular room, open <strong>Rooms</strong> in the sidebar and click <strong>Launch</strong> on that room's card. Each card shows the room slug, its brand and preset, session and attendee counts, and whether the room is active.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-rooms-launch.png\" alt=\"The Rooms page with four meeting room cards, each with a Launch button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Rooms → Launch. The capacity bar at the top shows how many rooms your plan allows.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">An Inactive Room Will Not Launch</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Each card has a <strong>Room active</strong> toggle. If it is off, the room is unavailable to everyone — switch it on before launching.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Complete Your Pre-Launch Check</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The Pre-Launch page is where you configure everything before entering. Set your <strong>name</strong>, confirm the <strong>meeting name</strong>, choose your <strong>camera</strong>, <strong>microphone</strong>, and <strong>headphones</strong>, and select whether you are joining as <strong>Moderator</strong> or <strong>Participant</strong>. Click <strong>Start Meeting</strong> when ready.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/scheduling-meetings-art-c-041.png\" alt=\"The Pre-Launch Check page with camera preview, device selectors and the Start Meeting button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Pre-Launch Check. Virtual Background can be set here, before anyone sees you.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Join as Moderator</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Moderator gives you host controls: admitting people, managing the stage, and recording. Participant gives you the attendee view — useful for testing what your audience sees.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s6\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">6</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Admit Your Participants</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">With the <strong>Waiting Room</strong> enabled, participants are held in a queue as they arrive. A notification appears in the room — click <strong>Admit</strong> next to each person, or <strong>Admit All</strong> to let everyone in at once.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Waiting Room Is Optional</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>With the Waiting Room turned off, participants enter the room automatically when they click the link. Toggle it from the Edit Meeting page.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s7\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">7</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Confirm Recording and Go</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Check that your <strong>recording</strong> is running if you need it — look for the recording indicator in the Meeting Control Bar at the top of the screen. Once confirmed, you are live.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Recording Must Be Started Manually</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Recording does not start on its own. Click <strong>Record</strong> in the Meeting Control Bar to begin. See the Recordings section for the full walkthrough.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/scheduling-meetings-art-c-042.png\" alt=\"A meeting room with participants and the Record button in the top control bar\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Meeting Control Bar, with the Record button at the top of the room.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Three Ways to Start Every route leads to the same place — the Pre-Launch Check , where you set your name, pick your devices, and choose how you are joining. Use whichever is closest to hand. WHERE TO START FROM Dashboard Start a meeting on the Dashboard hero — the fastest route. Go Live launcher The Go Live button in the top bar, or the G shortcut. Rooms Launch on a specific room card when the meeting belongs to that room. Sessions Start on a scheduled meeting in the Sessions list. 2 From the Dashboard On the Dashboard, the hero panel carries Start a meeting and Schedule . Click Start a meeting to go straight into a session now. ↑ Dashboard → Start a meeting. The Live Now panel on the right starts pulsing once you are on air. 3 From the Go Live Launcher Click Go Live in the top bar (or press G ) to open the session launcher. It asks what you are doing and offers three paths. ↑ The launcher. Each option has a keyboard shortcut: M, W, and L. LAUNCHER OPTIONS Start a meeting M Face-to-face, right now. Host a webinar W Opens the studio for a presentation to a large audience. Go live L Stream out to your connected destinations. Enter someone else's room Type a host's room name or paste a room link. Tick Join as a guest for the attendee view with no host controls. 4 From the Rooms Tab If the meeting belongs to a particular room, open Rooms in the sidebar and click Launch on that room's card. Each card shows the room slug, its brand and preset, session and attendee counts, and whether the room is active. ↑ Rooms → Launch. The capacity bar at the top shows how many rooms your plan allows. An Inactive Room Will Not Launch Each card has a Room active toggle. If it is off, the room is unavailable to everyone — switch it on before launching. 5 Complete Your Pre-Launch Check The Pre-Launch page is where you configure everything before entering. Set your name , confirm the meeting name , choose your camera , microphone , and headphones , and select whether you are joining as Moderator or Participant . Click Start Meeting when ready. ↑ Pre-Launch Check. Virtual Background can be set here, before anyone sees you. Pro Tip — Join as Moderator Moderator gives you host controls: admitting people, managing the stage, and recording. Participant gives you the attendee view — useful for testing what your audience sees. 6 Admit Your Participants With the Waiting Room enabled, participants are held in a queue as they arrive. A notification appears in the room — click Admit next to each person, or Admit All to let everyone in at once. Waiting Room Is Optional With the Waiting Room turned off, participants enter the room automatically when they click the link. Toggle it from the Edit Meeting page. 7 Confirm Recording and Go Check that your recording is running if you need it — look for the recording indicator in the Meeting Control Bar at the top of the screen. Once confirmed, you are live. Recording Must Be Started Manually Recording does not start on its own. Click Record in the Meeting Control Bar to begin. See the Recordings section for the full walkthrough. ↑ The Meeting Control Bar, with the Record button at the top of the room. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-d","title":"Managing Scheduled Meetings","blurb":"View, filter, and act on every scheduled session from the Sessions page.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">The Sessions Page</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\"><strong>Sessions</strong> is where every scheduled meeting, webinar, and live event lives. The page opens on <strong>Upcoming Sessions</strong>, with counters for total sessions, this week, live now, and drafts.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-sessions-list.png\" alt=\"The Sessions page with counters, filters and a scheduled meeting row\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Sessions → Upcoming. Each row shows the session type, date, time, and room.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Switch Views</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The controls at the top right change how your sessions are displayed.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-sessions-calendar.png\" alt=\"The Sessions page in Calendar view showing a September month grid with scheduled sessions\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Calendar view. Today is circled; <strong>Today</strong> and the arrows move between months.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">VIEWS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>List</td><td>A vertical list of sessions with their actions on the right.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Calendar</td><td>A month grid with every session on its day, coloured by type. Use <strong>Today</strong> and the arrows to move between months.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Card / List toggle</td><td>The two small icons beside the filters. List stacks sessions in full-width rows; cards put them two to a row.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-sessions-cards.png\" alt=\"The Sessions page in card view showing sessions as a two-column grid of cards\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Card view. Sessions sit two to a row, each with its type and status tags and its own actions.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find a Session</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Above the list, three controls narrow things down.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">FILTERS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Search sessions</td><td>Match by session name.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>All Types</td><td>Limit to meetings, webinars, or live streams.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Upcoming</td><td>Switch between upcoming and past sessions.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Meeting History and Recordings</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>The buttons at the top of the page — <strong>Meeting History</strong> and <strong>Recordings</strong> — jump straight to what has already happened, rather than filtering the upcoming list.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Act on a Session</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Each row carries its own actions on the right.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">ROW ACTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Join</td><td>Start or enter the session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Copy</td><td>Copy the session link to share.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Registrants</td><td>For webinars, open the registrant list.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Manage</td><td>Open the session panel to edit any of its details.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Editing Lives in Manage</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p><strong>Manage</strong> opens the full settings panel — title, schedule, room, recording, invitees, and the danger zone. See <strong>Editing a Scheduled Meeting</strong> for the walkthrough.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 The Sessions Page Sessions is where every scheduled meeting, webinar, and live event lives. The page opens on Upcoming Sessions , with counters for total sessions, this week, live now, and drafts. ↑ Sessions → Upcoming. Each row shows the session type, date, time, and room. 2 Switch Views The controls at the top right change how your sessions are displayed. ↑ Calendar view. Today is circled; Today and the arrows move between months. VIEWS List A vertical list of sessions with their actions on the right. Calendar A month grid with every session on its day, coloured by type. Use Today and the arrows to move between months. Card / List toggle The two small icons beside the filters. List stacks sessions in full-width rows; cards put them two to a row. ↑ Card view. Sessions sit two to a row, each with its type and status tags and its own actions. 3 Find a Session Above the list, three controls narrow things down. FILTERS Search sessions Match by session name. All Types Limit to meetings, webinars, or live streams. Upcoming Switch between upcoming and past sessions. Meeting History and Recordings The buttons at the top of the page — Meeting History and Recordings — jump straight to what has already happened, rather than filtering the upcoming list. 4 Act on a Session Each row carries its own actions on the right. ROW ACTIONS Join Start or enter the session. Copy Copy the session link to share. Registrants For webinars, open the registrant list. Manage Open the session panel to edit any of its details. Editing Lives in Manage Manage opens the full settings panel — title, schedule, room, recording, invitees, and the danger zone. See Editing a Scheduled Meeting for the walkthrough. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-e","title":"Ending Your Meeting","blurb":"Four ways to wrap up — end for all, end for all except host, or leave with or without assigning a new host.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Open the Exit Menu</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">In the <strong>Meeting Control Bar</strong> at the bottom of the screen, click the red <strong>Exit</strong> button on the far right. A menu appears with four ways to end or leave the session.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">YOUR FOUR OPTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>End Meeting for All</td><td>Ends the meeting and removes all participants.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>End Meeting for All, Except Host</td><td>Removes all participants but you stay in the meeting.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Leave &amp; Assign Host</td><td>Choose someone to continue hosting, then leave.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Leave Without Assigning Host</td><td>You leave and the room stays open with no host.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/mtg-end-menu.png\" alt=\"The End Meeting menu open above the red exit button in the meeting control bar\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The red exit button in the Meeting Control Bar opens the End Meeting menu.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">End Meeting for All</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Closes the session immediately. Everyone is removed from the room and redirected to your <strong>Exit URL</strong> if one is configured in your account settings.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Exit URL Is a Business Plan Feature</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Setting a custom Exit URL — the page participants land on after the meeting ends — is available on the <strong>Business Plan</strong>. On other plans, participants see a default end screen.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">End Meeting for All, Except Host</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Removes all participants while keeping the room active for co-hosts and presenters. Useful when you want to debrief privately after an audience leaves.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">With Co-hosts or Presenters in the Room</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Participants are removed immediately and the room stays active. No confirmation dialog appears.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">With No Co-host or Presenter Assigned</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Since nobody would be left in the room, a confirmation dialog asks whether you want to end the entire meeting or just remove all participants.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Leave and Assign Host</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Choose this when you need to step out but the meeting should carry on. An <strong>Assign New Host</strong> panel lists everyone currently in the room — pick someone to hand hosting to, then leave.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Hand Off Before You Go</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>If you leave without assigning a host, nobody has host controls. Assign first, confirm they have it, then exit.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Leave Without Assigning Host</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">You leave and the room stays open. Nobody is handed host controls, so the meeting carries on without a host.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Nobody Can End the Meeting</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>With no host in the room, no one has the controls to end it or manage participants. Use <strong>Leave &amp; Assign Host</strong> unless you are stepping out briefly and coming back.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Open the Exit Menu In the Meeting Control Bar at the bottom of the screen, click the red Exit button on the far right. A menu appears with four ways to end or leave the session. YOUR FOUR OPTIONS End Meeting for All Ends the meeting and removes all participants. End Meeting for All, Except Host Removes all participants but you stay in the meeting. Leave &amp; Assign Host Choose someone to continue hosting, then leave. Leave Without Assigning Host You leave and the room stays open with no host. ↑ The red exit button in the Meeting Control Bar opens the End Meeting menu. 2 End Meeting for All Closes the session immediately. Everyone is removed from the room and redirected to your Exit URL if one is configured in your account settings. Exit URL Is a Business Plan Feature Setting a custom Exit URL — the page participants land on after the meeting ends — is available on the Business Plan . On other plans, participants see a default end screen. 3 End Meeting for All, Except Host Removes all participants while keeping the room active for co-hosts and presenters. Useful when you want to debrief privately after an audience leaves. With Co-hosts or Presenters in the Room Participants are removed immediately and the room stays active. No confirmation dialog appears. With No Co-host or Presenter Assigned Since nobody would be left in the room, a confirmation dialog asks whether you want to end the entire meeting or just remove all participants. 4 Leave and Assign Host Choose this when you need to step out but the meeting should carry on. An Assign New Host panel lists everyone currently in the room — pick someone to hand hosting to, then leave. Pro Tip — Hand Off Before You Go If you leave without assigning a host, nobody has host controls. Assign first, confirm they have it, then exit. 5 Leave Without Assigning Host You leave and the room stays open. Nobody is handed host controls, so the meeting carries on without a host. Nobody Can End the Meeting With no host in the room, no one has the controls to end it or manage participants. Use Leave &amp; Assign Host unless you are stepping out briefly and coming back. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]}],"webinars":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Scheduling Your Webinar","blurb":"The four-step Create Webinar wizard — details, landing page, emails, and review.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Open the Create Webinar Wizard</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Go to <strong>Sessions</strong>, click <strong>Schedule</strong> at the top right, and choose <strong>Webinar</strong>. The wizard runs in four steps — only the first is required, and the rest can be skipped and filled in later.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/web-schedule-menu.png\" alt=\"The Sessions page with the Schedule dropdown open and Webinar highlighted\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Sessions → Schedule → Webinar.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">THE FOUR STEPS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>1. Webinar Details <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>Title, timing, host, and the core session settings.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>2. Event Landing Page</td><td>Your public registration page. Optional.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>3. Email Settings</td><td>Confirmation and reminder emails. Optional.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>4. Review &amp; Publish</td><td>Check everything, then publish.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 1 — Webinar Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The only required step. Fill in the title, date, time, and duration, and you have a webinar.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/web-step1-details.png\" alt=\"Step 1 of the Create Webinar wizard with title, date, time, host and toggles\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:620px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Step 1 of 4. Create &amp; finish publishes now; Customize (optional) continues to step 2.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WEBINAR DETAILS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Title (Public) <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>What registrants and attendees see.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Internal Name</td><td>For your dashboard reference only — never shown publicly.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Description</td><td>Optional summary of what you will cover.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Date / Time <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>When the webinar starts.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Duration <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>How long it is scheduled to run.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Timezone</td><td>The timezone your start time is set in.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Host Name / Host Email</td><td>Who is running it, and where registrant replies go.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Auto-Record</td><td>Start recording automatically when the webinar begins.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Waiting Room</td><td>Hold attendees on a countdown screen until you start.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stage Control</td><td>Expand to set how presenters and panelists appear on stage.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Three Ways to Leave This Step</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p><strong>Save Draft</strong> keeps it unpublished, <strong>Create &amp; finish</strong> publishes with defaults for everything else, and <strong>Customize (optional)</strong> takes you through steps 2 to 4.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 2 — Event Landing Page</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Your public registration page. Skip it and R-Link uses the Standard template with your default brand kit.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/web-step2-landing.png\" alt=\"Step 2 showing six registration page templates, brand kit selector and hero image\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:620px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Step 2 of 4. Six templates, your brand kit, and a hero image.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">REGISTRATION PAGE TEMPLATES</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Standard (Default)</td><td>The classic R-Link registration page — countdown timer, clean form.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Classic SaaS</td><td>Two-column hero with the form to the side.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Centered Big Promise</td><td>Centered single-message hero.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Background Card</td><td>Full background with a centered card.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Agenda First</td><td>Agenda and speakers shown first.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Evergreen On-Demand</td><td>Watch now / replay funnel.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">PAGE SETTINGS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Brand Kit</td><td>Colors, fonts, and logo for the page. Leave on <strong>Account Default</strong> to use your global kit.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Hero Image</td><td>The image at the top of the landing page. Recommended size 1366×1100.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Register button label</td><td>Override the default button text.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 3 — Email Settings</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">What R-Link sends registrants, and who it comes from.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/web-step3-email.png\" alt=\"Step 3 showing sender settings and toggles for confirmation, reminder and replay emails\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:620px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Step 3 of 4. Each email can be switched on or off independently.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SENDER SETTINGS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>From Name</td><td>The name shown in the From field.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Reply-To Email</td><td>Where replies from registrants are sent.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">THE EMAILS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Confirmation Email</td><td>Sent immediately after someone registers.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Additional Message</td><td>Optional text placed above the important details in the confirmation.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>24-Hour Reminder</td><td>Sent 24 hours before the webinar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>1-Hour Reminder</td><td>Sent 1 hour before the webinar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Reminder Additional Message</td><td>Optional text added to whichever reminders are enabled.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Replay Email</td><td>Sent after the webinar with the replay link, if replay is enabled.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Use the Additional Messages</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>A line like \"have your questions ready, we will run a live Q&amp;A at the end\" sets expectations before anyone joins, and it costs you nothing to add.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 4 — Review and Publish</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">A full summary of every setting across the three sections, each with an <strong>Edit</strong> link back to that step.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/web-step4-review.png\" alt=\"Step 4 showing the review summary for webinar details, landing page and email settings\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:620px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Step 4 of 4. Check the summary, then Publish Webinar.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Read the Summary Before Publishing</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>This is the one place you see everything at once — event time, capacity, registration, waitlist, passcode, and which emails are on. Catching a wrong timezone or an off reminder here is much easier than after invitations go out.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Publish Webinar</strong> to make it live, or <strong>Save Draft</strong> to come back to it.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 4 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Open the Create Webinar Wizard Go to Sessions , click Schedule at the top right, and choose Webinar . The wizard runs in four steps — only the first is required, and the rest can be skipped and filled in later. ↑ Sessions → Schedule → Webinar. THE FOUR STEPS 1. Webinar Details Required Title, timing, host, and the core session settings. 2. Event Landing Page Your public registration page. Optional. 3. Email Settings Confirmation and reminder emails. Optional. 4. Review &amp; Publish Check everything, then publish. 2 Step 1 — Webinar Details The only required step. Fill in the title, date, time, and duration, and you have a webinar. ↑ Step 1 of 4. Create &amp; finish publishes now; Customize (optional) continues to step 2. WEBINAR DETAILS Title (Public) Required What registrants and attendees see. Internal Name For your dashboard reference only — never shown publicly. Description Optional summary of what you will cover. Date / Time Required When the webinar starts. Duration Required How long it is scheduled to run. Timezone The timezone your start time is set in. Host Name / Host Email Who is running it, and where registrant replies go. Auto-Record Start recording automatically when the webinar begins. Waiting Room Hold attendees on a countdown screen until you start. Stage Control Expand to set how presenters and panelists appear on stage. Three Ways to Leave This Step Save Draft keeps it unpublished, Create &amp; finish publishes with defaults for everything else, and Customize (optional) takes you through steps 2 to 4. 3 Step 2 — Event Landing Page Your public registration page. Skip it and R-Link uses the Standard template with your default brand kit. ↑ Step 2 of 4. Six templates, your brand kit, and a hero image. REGISTRATION PAGE TEMPLATES Standard (Default) The classic R-Link registration page — countdown timer, clean form. Classic SaaS Two-column hero with the form to the side. Centered Big Promise Centered single-message hero. Background Card Full background with a centered card. Agenda First Agenda and speakers shown first. Evergreen On-Demand Watch now / replay funnel. PAGE SETTINGS Brand Kit Colors, fonts, and logo for the page. Leave on Account Default to use your global kit. Hero Image The image at the top of the landing page. Recommended size 1366×1100. Register button label Override the default button text. 4 Step 3 — Email Settings What R-Link sends registrants, and who it comes from. ↑ Step 3 of 4. Each email can be switched on or off independently. SENDER SETTINGS From Name The name shown in the From field. Reply-To Email Where replies from registrants are sent. THE EMAILS Confirmation Email Sent immediately after someone registers. Additional Message Optional text placed above the important details in the confirmation. 24-Hour Reminder Sent 24 hours before the webinar. 1-Hour Reminder Sent 1 hour before the webinar. Reminder Additional Message Optional text added to whichever reminders are enabled. Replay Email Sent after the webinar with the replay link, if replay is enabled. Pro Tip — Use the Additional Messages A line like \"have your questions ready, we will run a live Q&amp;A at the end\" sets expectations before anyone joins, and it costs you nothing to add. 5 Step 4 — Review and Publish A full summary of every setting across the three sections, each with an Edit link back to that step. ↑ Step 4 of 4. Check the summary, then Publish Webinar. Read the Summary Before Publishing This is the one place you see everything at once — event time, capacity, registration, waitlist, passcode, and which emails are on. Catching a wrong timezone or an off reminder here is much easier than after invitations go out. Click Publish Webinar to make it live, or Save Draft to come back to it. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Event Landing Page","blurb":"Your Event Landing Page is what registrants see when they receive your webinar link.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</a><span>›</span><span>Event Landing Page</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</div>\n        <h1>Event Landing Page</h1>\n        <div><span>Business Only</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 4 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>★ Business</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>Your Event Landing Page is what registrants see when they receive your webinar link. This article covers how to set it up — including the hero image, registration settings, and form fields — and how to get your webinar URL after publishing. The flow differs depending on whether registration is required or not.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>Step-by-Step</div>\n\n      <div><div>1</div><div><div>Set Up Your Event Landing Page</div><div>In <strong>Step 2</strong> of the Create Webinar wizard, choose your landing page source and optionally upload a hero image.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ Step 2 of 4 — Event Landing Page source options and hero image upload.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Built-in Landing Page</div><div>R-Link generates your registration page automatically using your webinar title, date, time, and description. This is the default and works immediately with no setup.</div></div><div><div>Event Landing Page (Custom)</div><div>Custom Event Landing Page templates are currently in development. Stay tuned — this option will allow you to link a fully branded custom layout once available.</div></div><div><div>Hero Image</div><div>Upload a banner image that appears at the top of your landing page. Available whether registration is required or not. Recommended size: 1366×1100px.</div></div><div><div>Preview</div><div>The live preview on the right updates as you configure settings — check it before proceeding.</div></div></div></div><div><div>📌</div><div><div>Hero image tip</div><div>You can add a hero image regardless of whether registration is required. It will show at the top of your landing page in both cases.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- PATH DIVIDER -->\n      <div><div>PATH A — Registration Required</div></div>\n\n      <div>\n\n      <div><div>2A</div><div><div>Enable Registration &amp; Configure Form Fields</div><div>Scroll down in <strong>Event Landing Page</strong> to turn on registration and set up your form. When registration is required, the form will be visible on the landing page.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ Enable Registration Required, configure form fields, set replay access, passcode, and approval mode.</p><div><div><div>Registration Form Fields</div></div><div><div><div>Registration Required</div><div>Toggle <strong>on</strong>. The registration form becomes visible on your landing page — attendees must complete it before joining.</div></div><div><div>First Name / Last Name / Email</div><div>Always enabled and required. These are the minimum fields on every form.</div></div><div><div>+ Company, Job Title, Phone, LinkedIn, Questions</div><div>Optional fields you can add to the form. Each can be set as optional or required.</div></div><div><div>Custom Field</div><div>Type any label and click <strong>Add</strong> to collect event-specific information.</div></div><div><div>Require registration to watch replay</div><div>Viewers must complete the form before accessing the recorded replay.</div></div><div><div>Add 4-digit passcode</div><div>Adds a passcode gate to your landing page for private or invite-only events.</div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>3A</div><div><div>Set Approval Mode</div><div>Choose how registrations are processed — automatically or with manual review.</div><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Auto-Approve Registrations</div><div>Registrant submits the form → confirmation email is sent immediately with their join link. Best for open or public webinars.</div></div><div><div>Manual Approval</div><div>Each registration is held as <strong>Pending</strong> until you approve it from the Manage Registrants panel. Best for invite-only or paid events.</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>Use <strong>Manual Approval</strong> combined with a 4-digit passcode for maximum control over who attends a private webinar.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- PATH DIVIDER -->\n      <div><div>PATH B — No Registration Required</div></div>\n\n      <div>\n\n      <div><div>2B</div><div><div>Open Access — No Registration Form</div><div>If you don't need to collect registrant information, toggle registration off. The landing page will show your webinar details only — no form.</div><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Registration Required toggle</div><div>Toggle <strong>off</strong>. The registration form is hidden from your landing page.</div></div><div><div>What attendees see</div><div>Your landing page shows the webinar title, date, time, description, and hero image — but no registration form.</div></div><div><div>Access</div><div>Anyone with the webinar link can join directly without submitting any information.</div></div><div><div>When to use</div><div>Best for internal team sessions, exclusive invite groups, or events where you're sharing the link directly and don't need to track attendance.</div></div></div></div><div><div>📌</div><div><div>No registration — no email reminders</div><div>If registration is off, R-Link has no email addresses to send reminders or confirmation emails to. Make sure attendees save the join link themselves.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- FINAL STEP -->\n      <div>\n        <div>FINAL STEP — Both Paths</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n\n      <div><div>✓</div><div><div>Publish Your Webinar &amp; Share Your URL</div><div>Once you complete all wizard steps and click <strong>Publish Webinar</strong>, your event URL is generated and ready to share.</div><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>After publishing</div><div>A pop-up modal appears with your unique webinar event URL — copy it immediately to share with your audience.</div></div><div><div>Webinars tab</div><div>You can also find your event URL anytime from the <strong>Webinars</strong> section in your Admin Portal — locate your webinar and click <strong>Event Landing Page</strong> to open or copy the link.</div></div><div><div>Share the URL</div><div>Send your event URL via email, social media, or any channel where your audience will register or join.</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>After publishing, test your landing page by opening the URL in a private/incognito browser window to see exactly what your registrants will see.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      </div>\n\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — thanks!'\">👎 No</button></div></div>\n            \n    ","text":"Help Center › Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars › Event Landing Page Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars Event Landing Page Business Only 4 min read Updated April 2026 ★ Business Your Event Landing Page is what registrants see when they receive your webinar link. This article covers how to set it up — including the hero image, registration settings, and form fields — and how to get your webinar URL after publishing. The flow differs depending on whether registration is required or not. Step-by-Step 1 Set Up Your Event Landing Page In Step 2 of the Create Webinar wizard, choose your landing page source and optionally upload a hero image. Screenshot ↑ Step 2 of 4 — Event Landing Page source options and hero image upload. Details Built-in Landing Page R-Link generates your registration page automatically using your webinar title, date, time, and description. This is the default and works immediately with no setup. Event Landing Page (Custom) Custom Event Landing Page templates are currently in development. Stay tuned — this option will allow you to link a fully branded custom layout once available. Hero Image Upload a banner image that appears at the top of your landing page. Available whether registration is required or not. Recommended size: 1366×1100px. Preview The live preview on the right updates as you configure settings — check it before proceeding. 📌 Hero image tip You can add a hero image regardless of whether registration is required. It will show at the top of your landing page in both cases. PATH A — Registration Required 2A Enable Registration &amp; Configure Form Fields Scroll down in Event Landing Page to turn on registration and set up your form. When registration is required, the form will be visible on the landing page. Screenshot ↑ Enable Registration Required, configure form fields, set replay access, passcode, and approval mode. Registration Form Fields Registration Required Toggle on . The registration form becomes visible on your landing page — attendees must complete it before joining. First Name / Last Name / Email Always enabled and required. These are the minimum fields on every form. + Company, Job Title, Phone, LinkedIn, Questions Optional fields you can add to the form. Each can be set as optional or required. Custom Field Type any label and click Add to collect event-specific information. Require registration to watch replay Viewers must complete the form before accessing the recorded replay. Add 4-digit passcode Adds a passcode gate to your landing page for private or invite-only events. 3A Set Approval Mode Choose how registrations are processed — automatically or with manual review. Details Auto-Approve Registrations Registrant submits the form → confirmation email is sent immediately with their join link. Best for open or public webinars. Manual Approval Each registration is held as Pending until you approve it from the Manage Registrants panel. Best for invite-only or paid events. 💡 Tip Use Manual Approval combined with a 4-digit passcode for maximum control over who attends a private webinar. PATH B — No Registration Required 2B Open Access — No Registration Form If you don't need to collect registrant information, toggle registration off. The landing page will show your webinar details only — no form. Details Registration Required toggle Toggle off . The registration form is hidden from your landing page. What attendees see Your landing page shows the webinar title, date, time, description, and hero image — but no registration form. Access Anyone with the webinar link can join directly without submitting any information. When to use Best for internal team sessions, exclusive invite groups, or events where you're sharing the link directly and don't need to track attendance. 📌 No registration — no email reminders If registration is off, R-Link has no email addresses to send reminders or confirmation emails to. Make sure attendees save the join link themselves. FINAL STEP — Both Paths ✓ Publish Your Webinar &amp; Share Your URL Once you complete all wizard steps and click Publish Webinar , your event URL is generated and ready to share. Details After publishing A pop-up modal appears with your unique webinar event URL — copy it immediately to share with your audience. Webinars tab You can also find your event URL anytime from the Webinars section in your Admin Portal — locate your webinar and click Event Landing Page to open or copy the link. Share the URL Send your event URL via email, social media, or any channel where your audience will register or join. 💡 Tip After publishing, test your landing page by opening the URL in a private/incognito browser window to see exactly what your registrants will see. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Email Confirmation & Reminders","blurb":"R-Link Studio can automatically send emails to your registrants — but only when two conditions are met in your webinar settings: Confirmation Email is toggled on (in Email.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</a><span>›</span><span>Email Confirmation &amp; Reminders</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</div>\n        <h1>Email Confirmation &amp; Reminders</h1>\n        <div><span>Business Only</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 3 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>★ Business</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>R-Link Studio can automatically send emails to your registrants — but only when two conditions are met in your webinar settings: <strong>Confirmation Email is toggled on</strong> (in Email Settings) and <strong>Registration Required is enabled</strong> (in Registration Settings). This article covers how each email works, how approval mode affects when confirmation is sent, and how to configure reminders.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>Step-by-Step</div>\n\n      <div><div>1</div><div><div>Confirmation Email Settings</div><div>Configure your confirmation email in <strong>Step 3 — Email Settings</strong> of the Create Webinar wizard.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ Confirmation Email toggle and Additional Message field in Email Settings.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Confirmation Email toggle</div><div>When enabled, registrants receive a confirmation email immediately after sign-up (Auto-Approve) or after you manually approve them (Manual Approval).</div></div><div><div>Email Preview</div><div>Shows what registrants will receive — webinar title, date, time, join link, and a calendar (.ics) file attachment.</div></div><div><div>Additional Message (optional)</div><div>Add a custom message that appears above the standard confirmation content. Use this for instructions, what to expect, or anything you want registrants to see right away.</div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>2</div><div><div>Auto-Approve — Confirmation Sent Immediately</div><div>If your registration is set to <strong>Auto-Approve Registrations</strong>, the confirmation email is sent to the registrant as soon as they submit the form.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ Approval Mode set to Auto-Approve — registrants receive confirmation immediately.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Auto-Approve Registrations</div><div>Default mode. Registrant submits the form → confirmation email is sent immediately with their join link.</div></div><div><div>Where to set it</div><div>Registration Settings in Step 2 (Event Landing Page) of the Create Webinar wizard — <strong>Approval Mode</strong> dropdown.</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>Use Auto-Approve for open or public webinars where you want to maximise registrations without any manual steps.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>3</div><div><div>Manual Approval — You Control When Confirmation is Sent</div><div>If your registration is set to <strong>Manual Approval</strong>, registrants are held as <strong>Pending</strong> until you approve them. The confirmation email is only sent after you approve.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ Pending registrant awaiting manual approval — confirmation email is not sent until you click Approve.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Pending status</div><div>Registrant has submitted the form but has not yet received confirmation or their join link.</div></div><div><div>Approve</div><div>Click to approve the registration — confirmation email is sent immediately to the registrant.</div></div><div><div>Reject</div><div>Click to reject — registrant is removed and does not receive a join link.</div></div><div><div>Where to set it</div><div>Registration Settings in Step 2 of the Create Webinar wizard — <strong>Approval Mode → Manual Approval</strong>.</div></div></div></div><div><div>📌</div><div><div>Heads up</div><div>Registrants in Pending status cannot join the webinar. Make sure to review and approve them before the session starts.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>4</div><div><div>What the Confirmation Email Looks Like</div><div>Once approved (automatically or manually), registrants receive a confirmation email with everything they need to join.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ Confirmation email showing webinar name, date, time, access link, and calendar reminder prompt.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Webinar name</div><div>Shown prominently at the top of the email.</div></div><div><div>Date & Time</div><div>Displayed in the timezone set during scheduling.</div></div><div><div>Access link</div><div>A unique join link for the registrant — clicking this takes them directly into the webinar.</div></div><div><div>Calendar reminder</div><div>Registrants are prompted to add the event to their calendar. A .ics file is attached.</div></div><div><div>From Name</div><div>Set in Email Settings — defaults to your account name.</div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>5</div><div><div>Reminder Emails</div><div>Toggle on automated reminder emails in <strong>Step 3 — Email Settings</strong> to notify registrants before the webinar starts.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ 24-Hour Reminder and 1-Hour Reminder toggles — both on by default. Add an optional additional message.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>24-Hour Reminder</div><div>Sent automatically 24 hours before the webinar starts. Includes the webinar title, date, time, and join link.</div></div><div><div>1-Hour Reminder</div><div>Sent automatically 1 hour before the webinar starts. Same content as the 24-hour reminder.</div></div><div><div>Toggle on/off</div><div>Each reminder can be independently toggled on or off. Toggle off if you don't want that reminder sent.</div></div><div><div>Additional Message (optional)</div><div>Add a custom note that appears in both reminder emails — e.g. 'Don't forget to test your audio before joining!'</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>Both reminders are on by default. We recommend keeping them both enabled — reminders significantly reduce no-shows.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — we\\'ll improve it'\">👎 No</button></div></div>\n            \n    ","text":"Help Center › Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars › Email Confirmation &amp; Reminders Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars Email Confirmation &amp; Reminders Business Only 3 min read Updated April 2026 ★ Business R-Link Studio can automatically send emails to your registrants — but only when two conditions are met in your webinar settings: Confirmation Email is toggled on (in Email Settings) and Registration Required is enabled (in Registration Settings). This article covers how each email works, how approval mode affects when confirmation is sent, and how to configure reminders. Step-by-Step 1 Confirmation Email Settings Configure your confirmation email in Step 3 — Email Settings of the Create Webinar wizard. Screenshot ↑ Confirmation Email toggle and Additional Message field in Email Settings. Details Confirmation Email toggle When enabled, registrants receive a confirmation email immediately after sign-up (Auto-Approve) or after you manually approve them (Manual Approval). Email Preview Shows what registrants will receive — webinar title, date, time, join link, and a calendar (.ics) file attachment. Additional Message (optional) Add a custom message that appears above the standard confirmation content. Use this for instructions, what to expect, or anything you want registrants to see right away. 2 Auto-Approve — Confirmation Sent Immediately If your registration is set to Auto-Approve Registrations , the confirmation email is sent to the registrant as soon as they submit the form. Screenshot ↑ Approval Mode set to Auto-Approve — registrants receive confirmation immediately. Details Auto-Approve Registrations Default mode. Registrant submits the form → confirmation email is sent immediately with their join link. Where to set it Registration Settings in Step 2 (Event Landing Page) of the Create Webinar wizard — Approval Mode dropdown. 💡 Tip Use Auto-Approve for open or public webinars where you want to maximise registrations without any manual steps. 3 Manual Approval — You Control When Confirmation is Sent If your registration is set to Manual Approval , registrants are held as Pending until you approve them. The confirmation email is only sent after you approve. Screenshot ↑ Pending registrant awaiting manual approval — confirmation email is not sent until you click Approve. Details Pending status Registrant has submitted the form but has not yet received confirmation or their join link. Approve Click to approve the registration — confirmation email is sent immediately to the registrant. Reject Click to reject — registrant is removed and does not receive a join link. Where to set it Registration Settings in Step 2 of the Create Webinar wizard — Approval Mode → Manual Approval . 📌 Heads up Registrants in Pending status cannot join the webinar. Make sure to review and approve them before the session starts. 4 What the Confirmation Email Looks Like Once approved (automatically or manually), registrants receive a confirmation email with everything they need to join. Screenshot ↑ Confirmation email showing webinar name, date, time, access link, and calendar reminder prompt. Details Webinar name Shown prominently at the top of the email. Date & Time Displayed in the timezone set during scheduling. Access link A unique join link for the registrant — clicking this takes them directly into the webinar. Calendar reminder Registrants are prompted to add the event to their calendar. A .ics file is attached. From Name Set in Email Settings — defaults to your account name. 5 Reminder Emails Toggle on automated reminder emails in Step 3 — Email Settings to notify registrants before the webinar starts. Screenshot ↑ 24-Hour Reminder and 1-Hour Reminder toggles — both on by default. Add an optional additional message. Details 24-Hour Reminder Sent automatically 24 hours before the webinar starts. Includes the webinar title, date, time, and join link. 1-Hour Reminder Sent automatically 1 hour before the webinar starts. Same content as the 24-hour reminder. Toggle on/off Each reminder can be independently toggled on or off. Toggle off if you don't want that reminder sent. Additional Message (optional) Add a custom note that appears in both reminder emails — e.g. 'Don't forget to test your audio before joining!' 💡 Tip Both reminders are on by default. We recommend keeping them both enabled — reminders significantly reduce no-shows. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Managing Your Registrants","blurb":"The Registrants panel shows your webinar's stats and everyone who has signed up.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</a><span>›</span><span>Managing Your Registrants</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</div>\n        <h1>Managing Your Registrants</h1>\n        <div><span>Business Only</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 3 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>★ Business</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>The Registrants panel shows your webinar's stats and everyone who has signed up. From here you can search and filter registrants, add or import them, resend confirmation emails, mark attendance, and download the list as a CSV.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>Step-by-Step</div>\n\n      <div><div>1</div><div><div>Open Registrants</div><div>Go to <strong>Sessions</strong> in the left sidebar and open the <strong>Upcoming</strong> tab. Find your webinar in the list and click <strong>Registrants</strong>.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/registrants-open.png\" alt=\"Upcoming Sessions list with the Registrants button highlighted on a webinar\"/></div><p>↑ Each webinar row shows its date, time and registration count. Click <strong>Registrants</strong> to open the panel.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Registrants</div><div>Opens the webinar's stats and registrant list.</div></div><div><div>Manage</div><div>Opens the webinar's settings to edit it.</div></div><div><div>Registered count</div><div>Shown on the row next to the start time, e.g. \"75 registered\".</div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>2</div><div><div>Review Webinar Stats</div><div>The panel opens with the webinar title, date, duration and time zone, followed by performance stats. Before the webinar runs, only <strong>Registered</strong> has a value; the rest fill in once the session is live and after it ends.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/registrants-overview.png\" alt=\"Webinar stats panel with metric cards, Conversion Funnel, Attendance Breakdown, Engagement and Q&A & Leads\"/></div><p>↑ Metric cards at the top, then the Conversion Funnel, Attendance Breakdown, Engagement, and Q&amp;A &amp; Leads.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Registered / Attended</div><div>Total sign-ups and how many joined live.</div></div><div><div>Show Rate</div><div>Share of registrants who attended.</div></div><div><div>Avg Watch</div><div>Average minutes attendees stayed.</div></div><div><div>Engagement</div><div>Share of attendees who interacted during the session.</div></div><div><div>Product Revenue</div><div>Sales from the webinar, where tracked.</div></div><div><div>Peak Concurrent</div><div>Most attendees in the room at once.</div></div><div><div>No-Shows</div><div>Registrants who did not attend.</div></div><div><div>Chat Messages / Replay Views</div><div>Chat activity during the session and views of the replay.</div></div><div><div>Conversion Funnel</div><div>Landing visits → Registered → Attended live → Watched replay → Booked meeting.</div></div><div><div>Attendance Breakdown</div><div>Attended, Registered (no join), No-show and Waitlisted, with counts and percentages.</div></div><div><div>Engagement</div><div>Chat messages, reactions, total watch time and peak concurrent.</div></div><div><div>Q&amp;A &amp; Leads</div><div>Questions answered and pending, leads captured and bookings.</div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>3</div><div><div>View Registrants &amp; Attendees</div><div>Scroll down to <strong>Registrants &amp; Attendees</strong>. The total appears at the top of the section, followed by the full list.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/registrants-list.png\" alt=\"Registrants & Attendees table with search, status filter, Add, Import and CSV buttons\"/></div><p>↑ The list with search, status filter and the Add, Import and CSV buttons.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Search</div><div>Find a registrant by name, email or phone.</div></div><div><div>All Statuses</div><div>Filter the list by registration status.</div></div><div><div>Add</div><div>Add a registrant manually.</div></div><div><div>Import</div><div>Bulk-add registrants from a file.</div></div><div><div>CSV</div><div>Download the list as a CSV file.</div></div><div><div>Columns</div><div>Name, Email, Phone, Status, Registered (date and time, sortable), Watch Time and Attended.</div></div><div><div>Checkboxes</div><div>Select one or more registrants, or use the header checkbox to select all.</div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>4</div><div><div>Registrant Actions</div><div>Each row has these actions on the right.</div><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Resend (circular arrow)</div><div>Sends the confirmation email to that registrant again. Use this if they didn't receive it.</div></div><div><div>Mark attended (green person icon)</div><div>Marks the registrant as attended. The Attended column updates to match.</div></div><div><div>Message (speech bubble)</div><div>Send the registrant a message by email.</div></div><div><div>Note (document icon)</div><div>Add an internal note about the registrant. Notes are for your team only and are not sent to the registrant.</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>If you reschedule a webinar, reminder emails do not update automatically. Download the CSV and notify registrants of the new date.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>5</div><div><div>Approve Pending Registrations</div><div>If you chose <strong>Manual Approval</strong> in the webinar's Registration Settings, each new registrant waits as <strong>Pending</strong> until you approve them. They see a \"Registration received\" page and get no join link until you act. A <strong>pending approval</strong> count appears above the list whenever someone is waiting.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/registrants-pending.png\" alt=\"Registrants list with one Pending registrant and approve and reject actions\"/></div><p>↑ A pending registrant. Click the green check to approve, or the red ✕ to reject.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Pending approval badge</div><div>Shows how many registrants are waiting, e.g. \"1 pending approval\".</div></div><div><div>Approve (green check)</div><div>Approves the registrant. Their status changes to <strong>Registered</strong> and they are sent the confirmation email with their join link.</div></div><div><div>Reject (red ✕)</div><div>Declines the registration. The registrant does not receive a join link.</div></div><div><div>Message (speech bubble)</div><div>Send the registrant a message by email.</div></div><div><div>Note (document icon)</div><div>Add an internal note about the registrant. Notes are for your team only and are not sent to the registrant.</div></div></div></div><div>Once approved, a <strong>Registrant approved</strong> message appears, the status changes to <strong>Registered</strong>, and the usual row actions become available.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/registrants-approved.png\" alt=\"Registrant approved banner with the registrant now showing Registered status\"/></div><p>↑ After approval, the registrant shows as Registered.</p><div><div>📌</div><div><div>Approve before the session starts</div><div>Pending registrants cannot join the webinar. Filter by status to find anyone still waiting. With Auto-Approve, every registration is confirmed immediately and this step isn't needed.</div></div></div></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div></div><div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — thanks!'\">👎 No</button></div></div>      \n    ","text":"Help Center › Scheduling & Managing Your Webinars › Managing Your Registrants Scheduling & Managing Your Webinars Managing Your Registrants Business Only 3 min read Updated April 2026 ★ Business The Registrants panel shows your webinar's stats and everyone who has signed up. From here you can search and filter registrants, add or import them, resend confirmation emails, mark attendance, and download the list as a CSV. Step-by-Step 1 Open Registrants Go to Sessions in the left sidebar and open the Upcoming tab. Find your webinar in the list and click Registrants . ↑ Each webinar row shows its date, time and registration count. Click Registrants to open the panel. Details Registrants Opens the webinar's stats and registrant list. Manage Opens the webinar's settings to edit it. Registered count Shown on the row next to the start time, e.g. \"75 registered\". 2 Review Webinar Stats The panel opens with the webinar title, date, duration and time zone, followed by performance stats. Before the webinar runs, only Registered has a value; the rest fill in once the session is live and after it ends. ↑ Metric cards at the top, then the Conversion Funnel, Attendance Breakdown, Engagement, and Q&A & Leads. Details Registered / Attended Total sign-ups and how many joined live. Show Rate Share of registrants who attended. Avg Watch Average minutes attendees stayed. Engagement Share of attendees who interacted during the session. Product Revenue Sales from the webinar, where tracked. Peak Concurrent Most attendees in the room at once. No-Shows Registrants who did not attend. Chat Messages / Replay Views Chat activity during the session and views of the replay. Conversion Funnel Landing visits → Registered → Attended live → Watched replay → Booked meeting. Attendance Breakdown Attended, Registered (no join), No-show and Waitlisted, with counts and percentages. Engagement Chat messages, reactions, total watch time and peak concurrent. Q&A & Leads Questions answered and pending, leads captured and bookings. 3 View Registrants & Attendees Scroll down to Registrants & Attendees . The total appears at the top of the section, followed by the full list. ↑ The list with search, status filter and the Add, Import and CSV buttons. Details Search Find a registrant by name, email or phone. All Statuses Filter the list by registration status. Add Add a registrant manually. Import Bulk-add registrants from a file. CSV Download the list as a CSV file. Columns Name, Email, Phone, Status, Registered (date and time, sortable), Watch Time and Attended. Checkboxes Select one or more registrants, or use the header checkbox to select all. 4 Registrant Actions Each row has these actions on the right. Details Resend (circular arrow) Sends the confirmation email to that registrant again. Use this if they didn't receive it. Mark attended (green person icon) Marks the registrant as attended. The Attended column updates to match. Message (speech bubble) Send the registrant a message by email. Note (document icon) Add an internal note about the registrant. Notes are for your team only and are not sent to the registrant. 💡 Tip If you reschedule a webinar, reminder emails do not update automatically. Download the CSV and notify registrants of the new date. 5 Approve Pending Registrations If you chose Manual Approval in the webinar's Registration Settings, each new registrant waits as Pending until you approve them. They see a \"Registration received\" page and get no join link until you act. A pending approval count appears above the list whenever someone is waiting. ↑ A pending registrant. Click the green check to approve, or the red ✕ to reject. Details Pending approval badge Shows how many registrants are waiting, e.g. \"1 pending approval\". Approve (green check) Approves the registrant. Their status changes to Registered and they are sent the confirmation email with their join link. Reject (red ✕) Declines the registration. The registrant does not receive a join link. Message (speech bubble) Send the registrant a message by email. Note (document icon) Add an internal note about the registrant. Notes are for your team only and are not sent to the registrant. Once approved, a Registrant approved message appears, the status changes to Registered , and the usual row actions become available. ↑ After approval, the registrant shows as Registered. 📌 Approve before the session starts Pending registrants cannot join the webinar. Filter by status to find anyone still waiting. With Auto-Approve, every registration is confirmed immediately and this step isn't needed. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-4","title":"Replay Emails","blurb":"After your webinar ends, you can send a Replay Email to all registrants with a link to the recorded replay.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</a><span>›</span><span>Replay Emails</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</div>\n        <h1>Replay Emails</h1>\n        <div><span>Business Only</span></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg> 2 min read</div>\n          <div><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg> Updated April 2026</div>\n          <div>★ Business</div>\n        </div>\n        <p>After your webinar ends, you can send a Replay Email to all registrants with a link to the recorded replay. This can be set to send automatically during scheduling, or triggered manually from the Webinars tab.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>Step-by-Step</div>\n\n      <div><div>1</div><div><div>Send a Replay Email Manually</div><div>From the <strong>Webinars</strong> tab in your Admin Portal, find any ended webinar and click <strong>Send Replay Email</strong>.</div><div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div></div><p>↑ Past webinars showing the Send Replay Email button alongside Manage Registrants and Event Landing Page.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Send Replay Email</div><div>Visible on ended webinars only. Sends the replay link to all approved registrants immediately.</div></div><div><div>Replay: On</div><div>Shown on the webinar card — confirms that replay is enabled and a recording is available.</div></div><div><div>When to use</div><div>Use this if you did not set Replay Email to auto-send during scheduling, or if you want to resend it to registrants.</div></div></div></div><div><div>📌</div><div><div>Auto-send vs Manual</div><div>If you toggled <strong>Replay Email</strong> on during Step 3 of the Create Webinar wizard (Email Settings), the replay email is sent automatically after the session ends. The <strong>Send Replay Email</strong> button is for manual sends or resends.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>2</div><div><div>Set Replay Email During Scheduling</div><div>The preferred way is to configure the replay email <em>before</em> the webinar — during the Email Settings step of the Create Webinar wizard.</div><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Replay Email toggle</div><div>Enable in Step 3 (Email Settings) of the Create Webinar wizard. Automatically sends the replay link to all registrants after the webinar ends.</div></div><div><div>Replay Expiration Date</div><div>Optionally set a date after which the replay link expires. Leave blank for no expiration.</div></div><div><div>Require registration to watch replay</div><div>If enabled in Registration Settings, viewers must complete the registration form before accessing the replay.</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>Always enable <strong>Auto-Record</strong> and <strong>Replay Email</strong> together when scheduling a webinar. This ensures your replay is captured and delivered to registrants automatically — no manual steps needed after the session.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      </div>\n      <div></div><div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button><button onclick=\"this.textContent='Noted — thanks!'\">👎 No</button></div></div>      \n    ","text":"Help Center › Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars › Replay Emails Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars Replay Emails Business Only 2 min read Updated April 2026 ★ Business After your webinar ends, you can send a Replay Email to all registrants with a link to the recorded replay. This can be set to send automatically during scheduling, or triggered manually from the Webinars tab. Step-by-Step 1 Send a Replay Email Manually From the Webinars tab in your Admin Portal, find any ended webinar and click Send Replay Email . Screenshot ↑ Past webinars showing the Send Replay Email button alongside Manage Registrants and Event Landing Page. Details Send Replay Email Visible on ended webinars only. Sends the replay link to all approved registrants immediately. Replay: On Shown on the webinar card — confirms that replay is enabled and a recording is available. When to use Use this if you did not set Replay Email to auto-send during scheduling, or if you want to resend it to registrants. 📌 Auto-send vs Manual If you toggled Replay Email on during Step 3 of the Create Webinar wizard (Email Settings), the replay email is sent automatically after the session ends. The Send Replay Email button is for manual sends or resends. 2 Set Replay Email During Scheduling The preferred way is to configure the replay email before the webinar — during the Email Settings step of the Create Webinar wizard. Details Replay Email toggle Enable in Step 3 (Email Settings) of the Create Webinar wizard. Automatically sends the replay link to all registrants after the webinar ends. Replay Expiration Date Optionally set a date after which the replay link expires. Leave blank for no expiration. Require registration to watch replay If enabled in Registration Settings, viewers must complete the registration form before accessing the replay. 💡 Tip Always enable Auto-Record and Replay Email together when scheduling a webinar. This ensures your replay is captured and delivered to registrants automatically — no manual steps needed after the session. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-5","title":"Panelist & Attendee Roles","blurb":"Understand the difference between hosts, co-hosts, presenters, panelists, and attendees.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</a><span>›</span><span>Panelist &amp; Attendee Roles</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</div>\n        <h1>Panelist &amp; Attendee Roles</h1>\n        <div><span>Business Only</span></div>\n        <div><div>⏱ 3 min read</div><div>📅 Updated April 2026</div></div>\n        <p>Understand the difference between hosts, co-hosts, presenters, panelists, and attendees.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>Step-by-Step</div>\n      <div><div>1</div><div><div>Coming soon</div><div>This article is being built.</div><div><div><div>📷</div><div>Coming soon</div></div></div></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button></div></div>\n    ","text":"Help Center › Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars › Panelist &amp; Attendee Roles Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars Panelist &amp; Attendee Roles Business Only ⏱ 3 min read 📅 Updated April 2026 Understand the difference between hosts, co-hosts, presenters, panelists, and attendees. Step-by-Step 1 Coming soon This article is being built. 📷 Coming soon Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes","headings":[]},{"id":"art-6","title":"Managing Scheduled Webinars","blurb":"Manage your upcoming webinars from the Sessions page, then review the full analytics report once a webinar has ended.","html":"\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</a><span>›</span><span>Managing Scheduled Webinars</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</div>\n        <h1>Managing Scheduled Webinars</h1>\n        <div><span>Business Only</span></div>\n        <div><div>⏱ 3 min read</div><div>📅 Updated April 2026</div></div>\n        <p>Manage your upcoming webinars from the Sessions page, then review the full analytics report once a webinar has ended.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>Upcoming Webinars</div>\n      <div><div>1</div><div><div>Manage an Upcoming Webinar</div><div>Go to <strong>Sessions</strong> in the left sidebar and open the <strong>Upcoming</strong> tab. Every scheduled webinar is listed with its date, start time and registration count.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/registrants-open.png\" alt=\"Upcoming Sessions list with Webinar Start Links and the Registrants and Manage buttons\"/></div><p>↑ The Upcoming tab. Each webinar row has <strong>Registrants</strong> and <strong>Manage</strong> buttons.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Webinar Start Links</div><div>Webinars scheduled in the next 30 days, each with a <strong>Start Webinar</strong> button.</div></div><div><div>Registrants</div><div>See who has signed up, add or import registrants, and download the list. See <strong>Managing Your Registrants</strong>.</div></div><div><div>Manage</div><div>Open the webinar's settings to edit it.</div></div><div><div>Registered count and countdown</div><div>Shown on each row, e.g. \"75 registered · starts in 31 hours\".</div></div></div></div><div><div>📌</div><div><div>Analytics come after the webinar</div><div>Before the webinar runs, the stats in the Registrants panel stay at zero except for Registered. The full analytics report below is available once the webinar has ended.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div>After the Webinar — Analytics</div>\n\n      <div><div>2</div><div><div>Open Analytics for a Past Webinar</div><div>Once a webinar has ended, its Registrants panel becomes a full analytics report. Open the ended webinar from <strong>Sessions</strong> and click <strong>Registrants</strong>. The report opens with the webinar title, date, duration and time zone at the top.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/webinar-analytics-overview.png\" alt=\"Webinar analytics panel with metric cards, Conversion Funnel and Attendance Breakdown\"/></div><p>↑ Analytics for an ended webinar: metric cards, Conversion Funnel and Attendance Breakdown.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Registered</div><div>Total sign-ups.</div></div><div><div>Attended</div><div>Registrants who joined live.</div></div><div><div>Show Rate</div><div>Attended as a share of Registered.</div></div><div><div>Avg Watch</div><div>Average minutes each attendee stayed.</div></div><div><div>Engagement</div><div>Share of attendees who interacted during the session.</div></div><div><div>Product Revenue</div><div>Sales from the webinar. Shows \"Not tracked yet\" when no sales are connected.</div></div><div><div>Peak Concurrent</div><div>Most attendees in the room at the same time.</div></div><div><div>No-Shows</div><div>Registrants who did not join.</div></div><div><div>Chat Messages</div><div>Messages sent in chat during the session.</div></div><div><div>Replay Views</div><div>Views of the recording after the session.</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>These numbers are final once the webinar ends. For an upcoming webinar, only Registered has a value.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>3</div><div><div>Conversion Funnel and Attendance Breakdown</div><div>The <strong>Conversion Funnel</strong> follows registrants from the landing page to a booked meeting. The <strong>Attendance Breakdown</strong> splits your registrant list by what each person did.</div><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Conversion Funnel</div><div>Landing visits → Registered → Attended live → Watched replay → Booked meeting, each with a count and percentage.</div></div><div><div>Attended</div><div>Joined the live session.</div></div><div><div>Registered (no join)</div><div>Registered but has not joined yet.</div></div><div><div>No-show</div><div>Registered and did not attend the live session.</div></div><div><div>Waitlisted</div><div>On the waitlist for a full webinar.</div></div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>4</div><div><div>Engagement, Retention and Devices</div><div>Scroll down for engagement totals, the Audience Retention Curve and device breakdown.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/webinar-analytics-engagement.png\" alt=\"Engagement, Q&A & Leads, Audience Retention Curve and Devices panels\"/></div><p>↑ Engagement and Q&amp;A totals, the Audience Retention Curve with its peak drop marker, and the Devices breakdown.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Engagement</div><div>Chat messages, reactions, total watch time across all attendees, and peak concurrent.</div></div><div><div>Q&amp;A &amp; Leads</div><div>Questions answered and pending, leads captured and bookings made.</div></div><div><div>Audience Retention Curve</div><div>How many viewers stayed over the length of the session. The red dotted line marks the <strong>peak drop</strong>, the point where the most viewers left.</div></div><div><div>Devices</div><div>Share of attendees on Desktop, Mobile and Tablet.</div></div></div></div><div><div>📌</div><div><div>Collapsible sections</div><div>Click the arrow on the right of Audience Retention Curve, Devices or Registrants &amp; Attendees to collapse or expand that section.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      <div><div>5</div><div><div>Registrant Status</div><div>At the bottom, <strong>Registrants &amp; Attendees</strong> lists everyone with a status showing what they did. Use the <strong>All Statuses</strong> dropdown to show one status at a time.</div><div><img src=\"assets/img/webinar-analytics-registrants.png\" alt=\"Registrants & Attendees list showing Registered, Attended and replay_viewer statuses\"/></div><p>↑ Status badges show whether each person attended live, watched the replay, or has only registered.</p><div><div><div>Details</div></div><div><div><div>Registered</div><div>Signed up but has not attended the live session or watched the replay.</div></div><div><div>Attended</div><div>Joined the live session. Their <strong>Watch Time</strong> column shows how long they stayed.</div></div><div><div>replay_viewer</div><div>Did not attend live, but watched the replay.</div></div><div><div>Guest emails</div><div>Attendees who joined as guests without registering show a generated address ending in <strong>@anonymous.studio.local</strong>.</div></div></div></div><div><div>💡</div><div><div>Tip</div><div>Filter by status and click <strong>CSV</strong> to download a list, e.g. no-shows for a follow-up email or replay viewers for a sales sequence.</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button></div></div>>\n      <div><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com/home\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#\">Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</a><span>›</span><span>Going Live — Webinar Host Controls</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><span></span> Scheduling &amp; Managing Your Webinars</div>\n        <h1>Going Live — Webinar Host Controls</h1>\n        <div><span>Business Only</span></div>\n        <div><div>⏱ 3 min read</div><div>📅 Updated April 2026</div></div>\n        <p>What to expect when you start your webinar — the host view and stage controls.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>Step-by-Step</div>\n      <div><div>1</div><div><div>Coming soon</div><div>This article is being built.</div><div><div><div>📷</div><div>Coming soon</div></div></div></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div></div>\n      <div><p>Was this article helpful?</p><div><button onclick=\"this.textContent='👍 Thanks!'\">👍 Yes</button></div></div>\n    \n\n  </main>\n\n  <!-- RIGHT SIDEBAR -->\n  <aside>\n    <div>In This Category</div>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(0)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Scheduling Your Webinar</a>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(1)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Event Landing Page</a>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(2)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Email Confirmation &amp; Reminders</a>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(3)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Managing Your Registrants</a>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(4)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Replay Emails</a>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(5)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Panelist &amp; Attendee Roles </a>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(6)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Managing Scheduled Webinars </a>\n    <a onclick=\"showArticle(7)\" href=\"#\"><span></span> Going Live — Webinar Host Controls </a>\n    <div></div>\n    <a href=\"https://studio.r-link.com/dashboard/help-support\">\n      <svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg>\n      Contact Support\n    </a>\n  </aside>\n\n","text":"Help Center › Scheduling & Managing Your Webinars › Managing Scheduled Webinars Scheduling & Managing Your Webinars Managing Scheduled Webinars Business Only ⏱ 3 min read 📅 Updated April 2026 Manage your upcoming webinars from the Sessions page, then review the full analytics report once a webinar has ended. Upcoming Webinars 1 Manage an Upcoming Webinar Go to Sessions in the left sidebar and open the Upcoming tab. Every scheduled webinar is listed with its date, start time and registration count. ↑ The Upcoming tab. Each webinar row has Registrants and Manage buttons. Details Webinar Start Links Webinars scheduled in the next 30 days, each with a Start Webinar button. Registrants See who has signed up, add or import registrants, and download the list. See Managing Your Registrants . Manage Open the webinar's settings to edit it. Registered count and countdown Shown on each row, e.g. \"75 registered · starts in 31 hours\". 📌 Analytics come after the webinar Before the webinar runs, the stats in the Registrants panel stay at zero except for Registered. The full analytics report below is available once the webinar has ended. After the Webinar — Analytics 2 Open Analytics for a Past Webinar Once a webinar has ended, its Registrants panel becomes a full analytics report. Open the ended webinar from Sessions and click Registrants . The report opens with the webinar title, date, duration and time zone at the top. ↑ Analytics for an ended webinar: metric cards, Conversion Funnel and Attendance Breakdown. Details Registered Total sign-ups. Attended Registrants who joined live. Show Rate Attended as a share of Registered. Avg Watch Average minutes each attendee stayed. Engagement Share of attendees who interacted during the session. Product Revenue Sales from the webinar. Shows \"Not tracked yet\" when no sales are connected. Peak Concurrent Most attendees in the room at the same time. No-Shows Registrants who did not join. Chat Messages Messages sent in chat during the session. Replay Views Views of the recording after the session. 💡 Tip These numbers are final once the webinar ends. For an upcoming webinar, only Registered has a value. 3 Conversion Funnel and Attendance Breakdown The Conversion Funnel follows registrants from the landing page to a booked meeting. The Attendance Breakdown splits your registrant list by what each person did. Details Conversion Funnel Landing visits → Registered → Attended live → Watched replay → Booked meeting, each with a count and percentage. Attended Joined the live session. Registered (no join) Registered but has not joined yet. No-show Registered and did not attend the live session. Waitlisted On the waitlist for a full webinar. 4 Engagement, Retention and Devices Scroll down for engagement totals, the Audience Retention Curve and device breakdown. ↑ Engagement and Q&A totals, the Audience Retention Curve with its peak drop marker, and the Devices breakdown. Details Engagement Chat messages, reactions, total watch time across all attendees, and peak concurrent. Q&A & Leads Questions answered and pending, leads captured and bookings made. Audience Retention Curve How many viewers stayed over the length of the session. The red dotted line marks the peak drop , the point where the most viewers left. Devices Share of attendees on Desktop, Mobile and Tablet. 📌 Collapsible sections Click the arrow on the right of Audience Retention Curve, Devices or Registrants & Attendees to collapse or expand that section. 5 Registrant Status At the bottom, Registrants & Attendees lists everyone with a status showing what they did. Use the All Statuses dropdown to show one status at a time. ↑ Status badges show whether each person attended live, watched the replay, or has only registered. Details Registered Signed up but has not attended the live session or watched the replay. Attended Joined the live session. Their Watch Time column shows how long they stayed. replay_viewer Did not attend live, but watched the replay. Guest emails Attendees who joined as guests without registering show a generated address ending in @anonymous.studio.local . 💡 Tip Filter by status and click CSV to download a list, e.g. no-shows for a follow-up email or replay viewers for a sales sequence. Was this article helpful? 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]}],"elements":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Elements Overview","blurb":"Elements are the building blocks of every R-Link Studio session — pre-built, reusable components you prepare in advance and activate instantly while you're live.","html":"\n  <nav><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#elements/art-0\" >Elements</a><span>›</span><span>Elements Overview</span></nav>\n  <div><span></span>Elements</div>\n  <h1>Elements Overview</h1>\n  <div>\n    <span><span></span>All Plans</span>\n    <span><span></span>Business — All Elements</span>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg>5 min read</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg>Updated May 2026</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg>Beginner</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Elements are the building blocks of every R-Link Studio session — pre-built, reusable components you prepare in advance and activate instantly while you're live. This article gives you a full picture of what Elements are, where to find them, every type available, and how Shared Libraries work.</p>\n  <div>\n    <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M21.44 11.05l-9.19 9.19a6 6 0 0 1-8.49-8.49l9.19-9.19a4 4 0 0 1 5.66 5.66l-9.2 9.19a2 2 0 0 1-2.83-2.83l8.49-8.48\"/></svg></div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Basic vs Business — What's Different with Elements</div>\n      <div>\n        <p><strong>Basic Plan</strong> — Core elements: Image / File, Video, Audio, Sound Effect, and Presentation.</p>\n        <p><strong>Business Plan</strong> — All Basic elements plus: CTA Banner, Talking Point, Web Overlay, Poll, Timer, Prompter, Product Showcase, Lead Capture, Auction, and Contract.</p>\n        <p>Not sure which plan you're on? See <a href=\"#best-practices/art-1\">Understanding Your Plan</a>.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div>OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>How Elements Work in R-Link Studio</div>\n      <p>Elements are created and saved in your <strong>Elements Library</strong> in the Admin Portal, under <strong>Studio Assets</strong> — before your session starts. Once you're live, every saved element appears in the studio <strong>Left Panel</strong>, ready to activate with a single click.</p>\n      <div>Elements are pre-built before a session and activated from the studio Left Panel while live.</div>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>The + Add Element list inside the studio Left Panel showing all available element types.</div></div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">HOW THE FLOW WORKS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Step 1 — Create</td><td>Go to <strong>Studio Assets → Elements</strong>. Click <strong>+ Add Element</strong>, choose a type, configure it, and save it to your library.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Step 2 — Organise</td><td>Group elements into <strong>Folders</strong> by session or event. Use <strong>Favorites</strong> to pin your most-used elements for quick access.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Step 3 — Activate Live</td><td>In a live session, open the Left Panel, find your element, and click to activate it instantly for all participants.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Step 4 — Reuse</td><td>Elements are saved permanently. Build once, use across as many sessions as you need.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Element Types at a Glance</div>\n      <p>R-Link Studio has 13 element types. Here's a full overview — each grouped by category to match your Elements Library.</p>\n      <div>All 13 types are available from the + Add Element button in the Elements Library or in the studio. The library groups them into four categories — Promote, Engage, Sell and Show — which you can filter by.</div>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>The Elements Library in the Admin Panel with the + Add Element dropdown open showing all 13 element types.</div></div>\n\n      <div>Show <span>All Plans</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"23 7 16 12 23 17 23 7\"/><rect x=\"1\" y=\"5\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"/></svg></div><span>Video</span></div><p>Play a pre-recorded video clip — product demos, intros, or supporting content.</p><div><span>All Plans</span><a href=\"#elements/art-3\" >Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M9 18V5l12-2v13\"/><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"18\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"16\" r=\"3\"/></svg></div><span>Audio</span></div><p>Play background music, sound effects, or audio files during your session.</p><div><span>All Plans</span><a href=\"#elements/art-3\" >Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"2\" y=\"3\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"21\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"21\"/></svg></div><span>Presentation</span></div><p>Share a slide deck in the session — upload and advance slides while you present.</p><div><span>All Plans</span><a href=\"#elements/art-3\" >Learn More →</a></div></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>Engage <span>Business Plan</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z\"/><line x1=\"9\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"15\" y2=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"7\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/></svg></div><span>CTA Banner</span></div><p>Display a call-to-action banner on screen with a headline and clickable link.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"18\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"3.01\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"3.01\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"3.01\" y2=\"18\"/></svg></div><span>Talking Point</span></div><p>Private on-screen notes visible only to the presenter — speaker cues and reminders.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"2\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"22\" y2=\"12\"/><path d=\"M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z\"/></svg></div><span>Web Overlay</span></div><p>Embed a live webpage directly into your session — websites, forms, or tools.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><line x1=\"18\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"18\" y2=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"4\"/><line x1=\"6\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"6\" y2=\"14\"/></svg></div><span>Poll</span></div><p>Ask your audience a question and display live voting results on screen.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg></div><span>Timer</span></div><p>Display a countdown or count-up timer on screen for timed activities.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"18\"/></svg></div><span>Prompter</span></div><p>A built-in teleprompter scrolling your script — visible to the presenter only.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>Sell <span>Business Plan</span></div>\n      <div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M6 2L3 6v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V6l-3-4z\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"6\"/><path d=\"M16 10a4 4 0 0 1-8 0\"/></svg></div><span>Product Showcase</span></div><p>Display a product card with image, description, and a buy or link button.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z\"/><polyline points=\"22,6 12,13 2,6\"/></svg></div><span>Lead Capture</span></div><p>Pop up a form to collect attendee name, email, and custom fields into your Leads.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M3 3h2l.4 2M7 13h10l4-8H5.4M7 13L5.4 5M7 13l-2.293 2.293c-.63.63-.184 1.707.707 1.707H17m0 0a2 2 0 1 0 0 4 2 2 0 0 0 0-4zm-8 2a2 2 0 1 0 0 4 2 2 0 0 0 0-4z\"/></svg></div><span>Auction</span></div><p>Run a live auction — display an item, set a bid, and collect bids from attendees.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n        <div><div><div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z\"/><polyline points=\"14 2 14 8 20 8\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"13\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div><span>Contract</span></div><p>Present a contract for attendees to review and sign digitally in real time.</p><div><span>Business</span><a href=\"#\">Learn More →</a></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>3</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>The Elements Library</div>\n      <p>The <strong>Elements Library</strong> is your home base for creating and organising all elements. Find it in the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> under <strong>Studio Assets</strong> in the left sidebar, on the <strong>Elements</strong> tab.</p>\n      <div>Admin Portal → Studio Assets → Elements. Your library is shared across all sessions in your account.</div>\n      <div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/studio-assets-elements-library.png\" alt=\"Studio Assets page on the Elements tab showing the Elements Library, Library sidebar and element cards\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Studio Assets → Elements. The Library sidebar sits on the left, search and category filters above your elements.</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">ELEMENTS LIBRARY — KEY FEATURES</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Studio Assets tabs</td><td>Elements sits alongside <strong>Room Presets</strong> and <strong>Event Landing Pages</strong> at the top of the page.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Library sidebar</td><td><strong>All</strong>, <strong>Favorites</strong> and your <strong>Folders</strong>, each with a live count of what is inside.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Category filters</td><td><strong>Promote</strong>, <strong>Engage</strong>, <strong>Sell</strong> and <strong>Show</strong> — filter the view down to one family of element types.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Cards / Table</td><td>Switch between visual cards with a preview and a compact table list.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>New folder</td><td>Create a folder to organise elements by session, topic, or event.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Copilot</td><td>An assistant panel at the top of the library that helps you build elements from a description.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n","text":"Help Center › Elements › Elements Overview Elements Elements Overview All Plans Business — All Elements 5 min read Updated May 2026 Beginner Elements are the building blocks of every R-Link Studio session — pre-built, reusable components you prepare in advance and activate instantly while you're live. This article gives you a full picture of what Elements are, where to find them, every type available, and how Shared Libraries work. Basic vs Business — What's Different with Elements Basic Plan — Core elements: Image / File, Video, Audio, Sound Effect, and Presentation. Business Plan — All Basic elements plus: CTA Banner, Talking Point, Web Overlay, Poll, Timer, Prompter, Product Showcase, Lead Capture, Auction, and Contract. Not sure which plan you're on? See Understanding Your Plan . OVERVIEW 1 How Elements Work in R-Link Studio Elements are created and saved in your Elements Library in the Admin Portal, under Studio Assets — before your session starts. Once you're live, every saved element appears in the studio Left Panel , ready to activate with a single click. Elements are pre-built before a session and activated from the studio Left Panel while live. Screenshot The + Add Element list inside the studio Left Panel showing all available element types. HOW THE FLOW WORKS Step 1 — Create Go to Studio Assets → Elements . Click + Add Element , choose a type, configure it, and save it to your library. Step 2 — Organise Group elements into Folders by session or event. Use Favorites to pin your most-used elements for quick access. Step 3 — Activate Live In a live session, open the Left Panel, find your element, and click to activate it instantly for all participants. Step 4 — Reuse Elements are saved permanently. Build once, use across as many sessions as you need. 2 Element Types at a Glance R-Link Studio has 13 element types. Here's a full overview — each grouped by category to match your Elements Library. All 13 types are available from the + Add Element button in the Elements Library or in the studio. The library groups them into four categories — Promote, Engage, Sell and Show — which you can filter by. Screenshot The Elements Library in the Admin Panel with the + Add Element dropdown open showing all 13 element types. Show All Plans Video Play a pre-recorded video clip — product demos, intros, or supporting content. All Plans Learn More → Audio Play background music, sound effects, or audio files during your session. All Plans Learn More → Presentation Share a slide deck in the session — upload and advance slides while you present. All Plans Learn More → Engage Business Plan CTA Banner Display a call-to-action banner on screen with a headline and clickable link. Business Learn More → Talking Point Private on-screen notes visible only to the presenter — speaker cues and reminders. Business Learn More → Web Overlay Embed a live webpage directly into your session — websites, forms, or tools. Business Learn More → Poll Ask your audience a question and display live voting results on screen. Business Learn More → Timer Display a countdown or count-up timer on screen for timed activities. Business Learn More → Prompter A built-in teleprompter scrolling your script — visible to the presenter only. Business Learn More → Sell Business Plan Product Showcase Display a product card with image, description, and a buy or link button. Business Learn More → Lead Capture Pop up a form to collect attendee name, email, and custom fields into your Leads. Business Learn More → Auction Run a live auction — display an item, set a bid, and collect bids from attendees. Business Learn More → Contract Present a contract for attendees to review and sign digitally in real time. Business Learn More → 3 The Elements Library The Elements Library is your home base for creating and organising all elements. Find it in the Admin Portal under Studio Assets in the left sidebar, on the Elements tab. Admin Portal → Studio Assets → Elements. Your library is shared across all sessions in your account. ↑ Studio Assets → Elements. The Library sidebar sits on the left, search and category filters above your elements. ELEMENTS LIBRARY — KEY FEATURES Studio Assets tabs Elements sits alongside Room Presets and Event Landing Pages at the top of the page. Library sidebar All , Favorites and your Folders , each with a live count of what is inside. Category filters Promote , Engage , Sell and Show — filter the view down to one family of element types. Cards / Table Switch between visual cards with a preview and a compact table list. New folder Create a folder to organise elements by session, topic, or event. Stream Copilot An assistant panel at the top of the library that helps you build elements from a description.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Creating & Managing Your Elements","blurb":"This article walks you through everything you need to build and manage your element library — from creating your first element to organising with folders, favorites, and search.","html":"\n  <nav><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#elements/art-0\" >Elements</a><span>›</span><span>Creating &amp; Managing Your Elements</span></nav>\n  <div><span></span>Elements</div>\n  <h1>Creating &amp; Managing Your Elements</h1>\n  <div>\n    <span><span></span>All Plans</span>\n    <span><span></span>Business — All Elements</span>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg>5 min read</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg>Updated May 2026</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg>Beginner</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>This article walks you through everything you need to build and manage your element library — from creating your first element to organising with folders, favorites, and search so you're fully prepared before any session goes live.</p>\n  <div>OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Navigating to the Elements Library</div>\n      <p>All element management happens in the <strong>Elements Library</strong> — open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong>, click <strong>Studio Assets</strong> in the left sidebar, and stay on the <strong>Elements</strong> tab. It is the central place to create, organise, and maintain every element for your sessions.</p>\n      <div>Admin Portal → Studio Assets → Elements. Only accessible to account Admins and the Owner.</div>\n      <div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/studio-assets-elements-library.png\" alt=\"Studio Assets page on the Elements tab showing the Elements Library, Library sidebar and element cards\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Studio Assets → Elements. The Library sidebar sits on the left, search and category filters above your elements.</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">ELEMENTS LIBRARY — AT A GLANCE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Library sidebar</td><td><strong>All</strong>, <strong>Favorites</strong> and your <strong>Folders</strong> — click any one to filter the view. Each shows a count.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Search all folders</td><td>Find any element across your entire library instantly by name.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Category filters</td><td><strong>Promote</strong>, <strong>Engage</strong>, <strong>Sell</strong>, <strong>Show</strong> — narrow the view to one family of element types.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Cards / Table</td><td>Toggle between card view (with a preview and Play button) and a compact table list.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>+ Add Element</td><td>Create a new element — opens the element type selector.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>New folder</td><td>Create a new folder to organise elements by session, topic, or event.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Copilot</td><td>An assistant panel at the top of the library — describe what you need and it helps you build the element.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Creating a New Element</div>\n      <p>Click <strong>+ Add Element</strong> to start building. Choose the element type, configure its settings, give it a name, and save it to your library.</p>\n      <div>The + Add Element button is available in the Elements Library and inside the studio Left Panel while live.</div>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>The + Add Element dropdown showing all 13 element types available.</div></div>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>In the Admin Portal, go to <strong>Studio Assets</strong> in the left sidebar and open the <strong>Elements</strong> tab.</span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>Click <strong>+ Add Element</strong>. The element type list will appear.</span></li>\n        <li><span>3</span><span>Select the element type you want to create.</span></li>\n        <li><span>4</span><span>Fill in the element's name, content, and type-specific settings.</span></li>\n        <li><span>5</span><span>Click <strong>Save</strong>. Your element is now in the library, ready for any session.</span></li>\n      </ol>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Pro Tip — Build Before You Go Live</div><div><p>Create and name all your elements before your session starts. Once you're live, activation is a single click — the more you prepare in advance, the smoother your session flow.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>3</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Organising with Folders</div>\n      <p>Folders let you group elements by session, event, or topic so your library stays tidy and you can find the right elements instantly. Think of each folder as a setlist for a specific show.</p>\n      <div>Folders appear in the main Elements Library view. Each folder displays the number of elements inside it.</div>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>The folder ⋮ action menu — Rename, Share..., and Delete.</div></div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">WORKING WITH FOLDERS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Create a Folder</td><td>Click <strong>+ Folder</strong> (top right). Name it to match the session or event.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Expand a Folder</td><td>Click the <strong>›</strong> arrow next to the folder name to see the elements inside.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Reorder Folders</td><td>Drag folders by the <strong>⠿</strong> grip handle on the left to reorder them.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Rename</td><td>Open the folder's ⋮ menu and select <strong>Rename</strong>.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Delete</td><td>Open the folder's ⋮ menu and select <strong>Delete</strong>. Elements return to the root library.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Pro Tip — Name Folders After Your Sessions</div><div><p>A folder per recurring session keeps your library organised as it grows. Order elements inside the folder to match the sequence you'll use them — your flow is ready before you go live.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>4</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Finding Elements — Favorites, Search, Filters &amp; Views</div>\n      <p>For elements you reuse across sessions, <strong>Favorites</strong>, <strong>Search</strong> and the <strong>category filters</strong> let you find them instantly — without digging through folders.</p>\n      <div>Favorites lives in the Library sidebar. Search and the category filters sit above your elements.</div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">FAVORITES &amp; SEARCH</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Mark as Favorite</td><td>Open the element's ⋮ menu and select <strong>Favorite</strong> to star it. The star shows as filled when active.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>View Favorites</td><td>Click <strong>Favorites</strong> in the Library sidebar to filter to only starred elements.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Remove Favorite</td><td>Open the element's ⋮ menu and select <strong>Favorite</strong> again to unstar it. The element stays in your library.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Search</td><td>Type in the <strong>Search all folders...</strong> bar to instantly filter your entire library by element name — works across all folders.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Filter by category</td><td>Click <strong>Promote</strong>, <strong>Engage</strong>, <strong>Sell</strong> or <strong>Show</strong> to see only that family of element types. Click again to clear.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Cards vs Table</td><td><strong>Cards</strong> shows each element with a preview thumbnail, its type, date and a Play button. <strong>Table</strong> lists more elements at once in a compact row view — useful for large libraries.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>5</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Editing, Duplicating &amp; Deleting Elements</div>\n      <p>Every element has a <strong>⋮ action menu</strong> — hover over the element row to reveal it. From here you can update, copy, move, or remove elements.</p>\n      <div>The ⋮ action menu appears on the right side of each element row on hover.</div>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>The element ⋮ action menu — Rename, Edit, Preview, Share, Duplicate, Favorite, Share..., Move to, and Delete.</div></div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">ELEMENT ACTION MENU (⋮)</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Rename</td><td>Update the element's display name without opening the full editor.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Edit</td><td>Open the element's full settings to update content, configuration, or type-specific options.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Preview</td><td>See exactly how the element will appear when activated during a live session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Duplicate</td><td>Create an identical copy saved to your library — useful for building variations of the same element type.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Favorite</td><td>Star the element to add it to your Favorites filter.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Move to</td><td>Move the element into a specific folder — a submenu lists your available folders.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Delete</td><td>Permanently removes the element. This action cannot be undone.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Before You Delete</div><div><p>Deleted elements cannot be recovered. If there's any chance you'll reuse one, <strong>Duplicate</strong> it first to keep a copy before deleting the original.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"5\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"19\" r=\"3\"/><line x1=\"8.59\" y1=\"13.51\" x2=\"15.42\" y2=\"17.49\"/><line x1=\"15.41\" y1=\"6.51\" x2=\"8.59\" y2=\"10.49\"/></svg></div>\n    <div><div>Want to Share Elements with Other Users?</div><div><p>You can share any folder from your Elements Library with other R-Link Studio users using a simple share code. See <a href=\"#elements/art-3\" >Sharing Elements →</a></p></div></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div>\n      <button onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n","text":"Help Center › Elements › Creating &amp; Managing Your Elements Elements Creating &amp; Managing Your Elements All Plans Business — All Elements 5 min read Updated May 2026 Beginner This article walks you through everything you need to build and manage your element library — from creating your first element to organising with folders, favorites, and search so you're fully prepared before any session goes live. OVERVIEW 1 Navigating to the Elements Library All element management happens in the Elements Library — open the Admin Portal , click Studio Assets in the left sidebar, and stay on the Elements tab. It is the central place to create, organise, and maintain every element for your sessions. Admin Portal → Studio Assets → Elements. Only accessible to account Admins and the Owner. ↑ Studio Assets → Elements. The Library sidebar sits on the left, search and category filters above your elements. ELEMENTS LIBRARY — AT A GLANCE Library sidebar All , Favorites and your Folders — click any one to filter the view. Each shows a count. Search all folders Find any element across your entire library instantly by name. Category filters Promote , Engage , Sell , Show — narrow the view to one family of element types. Cards / Table Toggle between card view (with a preview and Play button) and a compact table list. + Add Element Create a new element — opens the element type selector. New folder Create a new folder to organise elements by session, topic, or event. Stream Copilot An assistant panel at the top of the library — describe what you need and it helps you build the element. 2 Creating a New Element Click + Add Element to start building. Choose the element type, configure its settings, give it a name, and save it to your library. The + Add Element button is available in the Elements Library and inside the studio Left Panel while live. Screenshot The + Add Element dropdown showing all 13 element types available. 1 In the Admin Portal, go to Studio Assets in the left sidebar and open the Elements tab. 2 Click + Add Element . The element type list will appear. 3 Select the element type you want to create. 4 Fill in the element's name, content, and type-specific settings. 5 Click Save . Your element is now in the library, ready for any session. Pro Tip — Build Before You Go Live Create and name all your elements before your session starts. Once you're live, activation is a single click — the more you prepare in advance, the smoother your session flow. 3 Organising with Folders Folders let you group elements by session, event, or topic so your library stays tidy and you can find the right elements instantly. Think of each folder as a setlist for a specific show. Folders appear in the main Elements Library view. Each folder displays the number of elements inside it. Screenshot The folder ⋮ action menu — Rename, Share..., and Delete. WORKING WITH FOLDERS Create a Folder Click + Folder (top right). Name it to match the session or event. Expand a Folder Click the › arrow next to the folder name to see the elements inside. Reorder Folders Drag folders by the ⠿ grip handle on the left to reorder them. Rename Open the folder's ⋮ menu and select Rename . Delete Open the folder's ⋮ menu and select Delete . Elements return to the root library. Pro Tip — Name Folders After Your Sessions A folder per recurring session keeps your library organised as it grows. Order elements inside the folder to match the sequence you'll use them — your flow is ready before you go live. 4 Finding Elements — Favorites, Search, Filters &amp; Views For elements you reuse across sessions, Favorites , Search and the category filters let you find them instantly — without digging through folders. Favorites lives in the Library sidebar. Search and the category filters sit above your elements. FAVORITES &amp; SEARCH Mark as Favorite Open the element's ⋮ menu and select Favorite to star it. The star shows as filled when active. View Favorites Click Favorites in the Library sidebar to filter to only starred elements. Remove Favorite Open the element's ⋮ menu and select Favorite again to unstar it. The element stays in your library. Search Type in the Search all folders... bar to instantly filter your entire library by element name — works across all folders. Filter by category Click Promote , Engage , Sell or Show to see only that family of element types. Click again to clear. Cards vs Table Cards shows each element with a preview thumbnail, its type, date and a Play button. Table lists more elements at once in a compact row view — useful for large libraries. 5 Editing, Duplicating &amp; Deleting Elements Every element has a ⋮ action menu — hover over the element row to reveal it. From here you can update, copy, move, or remove elements. The ⋮ action menu appears on the right side of each element row on hover. Screenshot The element ⋮ action menu — Rename, Edit, Preview, Share, Duplicate, Favorite, Share..., Move to, and Delete. ELEMENT ACTION MENU (⋮) Rename Update the element's display name without opening the full editor. Edit Open the element's full settings to update content, configuration, or type-specific options. Preview See exactly how the element will appear when activated during a live session. Duplicate Create an identical copy saved to your library — useful for building variations of the same element type. Favorite Star the element to add it to your Favorites filter. Move to Move the element into a specific folder — a submenu lists your available folders. Delete Permanently removes the element. This action cannot be undone. Before You Delete Deleted elements cannot be recovered. If there's any chance you'll reuse one, Duplicate it first to keep a copy before deleting the original. Want to Share Elements with Other Users? You can share any folder from your Elements Library with other R-Link Studio users using a simple share code. See Sharing Elements → Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Launching Elements in the Live Studio","blurb":"Once you're live in R-Link Studio, your elements are one click away.","html":"\n  <nav><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#elements/art-0\" >Elements</a><span>›</span><span>Launching Elements in the Live Studio</span></nav>\n  <div><span></span>Elements</div>\n  <h1>Launching Elements in the Live Studio</h1>\n  <div>\n    <span><span></span>All Plans</span>\n    <span><span></span>Business — All Elements</span>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg>4 min read</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg>Updated May 2026</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg>Beginner</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Once you're live in R-Link Studio, your elements are one click away. This article walks you through finding your elements in the studio, launching them on stage, and controlling them while your session is running.</p>\n\n  <div>OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <!-- S1: The Elements Panel -->\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>The Elements Panel in the Studio</div>\n      <p>Once your session is live, all your saved elements are accessible from the <strong>Elements</strong> section in the <strong>Studio Controls</strong> panel on the left side of the studio. This is your command centre for everything you launch on stage.</p>\n      <div>The Left Panel shows Studio Controls → Elements. Your folders and elements load automatically from your library when you enter the session.</div>\n      <div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/studio-elements-panel-live.png\" alt=\"Live R-Link Studio session with the Studio Controls Elements panel open on the left\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Studio Controls → Elements inside a live session. Your folders load automatically from Studio Assets.</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">ELEMENTS PANEL — LIVE STUDIO</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Stream Copilot</td><td>An assistant card at the top of the panel — describe an element and it helps you build it mid-session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Search</td><td>Search elements by name to find what you need quickly during a live session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Favorites</td><td>Filter to only your starred elements for instant access to your most-used items.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>New folder</td><td>Create a folder without leaving the session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>+ Folder / + Add Element</td><td>Create new folders or add new elements on the fly without stopping your session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Element Folders</td><td>Your library folders appear below — expand any folder to see the elements inside, then click to launch.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- S2: Launching an Element -->\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Launching an Element on Stage</div>\n      <p>Activating an element is a single click. The element goes live immediately for all participants — no loading screen, no delay.</p>\n      <div>The active element highlights in purple in the Left Panel so you always know what's currently running on stage.</div>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>In the <strong>Elements</strong> section of the Left Panel, expand the folder containing the element you want to launch.</span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>Click the element name. It activates instantly — appearing on stage for all participants.</span></li>\n        <li><span>3</span><span>The element row highlights <strong>purple</strong> in the Left Panel, confirming it is currently active and live on stage.</span></li>\n        <li><span>4</span><span>To switch to a different element, simply click another one. The previous element is automatically removed from stage.</span></li>\n      </ol>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Pro Tip — Order Your Elements Like a Setlist</div>\n        <div><p>Arrange elements inside a folder in the order you'll use them during your session. You can then work top to bottom through the list as your session flows — no searching, no hesitation while you're live.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- S3: Controls While Live -->\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>3</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Element Controls While Live</div>\n      <p>Each element type has its own set of controls that appear when it's active. Here's what you'll see for each Core Element.</p>\n      <div>Controls appear on the stage area — not in the Left Panel — when an element is actively running.</div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"2\" y=\"3\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"21\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"21\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Pop Out Presenter — Keep the Host Visible on Stage</div>\n        <div><p>Whenever an element takes over the stage — whether it's a video, audio, or presentation — a <strong>Pop Out Presenter</strong> button appears in the bottom right corner of the stage area. Clicking it opens the host's camera feed in a separate floating window so participants can still see and hear the presenter alongside the element content. This keeps the session feel personal and connected, even when a video or slide is the focus.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-0\">Audio Controls</h3>\n      <p>When an Audio element is active, a <strong>floating playback bar</strong> appears at the bottom of the stage. No visual is shown on stage for participants — audio plays through the room.</p>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>Audio element active — the floating playback bar at the bottom of the stage showing title, progress, play/pause, repeat, loop, volume, and stop controls.</div></div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">AUDIO PLAYBACK BAR</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Progress Bar</td><td>Shows current playback position and total duration (e.g. 0:00 / 0:30).</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Play / Pause</td><td>Start or pause audio playback.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Repeat</td><td>Replay the audio from the beginning.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Loop</td><td>Toggle looping on or off during the session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Volume</td><td>Adjust the volume of this audio element in real time.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>✕ Stop</td><td>Stops the audio and removes it from stage.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-1\">Video Controls</h3>\n      <p>When a Video element is active, the video fills the stage (or appears in Picture in Picture / Background depending on the Display Mode setting). Controls appear on the video itself.</p>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>Video element active on stage — playing in full screen mode with play/pause and progress controls on the video, and an ✕ button to stop.</div></div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">VIDEO CONTROLS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Play / Pause</td><td>Start or pause the video.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Progress Bar</td><td>Shows current playback time and total duration (e.g. 0:13 / 1:18).</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Volume</td><td>Adjust the video's volume during playback.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>✕ Stop</td><td>Stops the video and removes it from stage.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-2\">Presentation Controls</h3>\n      <p>When a Presentation element is active, the document displays on stage with a full control bar at the bottom and an <strong>annotation toolbar</strong> at the top — letting you draw, highlight, and mark up slides in real time.</p>\n      <div><div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div><div>Presentation element active — showing the slide on stage, page navigation (1/11), annotation toolbar at top, and End button.</div></div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">PRESENTATION CONTROLS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>‹ / › Navigation</td><td>Advance to the next slide or go back to the previous one. Page count shows your position (e.g. 1/11).</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Zoom</td><td>Zoom in or out on the current slide for a closer look at details.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Full Screen ⛶</td><td>Expand the presentation to fill the entire stage view.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>End</td><td>Stops the presentation and removes it from stage.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">ANNOTATION TOOLBAR</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Pen</td><td>Draw freehand on the slide — visible to all participants in real time.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Highlighter</td><td>Highlight text or areas on the slide.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Square / Circle / Arrow</td><td>Draw shapes and arrows to point out specific content.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Colors &amp; Size</td><td>Choose annotation color and line thickness.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Fade</td><td>Set how many seconds annotations stay visible before fading out.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Clear</td><td>Remove all current annotations from the slide.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- S4: Stopping Elements -->\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>4</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Stopping &amp; Switching Elements</div>\n      <p>Removing an element from stage is as straightforward as launching it.</p>\n      <div>Only one element of each type can be active at a time. Launching a second element of the same type replaces the first.</div>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">HOW TO STOP OR SWITCH</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Click ✕ or End</td><td>Every active element has a stop button (✕ or <strong>End</strong>) in its control bar. Click it to immediately remove the element from stage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Click Another Element</td><td>Clicking a different element in the Left Panel automatically stops the current one and launches the new one in a single action.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Click the Active Element</td><td>Clicking the currently active (purple-highlighted) element in the Left Panel will deactivate and remove it from stage without launching anything new.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"16\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Elements Don't Affect Your Mic or Camera</div>\n        <div><p>Launching or stopping an element doesn't mute your microphone or turn off your camera. Your live feed continues uninterrupted — elements are an <em>addition</em> to your session, not a replacement for it. The only exception is Audio Ducking, which temporarily lowers mic volume while audio plays if enabled in the element settings.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div>\n      <button onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n","text":"Help Center › Elements › Launching Elements in the Live Studio Elements Launching Elements in the Live Studio All Plans Business — All Elements 4 min read Updated May 2026 Beginner Once you're live in R-Link Studio, your elements are one click away. This article walks you through finding your elements in the studio, launching them on stage, and controlling them while your session is running. OVERVIEW 1 The Elements Panel in the Studio Once your session is live, all your saved elements are accessible from the Elements section in the Studio Controls panel on the left side of the studio. This is your command centre for everything you launch on stage. The Left Panel shows Studio Controls → Elements. Your folders and elements load automatically from your library when you enter the session. ↑ Studio Controls → Elements inside a live session. Your folders load automatically from Studio Assets. ELEMENTS PANEL — LIVE STUDIO Stream Copilot An assistant card at the top of the panel — describe an element and it helps you build it mid-session. Search Search elements by name to find what you need quickly during a live session. Favorites Filter to only your starred elements for instant access to your most-used items. New folder Create a folder without leaving the session. + Folder / + Add Element Create new folders or add new elements on the fly without stopping your session. Element Folders Your library folders appear below — expand any folder to see the elements inside, then click to launch. 2 Launching an Element on Stage Activating an element is a single click. The element goes live immediately for all participants — no loading screen, no delay. The active element highlights in purple in the Left Panel so you always know what's currently running on stage. 1 In the Elements section of the Left Panel, expand the folder containing the element you want to launch. 2 Click the element name. It activates instantly — appearing on stage for all participants. 3 The element row highlights purple in the Left Panel, confirming it is currently active and live on stage. 4 To switch to a different element, simply click another one. The previous element is automatically removed from stage. Pro Tip — Order Your Elements Like a Setlist Arrange elements inside a folder in the order you'll use them during your session. You can then work top to bottom through the list as your session flows — no searching, no hesitation while you're live. 3 Element Controls While Live Each element type has its own set of controls that appear when it's active. Here's what you'll see for each Core Element. Controls appear on the stage area — not in the Left Panel — when an element is actively running. Pop Out Presenter — Keep the Host Visible on Stage Whenever an element takes over the stage — whether it's a video, audio, or presentation — a Pop Out Presenter button appears in the bottom right corner of the stage area. Clicking it opens the host's camera feed in a separate floating window so participants can still see and hear the presenter alongside the element content. This keeps the session feel personal and connected, even when a video or slide is the focus. Audio Controls When an Audio element is active, a floating playback bar appears at the bottom of the stage. No visual is shown on stage for participants — audio plays through the room. Screenshot Audio element active — the floating playback bar at the bottom of the stage showing title, progress, play/pause, repeat, loop, volume, and stop controls. AUDIO PLAYBACK BAR Progress Bar Shows current playback position and total duration (e.g. 0:00 / 0:30). Play / Pause Start or pause audio playback. Repeat Replay the audio from the beginning. Loop Toggle looping on or off during the session. Volume Adjust the volume of this audio element in real time. ✕ Stop Stops the audio and removes it from stage. Video Controls When a Video element is active, the video fills the stage (or appears in Picture in Picture / Background depending on the Display Mode setting). Controls appear on the video itself. Screenshot Video element active on stage — playing in full screen mode with play/pause and progress controls on the video, and an ✕ button to stop. VIDEO CONTROLS Play / Pause Start or pause the video. Progress Bar Shows current playback time and total duration (e.g. 0:13 / 1:18). Volume Adjust the video's volume during playback. ✕ Stop Stops the video and removes it from stage. Presentation Controls When a Presentation element is active, the document displays on stage with a full control bar at the bottom and an annotation toolbar at the top — letting you draw, highlight, and mark up slides in real time. Screenshot Presentation element active — showing the slide on stage, page navigation (1/11), annotation toolbar at top, and End button. PRESENTATION CONTROLS ‹ / › Navigation Advance to the next slide or go back to the previous one. Page count shows your position (e.g. 1/11). Zoom Zoom in or out on the current slide for a closer look at details. Full Screen ⛶ Expand the presentation to fill the entire stage view. End Stops the presentation and removes it from stage. ANNOTATION TOOLBAR Pen Draw freehand on the slide — visible to all participants in real time. Highlighter Highlight text or areas on the slide. Square / Circle / Arrow Draw shapes and arrows to point out specific content. Colors &amp; Size Choose annotation color and line thickness. Fade Set how many seconds annotations stay visible before fading out. Clear Remove all current annotations from the slide. 4 Stopping &amp; Switching Elements Removing an element from stage is as straightforward as launching it. Only one element of each type can be active at a time. Launching a second element of the same type replaces the first. HOW TO STOP OR SWITCH Click ✕ or End Every active element has a stop button (✕ or End ) in its control bar. Click it to immediately remove the element from stage. Click Another Element Clicking a different element in the Left Panel automatically stops the current one and launches the new one in a single action. Click the Active Element Clicking the currently active (purple-highlighted) element in the Left Panel will deactivate and remove it from stage without launching anything new. Elements Don't Affect Your Mic or Camera Launching or stopping an element doesn't mute your microphone or turn off your camera. Your live feed continues uninterrupted — elements are an addition to your session, not a replacement for it. The only exception is Audio Ducking, which temporarily lowers mic volume while audio plays if enabled in the element settings. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[{"id":"h-0","text":"Audio Controls","level":3},{"id":"h-1","text":"Video Controls","level":3},{"id":"h-2","text":"Presentation Controls","level":3}]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Core Elements","blurb":"Image / File, Video, Audio, Sound Effect and Presentation — the media elements available on both Basic and Business plans.","html":"\n  <nav><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#elements/art-0\" >Elements</a><span>›</span><span>Core Elements</span></nav>\n  <div><span></span>Elements</div>\n  <h1>Core Elements</h1>\n  <div>\n    <span><span></span>All Plans</span>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg>6 min read</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg>Updated May 2026</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg>Beginner</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>The Core Elements are available on both Basic and Business plans. These are the foundation of any R-Link Studio session, letting you play videos, add audio, and share slide decks directly on stage. This article walks you through setting up each one.</p>\n\n  <div>OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <!-- ── VIDEO ── -->\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Video</div>\n      <p>The Video element lets you play a pre-recorded video clip directly on stage during your session — visible to all participants. Use it for product demos, intro clips, testimonials, or any pre-recorded content you want to present as part of your session flow.</p>\n      <div>Video elements play on the main stage. You control when to start them — they don't play automatically unless Autoplay is enabled.</div>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-0\">Step 1 — Choose Your Video Source</h3>\n      <p>When creating or editing a Video element, you have three ways to source your video:</p>\n\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">VIDEO SOURCE OPTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Upload</td><td>Upload a video file directly from your computer. Supported formats: <strong>MP4, MOV, WebM</strong> — max file size <strong>1 GB</strong>. The file is saved to your account.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Library</td><td>Pick a video you've already uploaded. Keeps your elements organised without re-uploading the same file.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>URL</td><td>Link to an external video using a direct video URL. Click <strong>Validate</strong> to confirm the URL is a playable video before saving.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n          <div>Upload tab — drag and drop or click to upload an MP4, MOV, or WebM file up to 1 GB.</div>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n          <div>URL tab — paste a direct video URL and click Validate to confirm it's playable.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div><div>\n        <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        <div>Library tab — pick from videos you have already uploaded.</div>\n      </div></div>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-1\">Step 2 — Name, Folder &amp; Description</h3>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">ELEMENT DETAILS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Video Name <span>Required</span></td><td>Give the element a clear name so you can identify it quickly in your library during a live session (e.g. \"Intro Video\", \"Product Demo Q2\").</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Folder <span>Required</span></td><td>Assign the element to a folder in your library. Keeps your elements organised by session or event.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Description</td><td>Optional internal notes about the video — not visible to attendees. Useful for reminding yourself when or how to use this clip.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-2\">Step 3 — Configure Playback Settings</h3>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">PLAYBACK SETTINGS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Autoplay</td><td>When <strong>ON</strong> — the video starts playing automatically the moment you add it to the stage. When <strong>OFF</strong> — the video is placed on stage but you control when it starts.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Loop</td><td>When <strong>ON</strong> — the video repeats automatically when it finishes. When <strong>OFF</strong> — it plays once and stops.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-3\">Step 4 — Audio Mode &amp; Display Mode</h3>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">AUDIO MODE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Normal</td><td>Full volume. The video audio plays at its original volume alongside any other audio in the session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Background</td><td>Ducks other audio — lowers the volume of other audio sources (microphones, music) while the video plays, so the video is heard clearly.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Muted</td><td>No sound. The video plays silently — useful for background visual content or when the presenter is talking over the video.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">DISPLAY MODE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Full Screen</td><td>The video fills the entire stage — takes over the full viewing area for all participants. Best for main content videos.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Picture in Picture</td><td>The video appears as a small overlay on the stage while the presenter remains visible. Good for supplementary clips.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Background</td><td>The video plays behind participants — visible as a video background layer. Good for intro loops or branded backgrounds.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Pro Tip — Upload Before You Go Live</div>\n        <div><p>Upload your videos before your session starts. Using the <strong>Library</strong> source tab is faster than re-uploading each time, and keeps your elements lightweight. Remember: video files count toward your storage limit (<strong>Basic: 10 GB / Business: 50 GB</strong>).</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- ── AUDIO ── -->\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Audio</div>\n      <p>The Audio element lets you play music, sound effects, or any audio file during your session — heard by all participants without any video on screen. Use it for background music while attendees join, intro music, transitions between segments, or any audio-only content.</p>\n      <div>Audio plays through the session room for all participants. No visual appears on stage — audio only.</div>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-4\">Step 1 — Choose Your Audio Source</h3>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">AUDIO SOURCE OPTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Upload</td><td>Upload an audio file from your computer. Supported formats: <strong>MP3, WAV, AAC, OGG, M4A</strong> — max file size <strong>50 MB</strong>. The file is saved to your account.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Library</td><td>Select from audio files you have already uploaded — no re-uploading needed.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>URL</td><td>Link to an external audio file using a direct URL. Click <strong>Validate</strong> to confirm the URL is a playable audio file before saving.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n          <div>Upload tab — click to upload MP3, WAV, AAC, OGG, or M4A up to 50 MB.</div>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n          <div>Library tab — browse and select from your uploaded audio files.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div><div>\n        <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        <div>URL tab — paste a direct audio URL and click Validate to confirm it's playable.</div>\n      </div></div>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-5\">Step 2 — Name, Folder, Category &amp; Description</h3>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">ELEMENT DETAILS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Audio Name <span>Required</span></td><td>Give the element a clear name for quick identification in your library (e.g. \"Intro Music\", \"Background Lo-fi\").</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Folder <span>Required</span></td><td>Assign the element to a folder to keep your library organised by session or event.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Category</td><td>Classify the audio by type (e.g. Background Music, Sound Effect). Helps filter and locate elements quickly across a large library.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Description</td><td>Optional internal notes — not visible to attendees. Useful for noting when or how to use the clip.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-6\">Step 3 — Configure Playback Settings</h3>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">PLAYBACK SETTINGS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Autoplay</td><td>When <strong>ON</strong> — audio starts playing automatically the moment you activate the element. When <strong>OFF</strong> — the element is queued and you start playback manually.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Loop</td><td>When <strong>ON</strong> — the audio repeats automatically when it finishes. When <strong>OFF</strong> — it plays once and stops.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Volume</td><td>Set the playback volume with the slider (0–100%). Default is 80%. Adjusts the volume of this audio element independently from other audio in the session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Audio Ducking</td><td>When <strong>ON</strong> — automatically reduces the volume of microphones and other audio sources while this audio plays, so it can be heard clearly. When <strong>OFF</strong> — all audio plays at its set level simultaneously.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"16\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Audio vs Video — Key Differences</div>\n        <div>\n          <p>Audio elements have no Display Mode — they are audio only, nothing appears on stage visually. The Audio element also has a <strong>Category</strong> field and a <strong>Volume slider</strong> that Video doesn't have, giving you more granular control over how audio fits into your session mix.</p>\n          <p>Max upload size for Audio is <strong>50 MB</strong> (compared to 1 GB for Video).</p>\n        </div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- ── PRESENTATION ── -->\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>3</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Presentation</div>\n      <p>The Presentation element lets you display documents and files directly on stage — visible to all participants as you advance through them. Despite the name, it's not limited to slide decks. You can upload <strong>PDFs, Word documents, PowerPoint files, Excel spreadsheets, and images</strong> — making it a versatile tool for sharing any visual content during your session.</p>\n      <div>The file is displayed on stage page by page. You advance it manually from the Left Panel during the session.</div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"16\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Not Just PowerPoint</div>\n        <div><p>The Presentation element accepts a wide range of file types — use it for sales decks, one-pagers, contracts, spreadsheets, product images, infographics, or any document you want to walk attendees through on screen. <strong>PowerPoint files are automatically converted to PDF</strong> when uploaded.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <h3 id=\"h-7\">Setting Up a Presentation Element</h3>\n\n      <div><div>\n        <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        <div>The Edit Presentation modal — Name, Folder, and File upload. Simple and clean.</div>\n      </div></div>\n\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">PRESENTATION ELEMENT — FIELDS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Name <span>Required</span></td><td>Give the element a clear name for easy identification in your library (e.g. \"Q4 Sales Deck\", \"Onboarding Slides\", \"Product Brochure\").</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Folder <span>Required</span></td><td>Assign to a folder to keep your library organised by session or event.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>File <span>Required</span></td><td>Upload the file you want to present. Click the upload area or drag and drop your file directly.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">SUPPORTED FILE TYPES &amp; LIMITS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Documents</td><td>PDF, Word (.doc, .docx)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Presentations</td><td>PowerPoint (.ppt, .pptx) — automatically converted to PDF on upload</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Spreadsheets</td><td>Excel (.xls, .xlsx)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Images</td><td>JPG, PNG, GIF</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Max File Size</td><td><strong>100 MB</strong></td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div>Pro Tips</div>\n        <div>\n          <p><strong>Convert to PDF before uploading</strong> — while PowerPoint converts automatically, exporting to PDF yourself first gives you more control over how fonts and layouts render on screen.</p>\n          <p><strong>One element per file</strong> — create a separate Presentation element for each document so your library stays organised and you can swap between different files mid-session without confusion.</p>\n        </div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div>\n      <button onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n","text":"OVERVIEW 1 How the Create Flow Works Every Core Element opens the same kind of dialog. Step 1 is always where it goes and what it is — a Folder, a name, and the file itself. Media types then have a second step for playback or display settings. A Live Preview panel on the right shows exactly what will appear on stage. Use Hide Preview to collapse it. SHARED ACROSS EVERY CORE ELEMENT Folder Required Pick which folder the element is saved into, or click + New to create one without leaving the dialog. Name Required A clear name so you can find the element quickly mid-session — \"Intro Video\", \"Q4 Sales Deck\", \"Applause Sting\". Upload / Library / URL Upload a new file, pick one you have already uploaded from Library , or point at a direct file URL . Image / File and Presentation use Upload or Browse Library only. Live Preview Shows the element as it will appear on stage. Updates as soon as a file is attached. Next / Create Create saves a single-step element. Next moves to step 2 for the types that have playback or display settings. 2 Image / File Put a static image or a PDF on stage. Use it for slides you have already exported, offers, diagrams, one-pagers, or anything you want held on screen while you talk. Image / File is a single-step element — attach the file and click Create . New Image / File. The upload area lists the accepted formats and size limit; the live preview shows what will hit the stage. IMAGE / FILE — FIELDS Folder Required Where the element is saved. + New creates a folder inline. Element Name Required The name shown in your Elements library. File Required Click to upload an image or PDF — JPG, PNG, GIF, WebP, SVG, or PDF , max 50 MB . Once attached, Replace swaps the file and Remove clears it. Once Saved The file appears in your Elements library and can be dropped on the stage from either the library or the live Studio Controls panel. Other file types — zip, exe, executable archives — are blocked for safety. 3 Video Play a preloaded video clip on stage — product demos, intros, testimonials, or any pre-recorded content you want to run as part of your session. Two steps: 1 Add Video (pick or upload your video) then 2 Playback . Step 1 — Add Video. Upload a file, pick one from Library, or paste a direct video URL. VIDEO SOURCE OPTIONS Upload Upload a video from your computer. MP4, MOV, WebM — max 100 MB . Library Pick a video you have already uploaded. Faster than re-uploading the same file. URL Paste a direct video file link. R-Link validates it before you can continue. With a file attached you get a scrubbable preview, the duration and file size, and Replace / Remove. Step 2 — Playback PLAYBACK SETTINGS Autoplay When ON — the video starts playing the moment you add it to the stage. When OFF — you control when it starts. Loop When ON — the video repeats when it finishes. When OFF — it plays once and stops. AUDIO MODE Normal Full volume. The video audio plays at its original level alongside other audio in the session. Background Ducks other audio — lowers microphones and music while the video plays. Muted No sound. Useful for background visuals or when you are talking over the video. DISPLAY MODE Full Screen The video fills the entire stage. Best for main content. Picture in Picture A small overlay while you stay visible. Good for supplementary clips. Background Plays behind participants as a video background. Good for intro loops. Pro Tip — Upload Before You Go Live Upload your videos before your session starts. Using the Library tab is faster than re-uploading each time. Uploaded files count toward your storage limit ( Basic: 10 GB / Business: 50 GB ). 4 Audio Trigger sound or music during your session — background beds, intro stings, or any audio you want running under the stage. Nothing appears on screen. Two steps: 1 Add Audio then 2 Playback . Step 1 — Add Audio. The Category field classifies the clip, for example Background Music. AUDIO — STEP 1 FIELDS Audio Name Required A clear name for quick identification — \"Intro Music\", \"Background Lo-fi\". Category Classify the clip, for example Background Music . Helps you filter a large library. Upload MP3, WAV, AAC, OGG, M4A — max 50 MB . Library / URL Pick an audio file you have already uploaded, or paste a direct audio URL. Step 2 — Playback PLAYBACK SETTINGS Autoplay When ON — audio starts the moment you activate the element. When OFF — you start it manually. Loop When ON — the audio repeats when it finishes. Volume Set playback volume with the slider, independently of other audio in the session. Audio Ducking When ON — lowers microphones and other sources while this audio plays. 5 Sound Effect A one-shot trigger sting — applause, a drum hit, a notification chime. Same upload flow as Audio, but fixed to the Sound Effect category and meant to fire once rather than run underneath the session. Two steps: 1 Add Sound then 2 Playback . Step 1 — Add Sound. Category is locked to Sound Effect. SOUND EFFECT — STEP 1 FIELDS Sound Effect Name Required Name it for what it does — \"Applause Sting\", \"Chime\". Category Fixed to Sound Effect . Upload MP3, WAV, AAC, OGG, M4A — max 50 MB . Library / URL Reuse a file you have already uploaded, or paste a direct audio URL. Sound Effect vs Audio Both take the same file types and the same 50 MB limit. Use Audio for anything that runs for a while — music beds, background tracks. Use Sound Effect for short one-shot stings you fire at a moment. 6 Presentation Display a slide deck on stage and advance through it while you present. Despite the name it is not limited to slides — anything that paginates works. Two steps: 1 Upload Slides then 2 Settings . Step 1 — Upload Slides. Browse Library reuses a file you have already uploaded; Upload New takes one from your computer. PRESENTATION — STEP 1 FIELDS Presentation Name Required A clear name for your library — \"Q4 Sales Deck\", \"Onboarding Slides\". File Required Browse Library to reuse an uploaded file, or Upload New to drop one in. Required before you can continue. SUPPORTED FILE TYPES &amp; LIMITS Documents PDF Presentations PowerPoint (.ppt, .pptx), Keynote (.key) Images JPG, PNG, GIF Max File Size 200 MB Pro Tips Export to PDF before uploading — it gives you the most control over how fonts and layouts render on screen. One element per deck — a separate Presentation element for each file keeps your library clean and lets you swap decks mid-session without hunting. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[{"id":"h-0","text":"Step 1 — Choose Your Video Source","level":3},{"id":"h-1","text":"Step 2 — Name, Folder & Description","level":3},{"id":"h-2","text":"Step 3 — Configure Playback Settings","level":3},{"id":"h-3","text":"Step 4 — Audio Mode & Display Mode","level":3},{"id":"h-4","text":"Step 1 — Choose Your Audio Source","level":3},{"id":"h-5","text":"Step 2 — Name, Folder, Category & Description","level":3},{"id":"h-6","text":"Step 3 — Configure Playback Settings","level":3},{"id":"h-7","text":"Setting Up a Presentation Element","level":3}]},{"id":"art-4","title":"CTA Banner","blurb":"A clickable call-to-action overlay you drop on stream — headline, supporting line, and a button participants can click inside the studio.","html":"<div class=\"co pu\">\n    <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"11\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"/></svg></div>\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"co-h\">Business Plan Only</div>\n      <div class=\"co-t\"><p>The CTA Banner is a <strong>Business Plan</strong> element. Accounts on the Basic Plan will not see it in the Create an element panel. If you are on Basic and want clickable calls-to-action on stream, upgrade from <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> in the Admin Portal.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"e-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">The Five-Step Wizard</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">A CTA Banner is a call-to-action overlay you drop on stream — a headline, a supporting line, and a button pointing at wherever you want people to go. The button is live: participants click it inside the studio, without leaving the session. It is built through a five-step wizard, and a <strong>Live Preview</strong> on the right shows the banner on the real stage layout as you work.</p>\n      <div class=\"ov-cap\">Studio Assets → Elements → <strong>Create an element</strong> → CTA Banner → <strong>Create →</strong>.</div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">THE FIVE STEPS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>1 — Brand Kit</td><td>Choose which brand kit the banner inherits its colours and styling from.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>2 — Template</td><td>Pick a starting point built for a specific kind of offer.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>3 — Content</td><td>Text, buttons, images, and extras.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>4 — Style</td><td>Background, colors, and animation.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>5 — Placement</td><td>Format and screen position, then <strong>Create</strong>.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co bl\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"16\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">You Can Move Around</div>\n        <div class=\"co-t\"><p>The step chips along the bottom are clickable — jump back to any completed step without losing what you have entered. <strong>Folder</strong> sits at the top of most steps, so you can change where the banner is saved at any point.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"e-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 2 — Choose a Template</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Templates are starting points, not cages. Each one pre-fills the layout and copy structure for a common offer — you edit everything in the next step.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/cta-step2-template.png\" alt=\"Create CTA Banner step 2 showing the eight template options\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 2 — Pick a starting point. The live preview updates as soon as you select one.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">TEMPLATES</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Offer / Discount</td><td>Coaches, course sellers, SaaS signups.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Lead Magnet Download</td><td>Free resources, guides, ebooks.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Book a Call</td><td>Consultations, coaching sessions.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Webinar Offer Stack</td><td>Value stacks, bundles, packages.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Join Newsletter / Community</td><td>Email lists, communities, groups.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Product Spotlight</td><td>Product showcases, demos.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Event Registration</td><td>Upcoming events, workshops.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Blank Canvas</td><td>Full creative control — start from nothing.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"e-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 3 — Content</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Everything the viewer reads and clicks. The banner name is internal; the headline, subheadline and body are what goes on screen.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/cta-step3-content.png\" alt=\"Create CTA Banner step 3 showing banner name, headline, subheadline, body text and text size sliders\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 3 — Text. The Text Size sliders set headline, subheadline and body sizes in pixels.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">TEXT</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Banner name</td><td>Only you see this — it labels the banner in your elements list.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Headline</td><td>The main line on the banner, for example \"Register Now\".</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Subheadline</td><td>A supporting line under the headline, for example \"Limited time discount\".</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Body Text</td><td>Optional additional details or description.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Text Size</td><td>Independent sliders for Headline, Subheadline and Body, in pixels.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/cta-step3-content-buttons.png\" alt=\"Create CTA Banner step 3 scrolled to content spacing, buttons and bullet points\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Further down step 3 — spacing, buttons, and bullet points.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">LAYOUT &amp; BUTTONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Content Spacing</td><td><strong>Inner Padding</strong> and <strong>Content Width</strong> sliders control how tight the banner sits around its text.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Button Text / Button URL</td><td>The label on the button and the link it opens. Participants click it directly on the stage during the session — no need to drop the link in chat.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Show Button</td><td>Toggle the call-to-action button on the banner off entirely.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Primary Button Size</td><td><strong>Small</strong>, <strong>Medium</strong> or <strong>Large</strong>.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Secondary Button</td><td>Add a softer second action, like Learn More.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Bullet Points</td><td><strong>+ Add point</strong> to list what is included — useful for offer stacks.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"e-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 4 — Style</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Background, colors and how the banner arrives on screen.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/cta-step4-style.png\" alt=\"Create CTA Banner step 4 showing background type, colors and animation options\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 4 — Background, colors, and animation.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">BACKGROUND</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Gradient</td><td>An R-Link color blend. Set a <strong>Start Color</strong> and <strong>End Color</strong> by hex value.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Solid</td><td>A single color fill.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Image</td><td>Use a background image behind the CTA content.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Accent Color</td><td>Controls the primary CTA button and the matching secondary outline.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">ANIMATION</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>None</td><td>The banner simply appears.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Fade</td><td>Fades in and out.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Slide</td><td>Slides in from its placement edge.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Zoom</td><td>Scales up into place.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Bounce</td><td>Arrives with a bounce — the most attention-grabbing option.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"e-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 5 — Placement</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Where the banner sits relative to your video. Watch the live preview here — placement changes how much of the stage the banner takes from your speakers.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/cta-step5-placement.png\" alt=\"Create CTA Banner step 5 showing display mode and placement options\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 5 — Format and screen position. Create saves the banner to your library.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">DISPLAY MODE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Vertical</td><td>Left or right sidebar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Horizontal</td><td>Top or bottom strip.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Centered</td><td>Overlay block in the center of the stage.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">PLACEMENT</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Left</td><td>Pinned to the left side.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Right</td><td>Pinned to the right side.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/cta-banner-live-participant.png\" alt=\"A live session with a vertical CTA Banner pinned to the left of the stage\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ What a participant sees — a Vertical banner placed Left, running alongside the speakers.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Check the Preview at Placement</div>\n        <div class=\"co-t\"><p>A vertical banner eats a full column of the stage. If you have more than two people on screen, a horizontal strip or a centered overlay usually reads better — the live preview shows you exactly what your audience will lose.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"Business only 4 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner Business Plan Only The CTA Banner is a Business Plan element. Accounts on the Basic Plan will not see it in the Create an element panel. If you are on Basic and want clickable calls-to-action on stream, upgrade from Billing &amp; Usage in the Admin Portal. OVERVIEW 1 The Five-Step Wizard A CTA Banner is a call-to-action overlay you drop on stream — a headline, a supporting line, and a button pointing at wherever you want people to go. The button is live: participants click it inside the studio, without leaving the session. It is built through a five-step wizard, and a Live Preview on the right shows the banner on the real stage layout as you work. Studio Assets → Elements → Create an element → CTA Banner → Create → . THE FIVE STEPS 1 — Brand Kit Choose which brand kit the banner inherits its colours and styling from. 2 — Template Pick a starting point built for a specific kind of offer. 3 — Content Text, buttons, images, and extras. 4 — Style Background, colors, and animation. 5 — Placement Format and screen position, then Create . You Can Move Around The step chips along the bottom are clickable — jump back to any completed step without losing what you have entered. Folder sits at the top of most steps, so you can change where the banner is saved at any point. 2 Step 2 — Choose a Template Templates are starting points, not cages. Each one pre-fills the layout and copy structure for a common offer — you edit everything in the next step. Step 2 — Pick a starting point. The live preview updates as soon as you select one. TEMPLATES Offer / Discount Coaches, course sellers, SaaS signups. Lead Magnet Download Free resources, guides, ebooks. Book a Call Consultations, coaching sessions. Webinar Offer Stack Value stacks, bundles, packages. Join Newsletter / Community Email lists, communities, groups. Product Spotlight Product showcases, demos. Event Registration Upcoming events, workshops. Blank Canvas Full creative control — start from nothing. 3 Step 3 — Content Everything the viewer reads and clicks. The banner name is internal; the headline, subheadline and body are what goes on screen. Step 3 — Text. The Text Size sliders set headline, subheadline and body sizes in pixels. TEXT Banner name Only you see this — it labels the banner in your elements list. Headline The main line on the banner, for example \"Register Now\". Subheadline A supporting line under the headline, for example \"Limited time discount\". Body Text Optional additional details or description. Text Size Independent sliders for Headline, Subheadline and Body, in pixels. Further down step 3 — spacing, buttons, and bullet points. LAYOUT &amp; BUTTONS Content Spacing Inner Padding and Content Width sliders control how tight the banner sits around its text. Button Text / Button URL The label on the button and the link it opens. Participants click it directly on the stage during the session — no need to drop the link in chat. Show Button Toggle the call-to-action button on the banner off entirely. Primary Button Size Small , Medium or Large . Secondary Button Add a softer second action, like Learn More. Bullet Points + Add point to list what is included — useful for offer stacks. 4 Step 4 — Style Background, colors and how the banner arrives on screen. Step 4 — Background, colors, and animation. BACKGROUND Gradient An R-Link color blend. Set a Start Color and End Color by hex value. Solid A single color fill. Image Use a background image behind the CTA content. Accent Color Controls the primary CTA button and the matching secondary outline. ANIMATION None The banner simply appears. Fade Fades in and out. Slide Slides in from its placement edge. Zoom Scales up into place. Bounce Arrives with a bounce — the most attention-grabbing option. 5 Step 5 — Placement Where the banner sits relative to your video. Watch the live preview here — placement changes how much of the stage the banner takes from your speakers. Step 5 — Format and screen position. Create saves the banner to your library. DISPLAY MODE Vertical Left or right sidebar. Horizontal Top or bottom strip. Centered Overlay block in the center of the stage. PLACEMENT Left Pinned to the left side. Right Pinned to the right side. ↑ What a participant sees — a Vertical banner placed Left, running alongside the speakers. Pro Tip — Check the Preview at Placement A vertical banner eats a full column of the stage. If you have more than two people on screen, a horizontal strip or a centered overlay usually reads better — the live preview shows you exactly what your audience will lose. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-5","title":"Web Overlay","blurb":"Embed a live webpage directly on your stage — a booking form, pricing page or dashboard your audience can click and scroll themselves.","html":"<div class=\"co pu\">\n    <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"11\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"/></svg></div>\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"co-h\">Business Plan Only</div>\n      <div class=\"co-t\"><p>The Web Overlay is a <strong>Business Plan</strong> element. Accounts on the Basic Plan will not see it in the Create an element panel. If you are on Basic and want to put a live webpage on stage, upgrade from <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> in the Admin Portal.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What a Web Overlay Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">A Web Overlay embeds a live webpage directly on your stage — a pricing page, a booking form, a dashboard, a checkout. It is the real site, loaded in the session, and you can let your audience click and scroll it themselves.</p>\n      <div class=\"ov-cap\">Built in four steps: <strong>1 Page</strong>, <strong>2 Interaction</strong>, <strong>3 Placement</strong>, <strong>4 Style</strong>. A <strong>Live Preview</strong> renders the actual page as you configure it.</div>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Not Every Site Can Be Embedded</div>\n        <div class=\"co-t\"><p>Web overlays require <strong>HTTPS</strong>, and some sites block iframe embeds outright. The live preview is the fastest way to spot a blocked page before you save — if it does not render there, it will not render on stage.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 1 — Page</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The URL, a name for your library, and which folder it lands in.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/overlay-step1-page.png\" alt=\"Create Web Overlay step 1 with the URL field validated and a live preview of the page\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 1 — URL, name, and folder. A green check confirms the URL is valid; the preview loads the real page.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">PAGE — FIELDS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Folder <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>Where the overlay is saved. <strong>+ New</strong> creates a folder inline.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Webpage to Share <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>The full HTTPS URL. <strong>Test in browser</strong> opens it in a new tab so you can confirm it is the page you meant.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Overlay Name <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>The label in your elements list, for example \"R-Link Website\".</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Embedding check</td><td>A reminder that overlays need HTTPS and that some sites block embeds. Watch the live preview.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 2 — Interaction</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Who gets to drive. This is the decision that changes how the overlay feels — a page your audience can fill in themselves, or one you walk them through.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/overlay-step2-interaction.png\" alt=\"Create Web Overlay step 2 showing display mode, interaction toggles and auto refresh\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 2 — Viewer controls and refresh.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">DISPLAY MODE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Interactive</td><td>The audience can click, scroll, and explore the page themselves.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Static</td><td>You control the view; the audience only sees it.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">CONTROLS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Audience Interaction</td><td>Allow clicks, form fields, and page controls.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Audience Scrolling</td><td>Let viewers scroll inside the webpage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Overlay Header</td><td>Show a small host label and URL chip above the page.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Auto Refresh</td><td><strong>Off</strong>, <strong>30 sec</strong>, <strong>1 min</strong> or <strong>5 min</strong> — reload the page on a timer. Useful for live dashboards and counters.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Interactive for Forms, Static for Walkthroughs</div>\n        <div class=\"co-t\"><p>Put a registration or checkout page in <strong>Interactive</strong> so people can complete it without leaving the session. Use <strong>Static</strong> when you are presenting — it stops stray clicks from navigating the page away from what you are talking about.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 3 — Placement</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Where the page sits on stage and how much room it takes.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/overlay-step3-placement.png\" alt=\"Create Web Overlay step 3 showing the six position options and display size sliders\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 3 — Position and size on stage.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">POSITION</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Fullscreen</td><td>Take over the stage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Center</td><td>Focused overlay card.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Left side</td><td>Dock to the left rail.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Right side</td><td>Dock to the right rail.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Top strip</td><td>Horizontal strip above content.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Bottom strip</td><td>Horizontal strip below content.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">DISPLAY SIZE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Width / Height</td><td>How much of the stage the overlay occupies, as a percentage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stage Margin</td><td>Controls the visible safe area around the overlay.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Horizontal / Vertical Offset</td><td>Nudge the overlay off centre without changing its position preset.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Step 4 — Style</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The frame around the page and how it separates from everything behind it.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/overlay-step4-style.png\" alt=\"Create Web Overlay step 4 showing border, drop shadow, backdrop toggles and sliders\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 4 — Frame, border, and backdrop. Create Overlay saves it to your library.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">FRAME &amp; BACKDROP</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Border</td><td>Add a subtle R-Link frame around the webpage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Drop Shadow</td><td>Lift the overlay from the stage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Backdrop</td><td>Dim the stage behind the webpage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Corner Radius</td><td>How rounded the overlay's corners are, in pixels.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Opacity</td><td>How solid the overlay is over the stage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Backdrop Strength</td><td>How far the stage behind is dimmed.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/overlay-live-participant.png\" alt=\"A live session with a fullscreen web overlay showing the R-Link pricing page\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ What a participant sees — a Fullscreen overlay in Interactive mode. The INTERACTIVE badge and URL chip come from the Overlay Header toggle.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Backdrop for Fullscreen, Border for Docked</div>\n        <div class=\"co-t\"><p>A dimmed backdrop makes a centered or fullscreen overlay read as the main thing on screen. When the overlay is docked to a side rail alongside speakers, the border and drop shadow do more work than the backdrop does.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"Business only 4 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner Business Plan Only The Web Overlay is a Business Plan element. Accounts on the Basic Plan will not see it in the Create an element panel. If you are on Basic and want to put a live webpage on stage, upgrade from Billing &amp; Usage in the Admin Portal. OVERVIEW 1 What a Web Overlay Does A Web Overlay embeds a live webpage directly on your stage — a pricing page, a booking form, a dashboard, a checkout. It is the real site, loaded in the session, and you can let your audience click and scroll it themselves. Built in four steps: 1 Page , 2 Interaction , 3 Placement , 4 Style . A Live Preview renders the actual page as you configure it. Not Every Site Can Be Embedded Web overlays require HTTPS , and some sites block iframe embeds outright. The live preview is the fastest way to spot a blocked page before you save — if it does not render there, it will not render on stage. 2 Step 1 — Page The URL, a name for your library, and which folder it lands in. Step 1 — URL, name, and folder. A green check confirms the URL is valid; the preview loads the real page. PAGE — FIELDS Folder Required Where the overlay is saved. + New creates a folder inline. Webpage to Share Required The full HTTPS URL. Test in browser opens it in a new tab so you can confirm it is the page you meant. Overlay Name Required The label in your elements list, for example \"R-Link Website\". Embedding check A reminder that overlays need HTTPS and that some sites block embeds. Watch the live preview. 3 Step 2 — Interaction Who gets to drive. This is the decision that changes how the overlay feels — a page your audience can fill in themselves, or one you walk them through. Step 2 — Viewer controls and refresh. DISPLAY MODE Interactive The audience can click, scroll, and explore the page themselves. Static You control the view; the audience only sees it. CONTROLS Audience Interaction Allow clicks, form fields, and page controls. Audience Scrolling Let viewers scroll inside the webpage. Overlay Header Show a small host label and URL chip above the page. Auto Refresh Off , 30 sec , 1 min or 5 min — reload the page on a timer. Useful for live dashboards and counters. Pro Tip — Interactive for Forms, Static for Walkthroughs Put a registration or checkout page in Interactive so people can complete it without leaving the session. Use Static when you are presenting — it stops stray clicks from navigating the page away from what you are talking about. 4 Step 3 — Placement Where the page sits on stage and how much room it takes. Step 3 — Position and size on stage. POSITION Fullscreen Take over the stage. Center Focused overlay card. Left side Dock to the left rail. Right side Dock to the right rail. Top strip Horizontal strip above content. Bottom strip Horizontal strip below content. DISPLAY SIZE Width / Height How much of the stage the overlay occupies, as a percentage. Stage Margin Controls the visible safe area around the overlay. Horizontal / Vertical Offset Nudge the overlay off centre without changing its position preset. 5 Step 4 — Style The frame around the page and how it separates from everything behind it. Step 4 — Frame, border, and backdrop. Create Overlay saves it to your library. FRAME &amp; BACKDROP Border Add a subtle R-Link frame around the webpage. Drop Shadow Lift the overlay from the stage. Backdrop Dim the stage behind the webpage. Corner Radius How rounded the overlay's corners are, in pixels. Opacity How solid the overlay is over the stage. Backdrop Strength How far the stage behind is dimmed. ↑ What a participant sees — a Fullscreen overlay in Interactive mode. The INTERACTIVE badge and URL chip come from the Overlay Header toggle. Pro Tip — Backdrop for Fullscreen, Border for Docked A dimmed backdrop makes a centered or fullscreen overlay read as the main thing on screen. When the overlay is docked to a side rail alongside speakers, the border and drop shadow do more work than the backdrop does. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-6","title":"Contracts","blurb":"Put a contract on stage for participants to review and sign live. Upload a PDF or paste the text, set who signs, and choose how it displays.","html":"<div class=\"co pu\"><div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"11\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"/></svg></div><div><div class=\"co-h\">Business Plan Only</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Contracts is a <strong>Business Plan</strong> element. Accounts on the Basic Plan will not see it in the Create an element panel. To use it, upgrade from <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> in the Admin Portal.</p></div></div></div>\n<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div><span id=\"c-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">1</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">What a Contract Does</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">A Contract puts an agreement in front of your participants during a live session so they can review and sign it without leaving the room. Upload a PDF or paste the text, choose who signs and how, then launch it on stage when you’re ready.</p><div class=\"ov-cap\">Built in three steps: <strong>1 Upload Contract</strong>, <strong>2 Signatures</strong>, <strong>3 Settings</strong>. The <strong>Live Preview</strong> on the right updates as you go. Click <strong>Hide Preview</strong> to give the form more room.</div></div></div><span id=\"c-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">2</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Step 1 — Upload Contract</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Add the contract itself, either as a PDF file or as text.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-step1-upload.png\" alt=\"Create Contract step 1 with the folder selector, PDF upload area and contract text box\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 1 — Upload a PDF, or paste the contract text below.</div></div><table class=\"dt\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">UPLOAD CONTRACT — FIELDS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Folder <span style=\"color:var(--am);font-size:11px\">Required</span></td><td>Where the contract is saved. <strong>+ New</strong> creates a folder inline.</td></tr><tr><td>Upload a PDF contract</td><td>Click to upload your contract. PDF files only.</td></tr><tr><td>Contract text (for interactive mode)</td><td>Paste or type the contract text instead of uploading a file.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><span id=\"c-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">3</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Step 2 — Signatures</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Choose whether signatures are needed, how people sign, and who signs.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-step2-signatures.png\" alt=\"Create Contract step 2 with Require signatures on, signature method options and Host and Guest signature fields\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 2 — Signature method, signature fields and extra requirements.</div></div><table class=\"dt\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SIGNATURE METHOD</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Typed</td><td>The signer types their name.</td></tr><tr><td>Drawn</td><td>The signer draws their signature with a mouse or finger.</td></tr><tr><td>Either</td><td>The signer chooses typed or drawn.</td></tr></tbody></table><table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SIGNATURE FIELDS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Require signatures</td><td>Turn on to make participants sign the contract.</td></tr><tr><td>+ Add</td><td>Adds another signature field.</td></tr><tr><td>Signer (Host / Guest)</td><td>Use the menu on each field to choose who signs it. The bin icon removes the field.</td></tr><tr><td>Require date</td><td>Each signer adds today’s date.</td></tr><tr><td>Require initials</td><td>Each page needs the signer’s initials.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><span id=\"c-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">4</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Step 3 — Settings</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Name the contract and choose how it appears on stage.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-step3-settings.png\" alt=\"Create Contract step 3 with contract name, participant email, contract mode, display size and integration options\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Step 3 — Name, display mode and integrations. Click Create to save.</div></div><table class=\"dt\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SETTINGS — FIELDS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Contract name</td><td>The label in your elements list.</td></tr><tr><td>Participant email</td><td>Used for signature requests and contract notifications.</td></tr><tr><td>Integration (optional)</td><td>Connect an integration for signing, or leave it on <strong>None – Manual signing</strong>.</td></tr></tbody></table><table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">CONTRACT MODE</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interactive</td><td>Participants can edit and sign the contract live.</td></tr><tr><td>Static</td><td>Participants can review the contract but not sign it.</td></tr></tbody></table><table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">DISPLAY SIZE</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Modal</td><td>Opens in a centered window over the stage.</td></tr><tr><td>Fullscreen</td><td>Fills the entire screen.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Create</strong> to save the contract to your folder.</p><div class=\"co gr\"><div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div><div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Check the Preview Before You Create</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>The Live Preview shows the file name, the number of signature fields and who signs each one, plus the mode and display size you picked. Check it before you click Create.</p></div></div></div></div></div><span id=\"c-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">5</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Preview Your Contract</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Once the contract is created, preview it from <strong>Studio Assets</strong> to see exactly how it will appear on stage. The preview uses the mode and display size you chose in Step 3.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-preview.png\" alt=\"Contract preview in Studio Assets showing the contract in a modal window with Download PDF and the sample agreement\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ A contract in Interactive mode, shown as a Modal. The footer reminds signers that both parties must sign to complete it.</div></div><table class=\"dt\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">PREVIEW</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mode label</td><td>Shown under the contract name, for example <strong>Interactive Mode – Live Editing</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>Download PDF</td><td>Downloads a copy of the contract.</td></tr><tr><td>Signature footer</td><td>Tells signers what is needed to complete the contract, for example <strong>Both parties must sign to complete the contract</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>Close Preview</td><td>Closes the preview and returns you to Studio Assets.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><span id=\"c-s6\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">6</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Launching a Contract in the Live Studio</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">During a live session, you launch the contract from the Elements panel. It opens for you and your participants at the same time.</p><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">Launch the contract</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">In <strong>Studio Controls</strong>, open <strong>Elements</strong> and find the contract in its folder under <strong>Your Elements</strong>. Click it to put it on stage. The panel header shows <strong>1 live</strong> while it is open.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-live-1-elements.png\" alt=\"Live Studio with the Elements panel open and the contract listed under My Elements\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The contract in the My Elements folder, ready to launch.</div></div><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">What the host sees</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">The contract opens with the document at the top, the contract terms below it, and a signature box for each signer.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-live-2-host.png\" alt=\"Host view of a live contract with page navigation, Edit Terms, and Host and Participant signature boxes\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The host view. Sign Here is active in the Host Signature box.</div></div><table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">HOST CONTROLS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Page arrows</td><td>Move through the pages of the contract.</td></tr><tr><td>Edit Terms</td><td>Edit the contract terms live while the contract is open.</td></tr><tr><td>Sign Here</td><td>Opens the signature box so you can sign as the host.</td></tr><tr><td>Send for Signature</td><td>Sends the contract to the participant to sign.</td></tr><tr><td>Download PDF</td><td>Downloads a copy of the contract.</td></tr></tbody></table><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">What the participant sees</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Participants see the same contract. Their own signature box has an active <strong>Sign Here</strong> button, and the host’s box shows <strong>Awaiting host signature</strong> until you sign.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-live-3-participant.png\" alt=\"Participant view of a live contract with Propose Changes and a green Sign Here button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The participant view. Participants can propose changes or sign.</div></div><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">Proposing changes</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Participants click <strong>Propose Changes</strong> to suggest edits to the terms. They type their proposal and click <strong>Send Proposal</strong>, and the host can update the terms with <strong>Edit Terms</strong>.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-live-4-propose.png\" alt=\"Propose Changes window with a written proposal and the Send Proposal button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ A participant’s proposed change, ready to send.</div></div><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">Signing</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Each signer clicks <strong>Sign Here</strong>, signs in the box, and clicks <strong>Save Signature</strong>. <strong>Clear</strong> wipes the box so they can try again.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-live-5-sign.png\" alt=\"Sign as Participant window with a drawn signature and Clear, Cancel and Save Signature buttons\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Signing as the participant.</div></div><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">Fully executed</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">When every signer has signed, the contract shows <strong>Fully Executed</strong>. Each signature box shows the signature with the date and time it was signed. Click <strong>Download PDF</strong> to save the signed copy.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-live-6-executed.png\" alt=\"Fully executed contract with host and participant signatures and timestamps\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ A fully executed contract with both signatures.</div></div><div class=\"co gr\"><div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div><div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Settle the Terms Before Anyone Signs</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Review any proposed changes and update the terms first, then sign. That way everyone signs the final version.</p></div></div></div></div></div><span id=\"c-s7\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">7</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Sending a Contract Outside a Live Session</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">You can also send a contract for signature without opening a room. Your signer gets an email with a secure link, signs in their browser, and the signed contract is stored against your account.</p><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">Open Signed Contracts</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">In the Admin Portal, click <strong>Monetize</strong> under <strong>Grow</strong>, then open the <strong>Signed Contracts</strong> tab. Click <strong>Upload contract</strong> to add a PDF, JPG or PNG.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-monetize-empty.png\" alt=\"Monetize page with the Signed Contracts tab open and no contracts yet\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Signed Contracts before any contracts have been added.</div></div><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">Send it for signature</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Each contract appears in the list with its status and signer. Click <strong>Send link</strong> to email the signer, or copy the <strong>Latest signer link</strong> and share it yourself.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-monetize-sent.png\" alt=\"Signed Contracts list with one sent contract, the latest signer link and Send link, Open, edit and delete buttons\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ A contract with the status Sent, and the signer link above it.</div></div><table class=\"dt\" style=\"margin-top:12px\"><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SIGNED CONTRACTS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Status filters</td><td><strong>All</strong>, <strong>Draft</strong>, <strong>Sent</strong>, <strong>Signed</strong> and <strong>Expired</strong>, each with a count.</td></tr><tr><td>Search</td><td>Find contracts by name or signer.</td></tr><tr><td>Latest signer link</td><td>The most recent signing link. <strong>Copy</strong> it or <strong>Open</strong> it in a new tab.</td></tr><tr><td>Send link</td><td>Emails the signing link to the signer.</td></tr><tr><td>Open</td><td>Opens or downloads the contract file.</td></tr><tr><td>Edit / Delete</td><td>Edit the contract details, or delete the contract.</td></tr></tbody></table><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">What the signer receives</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">The signer gets an email titled <strong>Contract Ready for Signature</strong> with the contract name and expiry date. They click <strong>Review and Sign</strong> to open the signing page. The link stops working after the expiry date.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-email.png\" alt=\"Contract Ready for Signature email with the contract name, expiry date and Review and Sign button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The signing request email.</div></div><div style=\"font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:15px;color:var(--t-1);margin:26px 0 6px;\">Signing</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">On the signing page, the signer reviews the document, confirms their <strong>Legal name</strong>, and chooses <strong>Type Name</strong> or <strong>Draw Signature</strong>. They click <strong>Complete signature</strong> to submit.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-sign-page.png\" alt=\"Secure signing page with the contract PDF on the left and the Recipient signature panel on the right\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The secure signing page. The link expiry date is shown in the top right.</div></div><p class=\"ov-desc\">The signer then sees <strong>Signature complete</strong>, and you are notified that the contract is signed. It moves to the <strong>Signed</strong> filter in Signed Contracts.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/contract-sign-complete.png\" alt=\"Signature complete confirmation page\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The confirmation the signer sees after submitting.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"fb-row\"><span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span><div class=\"fb-btns\"><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">Yes</button><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">No</button></div></div>","text":"Business only 6 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner Business Plan Only Contracts is a Business Plan element. Put an agreement in front of participants during a live session so they can review and sign it. Upload Contract Signatures Settings Typed Drawn Either Interactive Static Modal Fullscreen Preview Download PDF Close Preview Launching a Contract in the Live Studio Edit Terms Send for Signature Propose Changes Send Proposal Sign Here Save Signature Fully Executed Sending a Contract Outside a Live Session Monetize Signed Contracts Upload contract Send link signer link Review and Sign Complete signature Signature complete","headings":[{"level":2,"id":"c-s1","text":"What a Contract Does"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s2","text":"Step 1 — Upload Contract"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s3","text":"Step 2 — Signatures"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s4","text":"Step 3 — Settings"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s5","text":"Preview Your Contract"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s6","text":"Launching a Contract in the Live Studio"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s7","text":"Sending a Contract Outside a Live Session"}]}],"engagement":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Getting Started with Engagement Tools","blurb":"The four live tools your audience can act on — effects, whiteboard, captions and polls — and where each one lives in the studio.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"g-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What the Engagement Tools Are</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Engagement tools are the live, in-session features your audience can act on: animated effects, a shared whiteboard, live captions, and polls. They all run from the studio toolbar along the bottom of the stage, and every one of them is visible to participants the moment you turn it on.</p>\n      <div class=\"ov-cap\">Effects, Whiteboard and Live Captions are available on <strong>all plans</strong>. Polls are a <strong>Business Plan</strong> element.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"g-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Where to Find Each One</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Everything lives in the studio, not the Admin Portal — with one exception: a Poll is built ahead of time as an element, then launched from Studio Controls.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">THE FOUR TOOLS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Reactions &amp; Effects</td><td>The <strong>✨ Effects</strong> button in the studio toolbar. Triggers a full-screen animated effect for everyone, plus Raise Hand and Be Right Back statuses.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Whiteboard</td><td>The studio side panel. Toggle it on, choose Static or Interactive, then <strong>Open Shared Whiteboard</strong>.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Live Captions</td><td>The <strong>CC</strong> button in the studio toolbar. Real-time transcription with automatic language detection.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Polls</td><td>Created as an <strong>Engage — Poll</strong> element in Studio Assets, then launched on stage from <strong>Studio Controls</strong>.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"g-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Which Tool for Which Moment</div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">CHOOSING A TOOL</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Quick energy check</td><td><strong>Effects</strong> — instant, visual, and no one has to stop talking.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Brainstorm or teach something visual</td><td><strong>Whiteboard</strong> in Interactive mode.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Accessibility, noisy rooms, mixed languages</td><td><strong>Live Captions</strong>, on from the start of the session.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>A real decision or a measurable answer</td><td><strong>Polls</strong> — structured options and a live vote count.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Set Expectations Early</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Tell people in the first minute which tools you will use. Audiences that know a poll is coming participate at a far higher rate than ones surprised by it mid-session.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"4 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What the Engagement Tools Are Engagement tools are the live, in-session features your audience can act on: animated effects, a shared whiteboard, live captions, and polls. They all run from the studio toolbar along the bottom of the stage, and every one of them is visible to participants the moment you turn it on. Effects, Whiteboard and Live Captions are available on all plans . Polls are a Business Plan element. 2 Where to Find Each One Everything lives in the studio, not the Admin Portal — with one exception: a Poll is built ahead of time as an element, then launched from Studio Controls. THE FOUR TOOLS Reactions &amp; Effects The ✨ Effects button in the studio toolbar. Triggers a full-screen animated effect for everyone, plus Raise Hand and Be Right Back statuses. Whiteboard The studio side panel. Toggle it on, choose Static or Interactive, then Open Shared Whiteboard . Live Captions The CC button in the studio toolbar. Real-time transcription with automatic language detection. Polls Created as an Engage — Poll element in Studio Assets, then launched on stage from Studio Controls . 3 Which Tool for Which Moment CHOOSING A TOOL Quick energy check Effects — instant, visual, and no one has to stop talking. Brainstorm or teach something visual Whiteboard in Interactive mode. Accessibility, noisy rooms, mixed languages Live Captions , on from the start of the session. A real decision or a measurable answer Polls — structured options and a live vote count. Pro Tip — Set Expectations Early Tell people in the first minute which tools you will use. Audiences that know a poll is coming participate at a far higher rate than ones surprised by it mid-session. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[{"level":2,"id":"a-s1","text":"Engagement Tools"},{"level":2,"id":"a-s2","text":"Tool Categories"},{"level":2,"id":"a-s3","text":"Use Cases"}]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Reactions & Effects","blurb":"Trigger animated effects for the whole room, mute incoming ones with Focus Mode, and use Raise Hand or Be Right Back.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"r-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Triggering an Effect</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Effects are full-screen animations that play for <strong>everyone</strong> in the room at once. Open the <strong>✨ Effects</strong> button in the studio toolbar and pick one — it fires immediately, no confirmation step.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/eng-effects-panel.png\" alt=\"The Effects panel showing sixteen animated effects, Focus Mode, and status buttons\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">The Effects panel — sixteen effects, Focus Mode, and the two status buttons.</div></div>\n\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">THE SIXTEEN EFFECTS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Celebration</td><td>Balloons, Confetti, Party, Stars, Sparkles</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Approval</td><td>Hearts, Applause, Thumbs Up, 100</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Reaction</td><td>Laughing, Wow, Mind Blown, Spooky</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Energy</td><td>Fire, Bolt, Rocket</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Everyone Sees It</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>An effect is not a private reaction. Anything you trigger animates across every participant's screen, so treat it the way you would treat unmuting.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"r-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Focus Mode</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Focus Mode hides <strong>incoming</strong> effects on your screen only. Everyone else still sees them, and you can still trigger your own. It is the fix for a lively audience during a moment that needs concentration — a demo, a technical walkthrough, or a guest speaker.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Presenters Should Turn It On</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>If you are sharing your screen or running a demo, switch Focus Mode on before you start. The energy stays in the room for the audience while your own view stays clean.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"r-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Status — Raise Hand and Be Right Back</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Below the effects are two statuses. Unlike effects, these persist until you clear them.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">STATUS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Raise Hand</td><td>Flags you in the participant list so the host knows you want to speak. Clear it once you have had your turn.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Be Right Back</td><td>Marks you as temporarily away so the host does not call on you or hand you the stage.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"4 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Triggering an Effect Effects are full-screen animations that play for everyone in the room at once. Open the ✨ Effects button in the studio toolbar and pick one — it fires immediately, no confirmation step. The Effects panel — sixteen effects, Focus Mode, and the two status buttons. THE SIXTEEN EFFECTS Celebration Balloons, Confetti, Party, Stars, Sparkles Approval Hearts, Applause, Thumbs Up, 100 Reaction Laughing, Wow, Mind Blown, Spooky Energy Fire, Bolt, Rocket Everyone Sees It An effect is not a private reaction. Anything you trigger animates across every participant's screen, so treat it the way you would treat unmuting. 2 Focus Mode Focus Mode hides incoming effects on your screen only. Everyone else still sees them, and you can still trigger your own. It is the fix for a lively audience during a moment that needs concentration — a demo, a technical walkthrough, or a guest speaker. Pro Tip — Presenters Should Turn It On If you are sharing your screen or running a demo, switch Focus Mode on before you start. The energy stays in the room for the audience while your own view stays clean. 3 Status — Raise Hand and Be Right Back Below the effects are two statuses. Unlike effects, these persist until you clear them. STATUS Raise Hand Flags you in the participant list so the host knows you want to speak. Clear it once you have had your turn. Be Right Back Marks you as temporarily away so the host does not call on you or hand you the stage. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[{"level":2,"id":"b-s1","text":"Reactions Overview"},{"level":2,"id":"b-s2","text":"Available Reactions"},{"level":2,"id":"b-s3","text":"Sending a Reaction"},{"level":2,"id":"b-s3b","text":"Boosted Reactions & Effects"},{"level":2,"id":"b-s3c","text":"Reactions in Chat"},{"level":2,"id":"b-s4","text":"Host Controls"},{"level":2,"id":"b-s5","text":"Best Practices"}]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Whiteboard","blurb":"One shared board for everyone in the room. Choose who can draw, use the colour and text tools, and export it as a PNG.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"w-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Turning the Whiteboard On</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The whiteboard is a shared canvas everyone in the room joins — one board per room, not a copy per person. Switch it on from the Whiteboard panel in the studio, set who is allowed to draw, then open it.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/eng-whiteboard-panel.png\" alt=\"The Whiteboard panel with the on toggle, Static and Interactive audience access, and the Open Shared Whiteboard button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">The Whiteboard panel — toggle on, choose audience access, then Open Shared Whiteboard.</div></div>\n\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">AUDIENCE ACCESS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Static</td><td>Only hosts can draw. Guests see the board but cannot change it.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Interactive</td><td>Everyone in the room can draw on the same board.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Start Static, Switch to Interactive</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Open in Static while you set up the frame or write the prompt, then switch to Interactive when you actually want contributions. It keeps the board from filling with stray marks before you are ready.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"w-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">The Board and Its Tools</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The header confirms the state of the board: that everyone in the room is on the same one, whether editing is enabled, and the board ID.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/eng-whiteboard-board.png\" alt=\"The Shared Whiteboard with its colour palette, stroke sizes, and Draw, Text, Erase and Clear tools\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">The shared board. The floating toolbar carries colours, stroke sizes, and the four tools.</div></div>\n\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">TOOLBAR</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Colours</td><td>Six pen colours — red, blue, green, yellow, purple, and black.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stroke size</td><td>Four widths, from a fine line to a thick marker.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Draw</td><td>Freehand drawing with the selected colour and width.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Text</td><td>Click anywhere on the canvas and type.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Erase</td><td>Remove individual marks.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Clear</td><td>Wipes the whole board for everyone.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Clear Cannot Be Undone</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p><strong>Clear</strong> empties the board for every person in the room. Export the board first if there is anything on it worth keeping.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"w-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Saving the Board</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\"><strong>Export PNG</strong> in the top right downloads the board exactly as it looks. Do this before you clear or close it — a board is tied to the room, so there is nothing to come back to afterwards.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Export Before Each Reset</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>In a workshop that runs several rounds on one board, export between rounds. You end the session with a record of each stage instead of just the final state.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"4 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Turning the Whiteboard On The whiteboard is a shared canvas everyone in the room joins — one board per room, not a copy per person. Switch it on from the Whiteboard panel in the studio, set who is allowed to draw, then open it. The Whiteboard panel — toggle on, choose audience access, then Open Shared Whiteboard. AUDIENCE ACCESS Static Only hosts can draw. Guests see the board but cannot change it. Interactive Everyone in the room can draw on the same board. Pro Tip — Start Static, Switch to Interactive Open in Static while you set up the frame or write the prompt, then switch to Interactive when you actually want contributions. It keeps the board from filling with stray marks before you are ready. 2 The Board and Its Tools The header confirms the state of the board: that everyone in the room is on the same one, whether editing is enabled, and the board ID. The shared board. The floating toolbar carries colours, stroke sizes, and the four tools. TOOLBAR Colours Six pen colours — red, blue, green, yellow, purple, and black. Stroke size Four widths, from a fine line to a thick marker. Draw Freehand drawing with the selected colour and width. Text Click anywhere on the canvas and type. Erase Remove individual marks. Clear Wipes the whole board for everyone. Clear Cannot Be Undone Clear empties the board for every person in the room. Export the board first if there is anything on it worth keeping. 3 Saving the Board Export PNG in the top right downloads the board exactly as it looks. Do this before you clear or close it — a board is tied to the room, so there is nothing to come back to afterwards. Pro Tip — Export Before Each Reset In a workshop that runs several rounds on one board, export between rounds. You end the session with a record of each stage instead of just the final state. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[{"level":2,"id":"c-s1","text":"Whiteboard Overview"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s2","text":"Getting Started"},{"level":2,"id":"c-s3","text":"Permissions & Controls"}]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Live Captions","blurb":"Real-time transcription with automatic language detection, and a caption language each viewer picks for themselves.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"c-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Turning Captions On</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Live captions transcribe what is said in the session in real time. Open the <strong>CC</strong> button in the studio toolbar and switch <strong>Turn on live captions</strong> on. The spoken language is detected automatically — you do not need to tell it what you are speaking.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/eng-captions-panel.png\" alt=\"The Live Captions and Translation panel with the on toggle and caption language selector\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">The Live Captions &amp; Translation panel.</div></div>\n\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SETTINGS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Turn on live captions</td><td>Starts transcription. Spoken language is detected automatically.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Caption Language</td><td>The language your captions are displayed in. Set this to the language you want to <em>read</em>, not the one being spoken.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Languages &amp; translation</td><td>Opens the full language list for translated captions.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"c-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Captions During the Session</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once on, captions appear in a bar below the stage and a <strong>Live Captions</strong> chip shows in the top bar so you can see at a glance that they are running.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/eng-captions-live.png\" alt=\"A live session with the captions bar below the stage and the Live Captions chip in the top bar\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">Captions running live. The badge on the caption bar shows the active translation, and the gear opens the settings again.</div></div>\n\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">THE CAPTION BAR</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Transcript</td><td>The last lines of speech, updating as people talk.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Language badge</td><td>Shows the active source and caption language, for example <strong>Auto to English</strong>.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Gear</td><td>Reopens the Live Captions &amp; Translation panel without leaving the stage.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Close</td><td>Hides the caption bar on your screen.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Each Person Picks Their Own Language</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Caption language is a per-viewer setting. A single session can have people reading along in several different languages at once, so there is no need to run separate sessions per language.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"c-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Getting Accurate Captions</div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT IMPROVES ACCURACY</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>A decent microphone</td><td>Headset or external mic beats laptop mics by a wide margin.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>One speaker at a time</td><td>Crosstalk is the single biggest cause of garbled captions.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Steady pace</td><td>Normal conversational speed transcribes better than a rush.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Spelling out names</td><td>Say unusual product or person names clearly the first time they come up.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Captions Are Not a Transcript of Record</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Automatic transcription makes mistakes, particularly with jargon and proper nouns. Do not rely on captions alone for legal, medical, or compliance records.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"4 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner OVERVIEW 1 Turning Captions On Live captions transcribe what is said in the session in real time. Open the CC button in the studio toolbar and switch Turn on live captions on. The spoken language is detected automatically — you do not need to tell it what you are speaking. The Live Captions &amp; Translation panel. SETTINGS Turn on live captions Starts transcription. Spoken language is detected automatically. Caption Language The language your captions are displayed in. Set this to the language you want to read , not the one being spoken. Languages &amp; translation Opens the full language list for translated captions. 2 Captions During the Session Once on, captions appear in a bar below the stage and a Live Captions chip shows in the top bar so you can see at a glance that they are running. Captions running live. The badge on the caption bar shows the active translation, and the gear opens the settings again. THE CAPTION BAR Transcript The last lines of speech, updating as people talk. Language badge Shows the active source and caption language, for example Auto to English . Gear Reopens the Live Captions &amp; Translation panel without leaving the stage. Close Hides the caption bar on your screen. Pro Tip — Each Person Picks Their Own Language Caption language is a per-viewer setting. A single session can have people reading along in several different languages at once, so there is no need to run separate sessions per language. 3 Getting Accurate Captions WHAT IMPROVES ACCURACY A decent microphone Headset or external mic beats laptop mics by a wide margin. One speaker at a time Crosstalk is the single biggest cause of garbled captions. Steady pace Normal conversational speed transcribes better than a rush. Spelling out names Say unusual product or person names clearly the first time they come up. Captions Are Not a Transcript of Record Automatic transcription makes mistakes, particularly with jargon and proper nouns. Do not rely on captions alone for legal, medical, or compliance records. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[{"level":2,"id":"d-s1","text":"Why Captions Matter"},{"level":2,"id":"d-s2","text":"Turn on Closed Captions"},{"level":2,"id":"d-s2b","text":"Choose Your Spoken & Caption Language"},{"level":2,"id":"d-s2c","text":"How Live Captions Look in Studio"}]},{"id":"art-4","title":"Polls","blurb":"Build a poll as an Engage element, launch it from Studio Controls, and watch the votes land live on stage.","html":"<div class=\"co pu\">\n    <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"11\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"/></svg></div>\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"co-h\">Business Plan Only</div>\n      <div class=\"co-t\"><p>Polls are a <strong>Business Plan</strong> element. Accounts on the Basic Plan will not see <strong>Engage — Poll</strong> in the Create an element panel. Upgrade from <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> in the Admin Portal.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"p-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Building a Poll</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">A poll is an element, not a live-only button — you build it in advance and launch it when the moment comes. Create it in <strong>Studio Assets → Elements</strong>, choose <strong>Engage — Poll</strong>, write your question and options, and save it to a folder.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT A POLL NEEDS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Question</td><td>The prompt participants see at the top of the card.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Options</td><td>The choices. Each gets its own colour dot in the results.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Selection</td><td>Whether participants pick one option or several.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Folder</td><td>Where the poll is stored so you can find it in Studio Controls.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Build Polls Before the Session</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Writing a question well takes longer than you think, and doing it live means dead air. Prepare your polls in Studio Assets the same way you prepare slides.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"p-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Launching It on Stage</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open <strong>Studio Controls</strong> in the live studio, find the poll in its folder, and launch it. It appears on stage and starts collecting votes immediately — a dot on the element in the sidebar marks it as live.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/eng-poll-live-host.png\" alt=\"A live session with a poll on stage and the Quick Poll element highlighted in the Studio Controls sidebar\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">The host view — the poll on stage, and the live Quick Poll element marked in Studio Controls.</div></div>\n\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">As the host you see the running tally: vote counts, percentages, and a fill bar per option, with the total underneath. Results update as people answer, so you can call out the shift live.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"p-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What Participants See</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Participants get the poll as a card on their screen with the question, the option list, and the running total. They tap an option to vote.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/eng-poll-participant.png\" alt=\"The poll as a participant sees it, with five options and a running vote total\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">The participant view. Long option lists scroll inside the card.</div></div>\n\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Keep Options Short and Distinct</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Options that scroll are options that get skipped. Four or five clearly different choices produce a cleaner read than eight overlapping ones.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"p-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Closing the Poll</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Close the poll from the stage when you are done. Leave it up long enough for the count to settle — most of the votes arrive in the first fifteen to twenty seconds, then it tails off. Talk through the result before you take it down; the numbers are the part people remember.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"Business only 4 min read Updated September 2026 Beginner Business Plan Only Polls are a Business Plan element. Accounts on the Basic Plan will not see Engage — Poll in the Create an element panel. Upgrade from Billing &amp; Usage in the Admin Portal. OVERVIEW 1 Building a Poll A poll is an element, not a live-only button — you build it in advance and launch it when the moment comes. Create it in Studio Assets → Elements , choose Engage — Poll , write your question and options, and save it to a folder. WHAT A POLL NEEDS Question The prompt participants see at the top of the card. Options The choices. Each gets its own colour dot in the results. Selection Whether participants pick one option or several. Folder Where the poll is stored so you can find it in Studio Controls. Pro Tip — Build Polls Before the Session Writing a question well takes longer than you think, and doing it live means dead air. Prepare your polls in Studio Assets the same way you prepare slides. 2 Launching It on Stage Open Studio Controls in the live studio, find the poll in its folder, and launch it. It appears on stage and starts collecting votes immediately — a dot on the element in the sidebar marks it as live. The host view — the poll on stage, and the live Quick Poll element marked in Studio Controls. As the host you see the running tally: vote counts, percentages, and a fill bar per option, with the total underneath. Results update as people answer, so you can call out the shift live. 3 What Participants See Participants get the poll as a card on their screen with the question, the option list, and the running total. They tap an option to vote. The participant view. Long option lists scroll inside the card. Pro Tip — Keep Options Short and Distinct Options that scroll are options that get skipped. Four or five clearly different choices produce a cleaner read than eight overlapping ones. 4 Closing the Poll Close the poll from the stage when you are done. Leave it up long enough for the count to settle — most of the votes arrive in the first fifteen to twenty seconds, then it tails off. Talk through the result before you take it down; the numbers are the part people remember. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[{"level":2,"id":"e-s1","text":"Polls Overview"},{"level":2,"id":"e-s2","text":"Create a Poll in the Admin Panel"},{"level":2,"id":"e-s2b","text":"Create on the Fly in LIVE Studio"},{"level":2,"id":"e-s2c","text":"Start & Manage the Poll"},{"level":2,"id":"e-s2d","text":"Participant Experience"},{"level":2,"id":"e-s3","text":"Poll Types"},{"level":2,"id":"e-s4","text":"Best Practices & Tips"}]}],"team-members":[{"id":"art-a","title":"Understanding the Team / Users Tab","blurb":"The Team / Users Tab lets account owners invite trusted individuals to manage their meeting room(s) on their behalf — without sharing login credentials.","html":"\n      <div><div></div>Team Members</div>\n      <h1>Understanding the Team / Users Tab</h1>\n      <div>\n        <span><span></span>Business Plan</span>\n        <span><span></span>Basic + Add-On</span>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <span>🕐 3 min read</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>📅 Updated April 2026</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>✓ Beginner</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>The <strong>Team / Users Tab</strong> lets account owners invite trusted individuals to manage their meeting room(s) on their behalf — without sharing login credentials. Each team member gets their own separate access with a specific role assigned to a specific room.</p>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>📌</span>\n        <div>\n          <div>Meeting Rooms only</div>\n          <div>The Team / Users Tab applies to <strong>Meeting Rooms</strong> only. Webinars have a separate structure and are not managed here.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>💳</span>\n        <div>\n          <div>Plan requirement</div>\n          <div><strong>Business Plan</strong> accounts can add 1 Admin and 1 Moderator per room across multiple rooms. <strong>Basic Plan</strong> accounts must purchase a <strong>Team Member Add-On</strong> to unlock team member access.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>🔄</span>\n        <div>\n          <div>Terminology update</div>\n          <div><strong>Host</strong> has been renamed to <strong>Admin</strong> and <strong>Co-Host</strong> has been renamed to <strong>Moderator</strong> across the platform.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>STEP-BY-STEP</div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>1</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Navigate to the Team / Users Tab</div>\n          <div>From your Admin Panel, click <strong>Team / Users</strong> in the left navigation. This tab is only visible to the account owner — Admins and Moderators assigned to rooms do not have access to this tab.</div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>2</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Review the Stats Overview</div>\n          <div>At the top of the page, four stat cards give you a quick snapshot of your team:</div>\n          <div>\n            <table>\n              <thead><tr><th>Stat Card</th><th>What It Shows</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span>Total Members</span></td><td>All users added across all rooms</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Active Members</span></td><td>Users who accepted their invite and created an account</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Pending Invites</span></td><td>Invites sent but not yet accepted</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Admins</span></td><td>Users with the Admin role across any room</td></tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>3</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Read the Team Members Table</div>\n          <div>Below the stats, a table lists all invited team members with the following columns:</div>\n          <div>\n            <table>\n              <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span>User</span><span>Name and email address</span></td><td>The team member's identity</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Room</span><span>Their assigned room</span></td><td>Only the owner's rooms appear here</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Role</span><span>Admin or Moderator</span></td><td>One per role per room maximum</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Status</span><span>Pending or Active</span></td><td>See Step 4 for status definitions</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Date Added</span><span>Date invite was sent</span></td><td>—</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Last Login</span><span>Most recent login</span></td><td>Shows — if the user has never logged in</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Actions</span><span>Edit, Resend, Remove</span></td><td>Edit is available even for Pending users</td></tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>4</div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Understanding Status Indicators</div>\n          <div>Each team member shows one of two statuses in the table:</div>\n          <div>\n            <table>\n              <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Indicator</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td><span><span></span><strong>Pending</strong></span></td>\n                  <td>Yellow dot</td>\n                  <td>Invitation sent. The user has not yet created their account or accepted the invite.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td><span><span></span><strong>Active</strong></span></td>\n                  <td>Green dot</td>\n                  <td>The user accepted the invite and created their account. They can now log in.</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n        <div>\n          <span>Thanks for your feedback!</span>\n          <div>\n            <button onclick=\"submitFeedback(this,'thanks-a')\">👍 Yes</button>\n            <button onclick=\"submitFeedback(this,'thanks-a')\">👎 No</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    ","text":"Team Members Understanding the Team / Users Tab Business Plan Basic + Add-On 🕐 3 min read · 📅 Updated April 2026 · ✓ Beginner The Team / Users Tab lets account owners invite trusted individuals to manage their meeting room(s) on their behalf — without sharing login credentials. Each team member gets their own separate access with a specific role assigned to a specific room. 📌 Meeting Rooms only The Team / Users Tab applies to Meeting Rooms only. Webinars have a separate structure and are not managed here. 💳 Plan requirement Business Plan accounts can add 1 Admin and 1 Moderator per room across multiple rooms. Basic Plan accounts must purchase a Team Member Add-On to unlock team member access. 🔄 Terminology update Host has been renamed to Admin and Co-Host has been renamed to Moderator across the platform. STEP-BY-STEP 1 Navigate to the Team / Users Tab From your Admin Panel, click Team / Users in the left navigation. This tab is only visible to the account owner — Admins and Moderators assigned to rooms do not have access to this tab. Screenshot 2 Review the Stats Overview At the top of the page, four stat cards give you a quick snapshot of your team: Stat Card What It Shows Total Members All users added across all rooms Active Members Users who accepted their invite and created an account Pending Invites Invites sent but not yet accepted Admins Users with the Admin role across any room Screenshot 3 Read the Team Members Table Below the stats, a table lists all invited team members with the following columns: Column Description User Name and email address The team member's identity Room Their assigned room Only the owner's rooms appear here Role Admin or Moderator One per role per room maximum Status Pending or Active See Step 4 for status definitions Date Added Date invite was sent — Last Login Most recent login Shows — if the user has never logged in Actions Edit, Resend, Remove Edit is available even for Pending users Screenshot 4 Understanding Status Indicators Each team member shows one of two statuses in the table: Status Indicator Meaning Pending Yellow dot Invitation sent. The user has not yet created their account or accepted the invite. Active Green dot The user accepted the invite and created their account. They can now log in. Was this article helpful? Thanks for your feedback! 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-b","title":"Inviting a Team Member","blurb":"Only the Account Owner of a Business Plan can invite team members. You can invite anyone — whether or not they currently have an R-Link account.","html":"\n      <div><div></div>Team Members</div>\n      <h1>Inviting a Team Member</h1>\n      <div>\n        <span><span></span>Business Plan</span>\n        <span><span></span>Basic + Add-On</span>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <span>🕐 4 min read</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>📅 Updated April 2026</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>✓ Beginner</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>Only the <strong>Account Owner of a Business Plan</strong> can invite team members. You can invite anyone — whether or not they currently have an R-Link account. Existing subscribers will be directed to log in, while new users will be prompted to create an account.</p>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>⚠️</span>\n        <div>\n          <div>Invite slots must be available</div>\n          <div>Each room supports a maximum of <strong>1 Admin</strong> and <strong>1 Moderator</strong>. If a slot is already filled, that role option is greyed out in the invite modal for that room. Remove the current member to open the slot.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>STEP-BY-STEP</div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>1</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Click Invite User</div>\n          <div>From the <strong>Team / Users Tab</strong>, click the <strong>Invite User</strong> button. A modal will open with fields to set up the invitation.</div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>2</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Fill in the Invite Form</div>\n          <div>Complete the four fields in the modal, then click <strong>Send Invitation</strong>:</div>\n          <div>\n            <table>\n              <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span>Email Address</span><span>Required</span></td><td>The invitee's email — can be anyone, subscriber or not</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Full Name</span><span>Required</span></td><td>Pre-fills on the account creation form for new users</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Room</span><span>Dropdown — your rooms only</span></td><td>Only rooms you own appear. Rooms where you are a guest do not appear.</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Role</span><span>Admin or Moderator</span></td><td>Greyed out if that slot is already filled for the selected room</td></tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>3</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Invitation Email is Sent</div>\n          <div>The system automatically sends an invitation email from <strong>support@r-link.com</strong> with subject <em>\"You've been invited to join R-Link Studio.\"</em> The invite link expires in <strong>7 days</strong>. The invited user immediately appears in your team table with <strong>Pending</strong> status.</div>\n          <div>\n            <span>💡</span>\n            <div>\n              <div>Two versions of the invite email</div>\n              <div>The email is the same for both user types — only the CTA button differs. Existing R-Link subscribers see <strong>\"Accept Invitation\"</strong> (directs them to log in). New users see <strong>\"Create Your Account\"</strong> (directs them to the account creation page).</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>4</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Existing R-Link Subscriber — Accepts &amp; Logs In</div>\n          <div>If the invitee already has an R-Link account, they click <strong>Accept Invitation</strong> and are directed to log in with their existing credentials. Once logged in, the assigned room automatically appears in their <strong>Rooms Tab</strong> — no additional steps needed on their end.</div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>5</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>New User — Creates an Account</div>\n          <div>If the invitee does not yet have an R-Link account, they click <strong>Create Your Account</strong> and land on the <strong>\"You're Invited\"</strong> page. Their email, role, and room are pre-filled and locked. They set their name and password, then click <strong>Create Account &amp; Log In</strong> — they are automatically logged in with access to their assigned room only.</div>\n          <div>\n            <span>📌</span>\n            <div>\n              <div>Room-level access only</div>\n              <div>A new user account created via an invite has access <strong>only to the assigned room</strong>. It is not a full R-Link subscription. If their access is removed, the account remains but has no room attached.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>6</div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Account Active — Access Granted</div>\n          <div>Once the invitee completes their login or account creation, their status in your team table updates from <span><span></span>Pending</span> to <span><span></span>Active</span> and their <strong>Last Login</strong> time is recorded. They can now access and manage the assigned room.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n        <div>\n          <span>Thanks for your feedback!</span>\n          <div>\n            <button onclick=\"submitFeedback(this,'thanks-b')\">👍 Yes</button>\n            <button onclick=\"submitFeedback(this,'thanks-b')\">👎 No</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    ","text":"Team Members Inviting a Team Member Business Plan Basic + Add-On 🕐 4 min read · 📅 Updated April 2026 · ✓ Beginner Only the Account Owner of a Business Plan can invite team members. You can invite anyone — whether or not they currently have an R-Link account. Existing subscribers will be directed to log in, while new users will be prompted to create an account. ⚠️ Invite slots must be available Each room supports a maximum of 1 Admin and 1 Moderator . If a slot is already filled, that role option is greyed out in the invite modal for that room. Remove the current member to open the slot. STEP-BY-STEP 1 Click Invite User From the Team / Users Tab , click the Invite User button. A modal will open with fields to set up the invitation. Screenshot 2 Fill in the Invite Form Complete the four fields in the modal, then click Send Invitation : Field Notes Email Address Required The invitee's email — can be anyone, subscriber or not Full Name Required Pre-fills on the account creation form for new users Room Dropdown — your rooms only Only rooms you own appear. Rooms where you are a guest do not appear. Role Admin or Moderator Greyed out if that slot is already filled for the selected room Screenshot 3 Invitation Email is Sent The system automatically sends an invitation email from support@r-link.com with subject \"You've been invited to join R-Link Studio.\" The invite link expires in 7 days . The invited user immediately appears in your team table with Pending status. 💡 Two versions of the invite email The email is the same for both user types — only the CTA button differs. Existing R-Link subscribers see \"Accept Invitation\" (directs them to log in). New users see \"Create Your Account\" (directs them to the account creation page). 4 Existing R-Link Subscriber — Accepts &amp; Logs In If the invitee already has an R-Link account, they click Accept Invitation and are directed to log in with their existing credentials. Once logged in, the assigned room automatically appears in their Rooms Tab — no additional steps needed on their end. Screenshot 5 New User — Creates an Account If the invitee does not yet have an R-Link account, they click Create Your Account and land on the \"You're Invited\" page. Their email, role, and room are pre-filled and locked. They set their name and password, then click Create Account &amp; Log In — they are automatically logged in with access to their assigned room only. 📌 Room-level access only A new user account created via an invite has access only to the assigned room . It is not a full R-Link subscription. If their access is removed, the account remains but has no room attached. Screenshot 6 Account Active — Access Granted Once the invitee completes their login or account creation, their status in your team table updates from Pending to Active and their Last Login time is recorded. They can now access and manage the assigned room. Was this article helpful? Thanks for your feedback! 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-c","title":"Roles & Permissions","blurb":"There are three roles involved in the Team / Users Tab for Meeting Rooms: Owner , Admin , and Moderator . Each role has a distinct level of access.","html":"\n      <div><div></div>Team Members</div>\n      <h1>Roles &amp; Permissions</h1>\n      <div>\n        <span><span></span>All Plans</span>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <span>🕐 3 min read</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>📅 Updated April 2026</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>✓ Beginner</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>There are three roles involved in the Team / Users Tab for Meeting Rooms: <strong>Owner</strong>, <strong>Admin</strong>, and <strong>Moderator</strong>. Each role has a distinct level of access. Webinar roles are managed separately and are not covered here.</p>\n\n      <div>ROLES OVERVIEW</div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>1</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><span>Owner</span> &nbsp;Account Owner</div>\n          <div>The account owner has complete control over everything — billing, all rooms, team members, and platform settings. Only the owner can access the Team / Users Tab and manage invitations.</div>\n          <div>\n            <table>\n              <thead><tr><th>Access Area</th><th>Permissions</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span>Account &amp; Billing</span></td><td>Full control — manages subscriptions, add-ons, and billing</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Team / Users Tab</span></td><td>Full control — invite, edit, resend, revoke, and remove team members</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>All Rooms</span></td><td>Full control — manages room settings, recordings, elements, and branding across all owned rooms</td></tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>2</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><span>Admin</span> &nbsp;Room Administrator</div>\n          <div>An Admin is a trusted room administrator with their own separate login credentials. They have full control of the room they're assigned to but have no access to account-level settings or the Team / Users Tab.</div>\n          <div>\n            <table>\n              <thead><tr><th>Access Area</th><th>Permissions</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span>Account &amp; Billing</span></td><td>No access</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Team / Users Tab</span></td><td>No access</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Assigned Room</span></td><td>Full room control — room settings, recordings, elements, and branding</td></tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <div>\n            <span>💡</span>\n            <div>\n              <div>Common use case</div>\n              <div>Admins are typically team leaders, business partners, or family members who need full room management capability — running sessions, managing recordings, and customizing the room independently.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>3</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div><span>Moderator</span> &nbsp;Room Moderator</div>\n          <div>A Moderator helps run sessions within their assigned room — managing participants, chat, polls, and elements. They have no account access and limited room configuration rights compared to an Admin.</div>\n          <div>\n            <table>\n              <thead><tr><th>Access Area</th><th>Permissions</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span>Account &amp; Billing</span></td><td>No access</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Team / Users Tab</span></td><td>No access</td></tr>\n                <tr><td><span>Assigned Room</span></td><td>Attendee, chat, and element controls within the room during live sessions</td></tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <div>\n            <span>💡</span>\n            <div>\n              <div>Common use case</div>\n              <div>Moderators are typically team members or assistants who help facilitate meetings — managing the waiting room, handling chat, running polls, and assisting participants during live sessions.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>4</div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Rules Per Room — Maximum 1 Admin &amp; 1 Moderator</div>\n          <div>Each room can have a maximum of <strong>one Admin</strong> and <strong>one Moderator</strong>. Once a slot is filled, that role option is greyed out and unselectable in the invite modal for that room. You must remove the current occupant to open the slot for a new invite.</div>\n          <div>\n            <span>⚠️</span>\n            <div>\n              <div>Plan requirement to add team members</div>\n              <div>Adding an Admin or Moderator to a room requires a <strong>Business Plan</strong> or a <strong>Team Member Add-On</strong>. Basic Plan accounts cannot add team members without purchasing the add-on from Account &amp; Billing.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n        <div>\n          <span>Thanks for your feedback!</span>\n          <div>\n            <button onclick=\"submitFeedback(this,'thanks-c')\">👍 Yes</button>\n            <button onclick=\"submitFeedback(this,'thanks-c')\">👎 No</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    ","text":"Team Members Roles &amp; Permissions All Plans 🕐 3 min read · 📅 Updated April 2026 · ✓ Beginner There are three roles involved in the Team / Users Tab for Meeting Rooms: Owner , Admin , and Moderator . Each role has a distinct level of access. Webinar roles are managed separately and are not covered here. ROLES OVERVIEW 1 Owner &nbsp;Account Owner The account owner has complete control over everything — billing, all rooms, team members, and platform settings. Only the owner can access the Team / Users Tab and manage invitations. Access Area Permissions Account &amp; Billing Full control — manages subscriptions, add-ons, and billing Team / Users Tab Full control — invite, edit, resend, revoke, and remove team members All Rooms Full control — manages room settings, recordings, elements, and branding across all owned rooms 2 Admin &nbsp;Room Administrator An Admin is a trusted room administrator with their own separate login credentials. They have full control of the room they're assigned to but have no access to account-level settings or the Team / Users Tab. Access Area Permissions Account &amp; Billing No access Team / Users Tab No access Assigned Room Full room control — room settings, recordings, elements, and branding 💡 Common use case Admins are typically team leaders, business partners, or family members who need full room management capability — running sessions, managing recordings, and customizing the room independently. 3 Moderator &nbsp;Room Moderator A Moderator helps run sessions within their assigned room — managing participants, chat, polls, and elements. They have no account access and limited room configuration rights compared to an Admin. Access Area Permissions Account &amp; Billing No access Team / Users Tab No access Assigned Room Attendee, chat, and element controls within the room during live sessions 💡 Common use case Moderators are typically team members or assistants who help facilitate meetings — managing the waiting room, handling chat, running polls, and assisting participants during live sessions. 4 Rules Per Room — Maximum 1 Admin &amp; 1 Moderator Each room can have a maximum of one Admin and one Moderator . Once a slot is filled, that role option is greyed out and unselectable in the invite modal for that room. You must remove the current occupant to open the slot for a new invite. ⚠️ Plan requirement to add team members Adding an Admin or Moderator to a room requires a Business Plan or a Team Member Add-On . Basic Plan accounts cannot add team members without purchasing the add-on from Account &amp; Billing. Was this article helpful? Thanks for your feedback! 👍 Yes 👎 No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-d","title":"Managing Your Team Members","blurb":"After inviting team members, you can manage them at any time from the Team / Users Tab .","html":"\n      <div><div></div>Team Members</div>\n      <h1>Managing Your Team Members</h1>\n      <div>\n        <span><span></span>Business Plan</span>\n        <span><span></span>Basic + Add-On</span>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <span>🕐 3 min read</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>📅 Updated April 2026</span>\n        <span>·</span>\n        <span>✓ Beginner</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <p>After inviting team members, you can manage them at any time from the <strong>Team / Users Tab</strong>. Click the <strong>three-dot Actions menu</strong> on any row to access edit, resend, revoke, and remove options.</p>\n\n      <div>\n        <span>📌</span>\n        <div>\n          <div>Only the Account Owner can manage team members</div>\n          <div>Admins and Moderators assigned to rooms cannot access the Team / Users Tab or make any changes to team membership.</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>ACTIONS AVAILABLE</div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>1</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Edit a Team Member</div>\n          <div>Select <strong>Edit</strong> from the <strong>Actions menu (⋮ three dots)</strong> to update a team member's name, room assignment, or role. Edit is available for both <span><span></span>Pending</span> and <span><span></span>Active</span> members. If you change the room or role, the update takes effect immediately — no new invite is sent.</div>\n          <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>2</div>\n        <div></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Resend an Invitation</div>\n          <div>Select <strong>Resend Invite</strong> from the Actions menu to re-send the invitation email to the same address. This option is available only when the member's status is <span><span></span>Pending</span>. A fresh invite link is generated and the previous link is invalidated.</div>\n          <div>\n            <span>💡</span>\n            <div>\n              <div>Invite expires in 7 days</div>\n              <div>Invitation links expire 7 days after they are sent. If the invitee doesn't accept in time, use Resend Invite to generate a new link.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        </div>\n      ","text":"Team Members Managing Your Team Members Business Plan Basic + Add-On 🕐 3 min read · 📅 Updated April 2026 · ✓ Beginner After inviting team members, you can manage them at any time from the Team / Users Tab . Click the three-dot Actions menu on any row to access edit, resend, revoke, and remove options. 📌 Only the Account Owner can manage team members Admins and Moderators assigned to rooms cannot access the Team / Users Tab or make any changes to team membership. ACTIONS AVAILABLE 1 Edit a Team Member Select Edit from the Actions menu (⋮ three dots) to update a team member's name, room assignment, or role. Edit is available for both Pending and Active members. If you change the room or role, the update takes effect immediately — no new invite is sent. Screenshot 2 Resend an Invitation Select Resend Invite from the Actions menu to re-send the invitation email to the same address. This option is available only when the member's status is Pending . A fresh invite link is generated and the previous link is invalidated. 💡 Invite expires in 7 days Invitation links expire 7 days after they are sent. If the invitee doesn't accept in time, use Resend Invite to generate a new link.","headings":[]}],"ai-suite":[],"account-billing":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Billing & Usage Overview","blurb":"Billing & Usage is where you manage your subscription, payment methods, invoices and usage — all inside R-Link Studio.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Billing has moved in-platform</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Subscription management no longer happens in an external customer portal. Everything — plans, payment methods, invoices and usage — is handled inside R-Link Studio on the <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> page.</div></div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-bu-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Open Billing &amp; Usage</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. The page is split into five sections: your current plan, available plans, payment method, usage, and invoice history.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-usage-overview.png\" alt=\"Billing & Usage page showing the Business Plan card and Available Plans\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The top of Billing &amp; Usage — your current plan, its billing dates, and the plans you can switch to.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-bu-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Read Your Plan Card</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">The card at the top shows the plan you are on, whether it is active, and the dates that matter.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">On the plan card</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Plan name &amp; status</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">For example <strong>Business Plan — active</strong>.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Billing</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Monthly or Annual.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Started</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">The date your current subscription began.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Next invoice</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">The date you will next be charged.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Pause Plan</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Pauses billing for 30, 60 or 90 days.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Cancel Subscription</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Ends the subscription at the end of the current billing period.</div></div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-bu-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Payment, Usage and Invoices</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Scroll down for the rest of the page.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-usage-payment-invoices.png\" alt=\"Payment method, usage cards and invoice history\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Payment Method, your usage against plan limits, and Invoice History with downloads.</p><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Lower sections</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Payment Method</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Add a card, set the default, or remove one.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Usage</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Active rooms, storage used and total recordings against your plan limits.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Invoice History</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Every invoice with its date, number, amount, status and a download link.</div></div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 📌 Billing has moved in-platform Subscription management no longer happens in an external customer portal. Everything — plans, payment methods, invoices and usage — is handled inside R-Link Studio on the Billing &amp; Usage page. 1 Open Billing &amp; Usage Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. The page is split into five sections: your current plan, available plans, payment method, usage, and invoice history. ↑ The top of Billing &amp; Usage — your current plan, its billing dates, and the plans you can switch to. 2 Read Your Plan Card The card at the top shows the plan you are on, whether it is active, and the dates that matter. On the plan card Plan name &amp; status For example Business Plan — active . Billing Monthly or Annual. Started The date your current subscription began. Next invoice The date you will next be charged. Pause Plan Pauses billing for 30, 60 or 90 days. Cancel Subscription Ends the subscription at the end of the current billing period. 3 Payment, Usage and Invoices Scroll down for the rest of the page. ↑ Payment Method, your usage against plan limits, and Invoice History with downloads. Lower sections Payment Method Add a card, set the default, or remove one. Usage Active rooms, storage used and total recordings against your plan limits. Invoice History Every invoice with its date, number, amount, status and a download link.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Updating Your Plan","blurb":"Upgrade or downgrade between Basic and Business from the Available Plans section of Billing & Usage.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-plan-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Open Available Plans</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. Scroll to <strong>Available Plans</strong>. Your current plan is marked with a <strong>Current Plan</strong> badge and its button reads <em>This is your current plan</em>.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-usage-overview.png\" alt=\"Available Plans with Basic and Business side by side\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Basic and Business shown side by side. The plan you are on is badged <strong>Current Plan</strong>.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-plan-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Choose the Plan You Want</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Each card lists its price and what is included. Business covers 5 rooms running in parallel, webinars for up to 1,000 attendees, multi-platform live streaming (RTMP) and 50 GB of storage.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-plan-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Click Switch</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click <strong>Switch</strong> on the plan you want to move to. The plan card at the top updates to the new plan, and your next invoice reflects the change.</div><div class=\"callout tip\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">💡</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Check the billing cycle first</div><div class=\"callout-text\">The Monthly / Annual toggle above the plan cards controls which price you are switching to. Set it before you click Switch.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Open Available Plans Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. Scroll to Available Plans . Your current plan is marked with a Current Plan badge and its button reads This is your current plan . ↑ Basic and Business shown side by side. The plan you are on is badged Current Plan . 2 Choose the Plan You Want Each card lists its price and what is included. Business covers 5 rooms running in parallel, webinars for up to 1,000 attendees, multi-platform live streaming (RTMP) and 50 GB of storage. 3 Click Switch Click Switch on the plan you want to move to. The plan card at the top updates to the new plan, and your next invoice reflects the change. 💡 Check the billing cycle first The Monthly / Annual toggle above the plan cards controls which price you are switching to. Set it before you click Switch.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Switching Between Monthly and Annual","blurb":"Change your billing cycle with the Monthly / Annual toggle above the plan cards.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-cycle-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Find the Billing Toggle</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. In the <strong>Available Plans</strong> section, the <strong>Monthly</strong> / <strong>Annual</strong> toggle sits at the top right.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-usage-overview.png\" alt=\"Monthly and Annual toggle above the plan cards\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Monthly / Annual toggle controls the prices shown on both plan cards.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-cycle-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Pick Your Cycle</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click <strong>Annual</strong> or <strong>Monthly</strong>. The prices on the Basic and Business cards update to match.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-cycle-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Confirm With Switch</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click <strong>Switch</strong> on the plan you want. Your plan card at the top then shows the new cycle next to <strong>Billing</strong>, along with your next invoice date.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Find the Billing Toggle Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. In the Available Plans section, the Monthly / Annual toggle sits at the top right. ↑ The Monthly / Annual toggle controls the prices shown on both plan cards. 2 Pick Your Cycle Click Annual or Monthly . The prices on the Basic and Business cards update to match. 3 Confirm With Switch Click Switch on the plan you want. Your plan card at the top then shows the new cycle next to Billing , along with your next invoice date.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Pausing Your Plan","blurb":"Pause billing for 30, 60 or 90 days. Your plan resumes automatically when the pause ends.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pause-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Click Pause Plan</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. On your plan card at the top of the page, click <strong>Pause Plan</strong>.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pause-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Choose How Long</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Select <strong>30 days</strong>, <strong>60 days</strong> or <strong>90 days</strong>, then click <strong>Confirm Pause</strong>. Your plan automatically resumes after the selected time.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-pause-plan.png\" alt=\"Pause your plan dialog with 30, 60 and 90 day options\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:453px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The pause dialog. Pick a length and confirm — no action is needed to restart.</p><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Nothing to remember</div><div class=\"callout-text\">You do not need to come back and un-pause. Billing and access pick up again on their own at the end of the period you chose.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Click Pause Plan Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. On your plan card at the top of the page, click Pause Plan . 2 Choose How Long Select 30 days , 60 days or 90 days , then click Confirm Pause . Your plan automatically resumes after the selected time. ↑ The pause dialog. Pick a length and confirm — no action is needed to restart. 📌 Nothing to remember You do not need to come back and un-pause. Billing and access pick up again on their own at the end of the period you chose.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-4","title":"Cancelling Your Subscription","blurb":"Cancel from your plan card. Your account stays active until the end of the period you have already paid for.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-cancel-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Click Cancel Subscription</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. On your plan card, click <strong>Cancel Subscription</strong> and confirm.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-cancel-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Keep Using It Until the Period Ends</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">If you cancel before your rebilling date, your account stays active until that period is over. Nothing is cut off early.</div><div class=\"callout tip\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">💡</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Pausing instead</div><div class=\"callout-text\">If you only need a break, <strong>Pause Plan</strong> holds your subscription for 30, 60 or 90 days and restarts it for you.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Click Cancel Subscription Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. On your plan card, click Cancel Subscription and confirm. 2 Keep Using It Until the Period Ends If you cancel before your rebilling date, your account stays active until that period is over. Nothing is cut off early. 💡 Pausing instead If you only need a break, Pause Plan holds your subscription for 30, 60 or 90 days and restarts it for you.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-5","title":"Renewing Your Subscription","blurb":"Restart a cancelled subscription from Available Plans, with your rooms, recordings and settings intact.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-renew-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Open Billing &amp; Usage</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. A cancelled subscription still shows its end date on the plan card until the period runs out.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-renew-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Pick a Plan and Switch</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">In <strong>Available Plans</strong>, set the <strong>Monthly</strong> / <strong>Annual</strong> toggle, then click <strong>Switch</strong> on the plan you want. Billing restarts from that point.</div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Your content stays</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Renewing does not create a new workspace. Your rooms, recordings, branding and team members are exactly where you left them.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Open Billing &amp; Usage Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. A cancelled subscription still shows its end date on the plan card until the period runs out. 2 Pick a Plan and Switch In Available Plans , set the Monthly / Annual toggle, then click Switch on the plan you want. Billing restarts from that point. 📌 Your content stays Renewing does not create a new workspace. Your rooms, recordings, branding and team members are exactly where you left them.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-6","title":"Managing Your Payment Method","blurb":"Add a card, set which one is charged, or remove a card you no longer use.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pm-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Find the Payment Method Section</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. Scroll to <strong>Payment Method</strong>. Each saved card shows its brand, last four digits and expiry date.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-usage-payment-invoices.png\" alt=\"Payment Method section with a saved card, Default badge and Remove link\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Saved cards. The one marked <strong>Default</strong> is the card that gets charged.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pm-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Add a Card</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click <strong>+ Add New Card</strong> and enter the card details. The new card is saved to your account and can be used for future invoices.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pm-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Set the Default or Remove a Card</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Use the controls on each card row to manage it.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Card controls</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Default</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Marks the card that will be charged on your next invoice.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Remove</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Deletes the card from your account.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Keep one card on file</div><div class=\"callout-text\">An active subscription needs a valid default card. Add the replacement before removing the old one so a renewal is never missed.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Find the Payment Method Section Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. Scroll to Payment Method . Each saved card shows its brand, last four digits and expiry date. ↑ Saved cards. The one marked Default is the card that gets charged. 2 Add a Card Click + Add New Card and enter the card details. The new card is saved to your account and can be used for future invoices. 3 Set the Default or Remove a Card Use the controls on each card row to manage it. Card controls Default Marks the card that will be charged on your next invoice. Remove Deletes the card from your account. 📌 Keep one card on file An active subscription needs a valid default card. Add the replacement before removing the old one so a renewal is never missed.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-7","title":"Viewing & Downloading Invoices","blurb":"Every invoice is listed under Invoice History with its date, number, amount, status and a download link.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-inv-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Open Invoice History</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. <strong>Invoice History</strong> is at the bottom of the page and lists every invoice on your account.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-usage-payment-invoices.png\" alt=\"Invoice History listing an invoice with amount, paid status and download link\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Each row shows the date, invoice number, amount, status and a <strong>Download</strong> link.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-inv-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Download a Copy</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click <strong>Download</strong> on any row to save that invoice — useful for expense claims and bookkeeping. Click <strong>Refresh</strong> if an invoice you expect has not appeared yet.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Open Invoice History Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. Invoice History is at the bottom of the page and lists every invoice on your account. ↑ Each row shows the date, invoice number, amount, status and a Download link. 2 Download a Copy Click Download on any row to save that invoice — useful for expense claims and bookkeeping. Click Refresh if an invoice you expect has not appeared yet.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-8","title":"Usage & Storage Limits","blurb":"See how much of your plan you are using — active rooms, storage and recordings — at a glance.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-use-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Check Your Usage Cards</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar. Three cards sit between your payment method and invoice history, each showing what you have used against what your plan allows.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/billing-usage-payment-invoices.png\" alt=\"Usage cards showing active rooms, storage used and total recordings\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Usage at a glance — rooms in use, storage consumed and recordings stored.</p><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">What each card shows</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Active Rooms</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Rooms currently in use out of the number your plan allows.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Storage Used</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Recording storage consumed out of your plan allowance.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Total Recordings</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">How many recordings are stored on your account.</div></div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-use-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">If You Are Near a Limit</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Delete recordings you no longer need from <strong>Recordings</strong>, or move to a plan with a higher allowance from <strong>Available Plans</strong>.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Check Your Usage Cards Open the Admin Portal and click Billing &amp; Usage under Account in the left sidebar. Three cards sit between your payment method and invoice history, each showing what you have used against what your plan allows. ↑ Usage at a glance — rooms in use, storage consumed and recordings stored. What each card shows Active Rooms Rooms currently in use out of the number your plan allows. Storage Used Recording storage consumed out of your plan allowance. Total Recordings How many recordings are stored on your account. 2 If You Are Near a Limit Delete recordings you no longer need from Recordings , or move to a plan with a higher allowance from Available Plans .","headings":[]}],"settings-support":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Managing Your Profile","blurb":"Update your photo, display name, phone and timezone from Settings → Profile.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-prof-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Open Settings → Profile</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Settings</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar, then choose the <strong>Profile</strong> tab. The Profile tab holds your photo, personal information and password.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/settings-profile-tab.png\" alt=\"Settings page on the Profile tab showing photo, Personal Information and Password sections\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Profile tab. Settings is also where you find Account, Team &amp; Users and Integrations.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-prof-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Update Your Photo</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click the <strong>Photo</strong> badge on your avatar to upload a new image, or <strong>Remove photo</strong> to clear it. Use a square JPG or PNG, up to 3 MB.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-prof-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Edit Your Personal Information</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Fill in the fields under <strong>Personal Information</strong>, then click <strong>Save Changes</strong>.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Fields</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Display Name</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">The name shown to participants in the studio and on your sessions.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Email</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Your sign-in identity. It is read-only — contact support to change it.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Phone</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Optional contact number.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Timezone</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Used for scheduling and for the times shown across your dashboard.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"callout warn\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">✉️</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Your email cannot be changed</div><div class=\"callout-text\">The <strong>Email</strong> field is read-only — it is your sign-in identity and cannot be updated from Settings. If you need a different email on your account, <strong>contact the support team</strong> and they will update it for you.</div></div></div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Save before you leave</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Changes are only applied when you click <strong>Save Changes</strong>. Navigating away first discards them.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Open Settings → Profile Open the Admin Portal and click Settings under Account in the left sidebar, then choose the Profile tab. The Profile tab holds your photo, personal information and password. ↑ The Profile tab. Settings is also where you find Account, Team &amp; Users and Integrations. 2 Update Your Photo Click the Photo badge on your avatar to upload a new image, or Remove photo to clear it. Use a square JPG or PNG, up to 3 MB. 3 Edit Your Personal Information Fill in the fields under Personal Information , then click Save Changes . Fields Display Name The name shown to participants in the studio and on your sessions. Email Your sign-in identity. It is read-only — contact support to change it. Phone Optional contact number. Timezone Used for scheduling and for the times shown across your dashboard. ✉️ Your email cannot be changed The Email field is read-only — it is your sign-in identity and cannot be updated from Settings. If you need a different email on your account, contact the support team and they will update it for you. 📌 Save before you leave Changes are only applied when you click Save Changes . Navigating away first discards them.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Changing Your Password","blurb":"Change your password from the Password section of Settings → Profile.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pw-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Go to Settings → Profile</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong> and click <strong>Settings</strong> under <strong>Account</strong> in the left sidebar, then choose the <strong>Profile</strong> tab. Scroll down to the <strong>Password</strong> section.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/settings-profile-tab.png\" alt=\"Password section of the Settings Profile tab with current, new and confirm password fields\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Password section sits below Personal Information on the Profile tab.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pw-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Enter Your Passwords</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Type your <strong>Current Password</strong>, then your <strong>New Password</strong> and confirm it. New passwords must be at least 10 characters. Use the eye icon in any field to check what you typed.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-pw-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Click Update Password</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\"><strong>Update Password</strong> becomes available once all three fields are filled. Click it to save the change.</div><div class=\"callout tip\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">💡</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Locked out instead?</div><div class=\"callout-text\">If you cannot sign in at all, use <strong>Forgot Password?</strong> on the login screen — see <a href=\"#getting-started/art-1\">Resetting Your Password</a>.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Go to Settings → Profile Open the Admin Portal and click Settings under Account in the left sidebar, then choose the Profile tab. Scroll down to the Password section. ↑ The Password section sits below Personal Information on the Profile tab. 2 Enter Your Passwords Type your Current Password , then your New Password and confirm it. New passwords must be at least 10 characters. Use the eye icon in any field to check what you typed. 3 Click Update Password Update Password becomes available once all three fields are filled. Click it to save the change. 💡 Locked out instead? If you cannot sign in at all, use Forgot Password? on the login screen — see Resetting Your Password .","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Your Account Settings","blurb":"Organization details, regional defaults, legal links and account deletion — all on the Account tab.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-acct-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Open Settings → Account</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Open the <strong>Admin Portal</strong>, click <strong>Settings</strong> under <strong>Account</strong>, then choose the <strong>Account</strong> tab. This tab covers your organization details, regional defaults, legal links and account deletion.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/settings-account-tab.png\" alt=\"Settings page on the Account tab showing Organization Details, Regional Settings, Legal & Privacy and Danger Zone\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The Account tab — organization details, regional settings, legal links and the Danger Zone.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-acct-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Organization Details</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Set how your organization is identified across R-Link Studio.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Fields</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Company / Organization Name</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Up to 100 characters. Shown in your workspace switcher and on your sessions.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Owner / Admin Name</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Up to 80 characters.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Contact Email</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Locked to the sign-in identity of the owner. Contact support to change it.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Phone</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Optional, up to 20 characters.</div></div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-acct-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Regional Settings</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Choose the <strong>Timezone</strong> and <strong>Default Locale / Language</strong> for the account. These set the defaults used for scheduling and the times shown across your dashboard.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-acct-3\"><div class=\"step-num\">4</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Legal &amp; Privacy</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Links to the <strong>Privacy Policy</strong> and <strong>Terms of Service</strong> sit here, along with a note on how R-Link Studio AI features process meeting transcripts and prompts.</div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-acct-4\"><div class=\"step-num\">5</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Danger Zone</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\"><strong>Delete Account</strong> permanently removes your R-Link Studio account and personal data.</div><div class=\"callout warning\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">⚠️</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">This cannot be undone</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Deleting the account removes your rooms, recordings and settings for good. If you only want to stop being billed, <a href=\"#account-billing/art-3\">pause</a> or <a href=\"#account-billing/art-4\">cancel</a> your plan instead.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Open Settings → Account Open the Admin Portal , click Settings under Account , then choose the Account tab. This tab covers your organization details, regional defaults, legal links and account deletion. ↑ The Account tab — organization details, regional settings, legal links and the Danger Zone. 2 Organization Details Set how your organization is identified across R-Link Studio. Fields Company / Organization Name Up to 100 characters. Shown in your workspace switcher and on your sessions. Owner / Admin Name Up to 80 characters. Contact Email Locked to the sign-in identity of the owner. Contact support to change it. Phone Optional, up to 20 characters. 3 Regional Settings Choose the Timezone and Default Locale / Language for the account. These set the defaults used for scheduling and the times shown across your dashboard. 4 Legal &amp; Privacy Links to the Privacy Policy and Terms of Service sit here, along with a note on how R-Link Studio AI features process meeting transcripts and prompts. 5 Danger Zone Delete Account permanently removes your R-Link Studio account and personal data. ⚠️ This cannot be undone Deleting the account removes your rooms, recordings and settings for good. If you only want to stop being billed, pause or cancel your plan instead.","headings":[]},{"id":"art-3","title":"Support Tickets","blurb":"Search the knowledge base, submit a ticket with attachments, and track its progress from the Support page.","html":"<div class=\"steps\">\n        <div class=\"steps-label\">Step-by-step</div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-sup-0\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Open the Support Page</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click <strong>Support</strong> in the left sidebar of the Admin Portal. The page starts with the self-help resources: the <strong>Learning Center</strong> and a searchable <strong>Knowledge Base &amp; FAQs</strong>.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/support-page-top.png\" alt=\"Help & Support page with the Learning Center banner and Knowledge Base search\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Help &amp; Support. Search the knowledge base first — many questions are already answered there.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-sup-1\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Check the Quick Resources</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Four cards sit below the knowledge base.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Resources</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Documentation</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Comprehensive guides and walkthroughs.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Video Tutorials</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Step-by-step video guides.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Community Forum</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Connect with other R-Link users.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">System Status</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Check service availability — shows <strong>Operational</strong> when everything is running normally.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"callout note\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><div class=\"callout-icon\">📌</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><div class=\"callout-title\">Priority support</div><div class=\"callout-text\">Business plan customers get priority support with faster response times, noted directly on this page.</div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-sup-2\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Fill in the Contact Support Form</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Scroll to <strong>Contact Support</strong> and describe your issue.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/support-contact-form.png\" alt=\"Contact Support form with category, subject, description and attachments\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The ticket form. Attachments make issues much faster to reproduce.</p><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:16px;\"><div style=\"background:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t-4);\">Fields</div></div><div style=\"padding:0 16px 4px;\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Category</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Pick the area your issue belongs to.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Subject</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">A brief description, minimum 3 characters, up to 200.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--bd);\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Description</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Details of the issue, minimum 20 characters, up to 5,000.</div></div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr;gap:8px 16px;padding:9px 0;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t-1);\">Attachments</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--t-3);\">Up to 6 files, 100 MB each. Images (JPG, PNG, GIF, WebP) and videos (MP4, WebM, MOV). Click to upload, drag and drop, or paste a screenshot with Ctrl/Cmd+V.</div></div></div></div>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-sup-3\"><div class=\"step-num\">4</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Submit the Ticket</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\">Click <strong>Submit Ticket</strong>. It becomes available once the required fields meet their minimums. The form is replaced by a <strong>Ticket Submitted!</strong> confirmation and the team follows up by email.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/support-ticket-submitted.png\" alt=\"Ticket Submitted confirmation with a notice that the ticket has been saved\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ The confirmation after submitting. If a notice says delivery to the support system is delayed, the ticket is still saved — do not resubmit.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"step\" id=\"step-sup-4\"><div class=\"step-num\">5</div><div class=\"step-body\">\n            <div class=\"step-title\">Track Your Tickets</div>\n            <div class=\"step-desc\"><strong>Your Support Tickets</strong> lists your recent tickets with their reference number, age and status. Click the arrow on a row to expand it, or <strong>Refresh</strong> to pull the latest updates. The list shows up to 50 of your most recently updated tickets.</div><div class=\"real-screenshot\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\"><img src=\"assets/img/support-your-tickets.png\" alt=\"Your Support Tickets list showing open tickets with reference numbers\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:1225px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/></div><p class=\"ss-caption\">↑ Each ticket shows its reference, when it was last updated, and whether it is still open.</p>\n          </div></div>\n\n        </div>","text":"Step-by-step 1 Open the Support Page Click Support in the left sidebar of the Admin Portal. The page starts with the self-help resources: the Learning Center and a searchable Knowledge Base &amp; FAQs . ↑ Help &amp; Support. Search the knowledge base first — many questions are already answered there. 2 Check the Quick Resources Four cards sit below the knowledge base. Resources Documentation Comprehensive guides and walkthroughs. Video Tutorials Step-by-step video guides. Community Forum Connect with other R-Link users. System Status Check service availability — shows Operational when everything is running normally. 📌 Priority support Business plan customers get priority support with faster response times, noted directly on this page. 3 Fill in the Contact Support Form Scroll to Contact Support and describe your issue. ↑ The ticket form. Attachments make issues much faster to reproduce. Fields Category Pick the area your issue belongs to. Subject A brief description, minimum 3 characters, up to 200. Description Details of the issue, minimum 20 characters, up to 5,000. Attachments Up to 6 files, 100 MB each. Images (JPG, PNG, GIF, WebP) and videos (MP4, WebM, MOV). Click to upload, drag and drop, or paste a screenshot with Ctrl/Cmd+V. 4 Submit the Ticket Click Submit Ticket . It becomes available once the required fields meet their minimums. The form is replaced by a Ticket Submitted! confirmation and the team follows up by email. ↑ The confirmation after submitting. If a notice says delivery to the support system is delayed, the ticket is still saved — do not resubmit. 5 Track Your Tickets Your Support Tickets lists your recent tickets with their reference number, age and status. Click the arrow on a row to expand it, or Refresh to pull the latest updates. The list shows up to 50 of your most recently updated tickets. ↑ Each ticket shows its reference, when it was last updated, and whether it is still open.","headings":[]}],"participant":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Joining a Meeting as a Participant","blurb":"Got an invite to an R-Link Studio meeting? This guide walks you through exactly how to join — whether you're on a desktop browser or using the R-Link Studio mobile app.","html":"\n  <nav><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#elements/art-0\" >Joining as a Participant</a><span>›</span><span>Joining a Meeting as a Participant</span></nav>\n  <div><span></span>Joining as a Participant</div>\n  <h1>Joining a Meeting as a Participant</h1>\n  <div>\n    <span><span></span>All Plans</span>\n    <span><span></span>Guest &amp; Member</span>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg>3 min read</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg>Updated May 2026</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg>Beginner</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Got an invite to an R-Link Studio meeting? This guide walks you through exactly how to join — whether you're on a desktop browser or using the R-Link Studio mobile app. No account required if you're joining as a guest.</p>\n\n  <div>HOW TO JOIN</div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Join via Desktop Browser</div>\n      <p>The easiest way to join a meeting on desktop is directly through your browser — no app download needed.</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>Click the meeting link from your <strong>email invite</strong> or <strong>messaging app</strong> — it will open automatically in your browser. You can also <strong>copy the room link</strong> and paste it directly into your browser's address bar.<br><br>\n<span>\n  <span>Example Meeting URL</span>\n  <code>https://studio.r-link.com/<strong>rally</strong></code>\n  <span>The last part of the URL (<code>rally</code>) is the <strong>Room Name</strong> — you'll also need this if joining via the mobile app.</span>\n</span>\n</span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>The <strong>Pre-Launch Page</strong> will open. Here you can preview your camera, choose your microphone, and see the Room Name.</span></li>\n        <li><span>3</span><span>Type your <strong>name</strong> in the name field.</span></li>\n        <li><span>4</span><span>Click <strong>Join Meeting</strong> to enter the room.</span></li>\n      </ol>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"16\"/></svg></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Before you enter</div>\n          <div><p>On the Pre-Launch Page, make sure your camera and microphone are set correctly. You can toggle them on or off before joining using the icons in the preview area.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Join via Mobile Native App</div>\n      <p>R-Link Studio has a native app available on both iOS and Android. You can join as a signed-in member or as a guest.</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">DOWNLOAD THE APP</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Apple Store</td><td>Search <strong>R-Link Studio</strong> on the App Store and install.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Play Store</td><td>Search <strong>R-Link Studio</strong> on Google Play and install.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n\n      <p>If you have an R-Link account:</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>Open the app and tap <strong>Sign In</strong> under <em>For Members</em>.</span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>Enter your credentials to sign in to your account.</span></li>\n        <li><span>3</span><span>Join the meeting from your dashboard or via the meeting link.</span></li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <p>If you're joining as a guest:</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>Open the app. Under <strong>For Guests</strong>, type the <strong>Room Name</strong> (e.g. <code>rally</code>) and tap <strong>Join</strong>.<br><span>You can also find the room name in the meeting link — e.g. <code>studio.rlink.com/rally</code></span></span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>The <strong>Pre-Launch Page</strong> opens. Set your camera and microphone.</span></li>\n        <li><span>3</span><span>Enter your <strong>name</strong> and tap <strong>Join Meeting</strong>.</span></li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <div>\n        <div>\n          <div>\n            <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n            <div>↑ The R-Link Studio app home screen. Members tap Sign In; guests enter the Room Name and tap Join.</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <div>\n            <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n            <div>↑ The Pre-Launch Page — select your camera and mic, confirm Room Name, enter your name, then tap Join Meeting.</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Join as: Participant vs. Moderator</div>\n          <div><p>On the Pre-Launch Page you'll see a <strong>Join as</strong> toggle at the bottom. Select <strong>Participant</strong> (highlighted in purple) to join as an audience member. The Moderator role is for hosts and co-hosts with a room password.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div>\n      <button><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n","text":"Help Center › Joining as a Participant › Joining a Meeting as a Participant Joining as a Participant Joining a Meeting as a Participant All Plans Guest &amp; Member 3 min read Updated May 2026 Beginner Got an invite to an R-Link Studio meeting? This guide walks you through exactly how to join — whether you're on a desktop browser or using the R-Link Studio mobile app. No account required if you're joining as a guest. HOW TO JOIN 1 Join via Desktop Browser The easiest way to join a meeting on desktop is directly through your browser — no app download needed. 1 Click the meeting link from your email invite or messaging app — it will open automatically in your browser. You can also copy the room link and paste it directly into your browser's address bar. Example Meeting URL https://studio.r-link.com/ rally The last part of the URL ( rally ) is the Room Name — you'll also need this if joining via the mobile app. 2 The Pre-Launch Page will open. Here you can preview your camera, choose your microphone, and see the Room Name. 3 Type your name in the name field. 4 Click Join Meeting to enter the room. Before you enter On the Pre-Launch Page, make sure your camera and microphone are set correctly. You can toggle them on or off before joining using the icons in the preview area. 2 Join via Mobile Native App R-Link Studio has a native app available on both iOS and Android. You can join as a signed-in member or as a guest. DOWNLOAD THE APP Apple Store Search R-Link Studio on the App Store and install. Play Store Search R-Link Studio on Google Play and install. If you have an R-Link account: 1 Open the app and tap Sign In under For Members . 2 Enter your credentials to sign in to your account. 3 Join the meeting from your dashboard or via the meeting link. If you're joining as a guest: 1 Open the app. Under For Guests , type the Room Name (e.g. rally ) and tap Join . You can also find the room name in the meeting link — e.g. studio.rlink.com/rally 2 The Pre-Launch Page opens. Set your camera and microphone. 3 Enter your name and tap Join Meeting . Screenshot ↑ The R-Link Studio app home screen. Members tap Sign In; guests enter the Room Name and tap Join. Screenshot ↑ The Pre-Launch Page — select your camera and mic, confirm Room Name, enter your name, then tap Join Meeting. Join as: Participant vs. Moderator On the Pre-Launch Page you'll see a Join as toggle at the bottom. Select Participant (highlighted in purple) to join as an audience member. The Moderator role is for hosts and co-hosts with a room password. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-1","title":"Registering for a Webinar","blurb":"Some R-Link Studio webinars require registration before you can attend.","html":"\n  <nav><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#elements/art-0\" >Joining as a Participant</a><span>›</span><span>Registering for a Webinar</span></nav>\n  <div><span></span>Joining as a Participant</div>\n  <h1>Registering for a Webinar</h1>\n  <div>\n    <span><span></span>Business Plan</span>\n    <span><span></span>Guest &amp; Member</span>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg>2 min read</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg>Updated May 2026</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg>Beginner</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Some R-Link Studio webinars require registration before you can attend. This article explains how to register, what happens after you submit your details, and the reminder emails you may receive before the session.</p>\n\n  <div>\n    <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"16\"/></svg></div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Registration is optional — set by the host</div>\n      <div><p>Not all webinars require registration. The host decides when setting up the event. If no registration is required, you'll receive a direct join link instead.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z\"/></svg></div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Business Plan feature</div>\n      <div><p>Webinar scheduling and registration is available on the <strong>Business Plan</strong>. If you received a registration link, the host is on a Business Plan and has enabled registration for their event.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>HOW TO REGISTER</div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Open the Registration Link</div>\n      <p>The host will share a webinar registration link with you via email, social media, or messaging. Click or paste the link into your browser to open the registration page.</p>\n      <div>\n        <span>Example Registration URL</span>\n        <code>https://studio.r-link.com/webinar/<strong>idxx-aw7s-2swy</strong>/event</code>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Complete the Registration Form</div>\n      <p>The registration page is customised by the host. It shows the webinar title, date, time, a countdown timer, and a short form asking for your details.</p>\n      <div>\n        <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        <div>↑ An example webinar registration page — the host sets the event image, title, date, and form fields. Fill in your First Name, Last Name, and Email Address, then click <strong>Register</strong>.</div>\n      </div>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>Fill in your <strong>First Name</strong>, <strong>Last Name</strong>, and <strong>Email Address</strong>.</span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>Click the <strong>Register</strong> button to submit your registration.</span></li>\n        <li><span>3</span><span>Already registered? Click <strong>Already registered? Verify your email to join</strong> to retrieve your join link.</span></li>\n      </ol>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>3</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Registration Confirmed — Add to Calendar</div>\n      <p>After clicking <strong>Register</strong>, the page updates to <strong>You're Registered!</strong> and shows the email address your confirmation was sent to. The <strong>Event Time</strong> box lists the start time in your own time zone and in the host's, and a countdown shows how long until the webinar goes live. When the host starts, you'll be let in automatically.</p>\n      <div>\n        <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        <div>↑ The confirmation page: event details on the left; your event time, registration confirmation, countdown and <strong>Add to Calendar</strong> on the right.</div>\n      </div>\n      <p>Click <strong>Add to Calendar</strong> to save the event directly to your preferred calendar app:</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">CALENDAR OPTIONS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Google Calendar</td><td>Opens Google Calendar with the event pre-filled.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Outlook / Office 365</td><td>Opens Outlook or Office 365 calendar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Yahoo Calendar</td><td>Opens Yahoo Calendar with the event details.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Apple Calendar</td><td>Downloads an .ics file that opens in Apple Calendar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Download .ics</td><td>Saves a universal calendar file compatible with any calendar app.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>We recommend adding it to your calendar</div>\n          <div><p>Adding the webinar to your calendar ensures you get a reminder at the right time and have the event details handy. You won't need to search for the confirmation email when it's time to join.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div>If the Host Approves Registrations Manually</div>\n      <p>Some webinars require the host to approve each registration. In that case, after clicking <strong>Register</strong> you'll see <strong>Registration received</strong> instead. There is no countdown or Add to Calendar button yet. You'll receive a confirmation email with your join link once the host approves you.</p>\n      <div>\n        <img src=\"assets/img/webinar-registration-pending.png\" alt=\"Registration received page telling the registrant they will get a confirmation email once approved by the host\"/>\n        <div>↑ The page shown when a webinar uses manual approval.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>4</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Confirmation Email</div>\n      <p>After registering, what happens next depends on how the host configured the webinar:</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">REGISTRATION APPROVAL TYPES</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td>Auto-Approve</td>\n            <td>Your confirmation email with the <strong>join link</strong> is sent immediately after you register.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td>Manual Approval</td>\n            <td>The host reviews your registration first. Your confirmation email is only sent once the host <strong>approves</strong> your request.</td>\n          </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Keep your confirmation email</div>\n          <div><p>Your confirmation email contains the unique <strong>join link</strong> for the webinar. Save it — you'll need it to enter the session on the day.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>5</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Reminder Emails</div>\n      <p>If the host has configured reminders, you will receive automated emails before the webinar starts:</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">REMINDER SCHEDULE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>24 Hours Before</td><td>A reminder email with your join link, sent the day before the webinar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>1 Hour Before</td><td>A final reminder email with your join link, sent one hour before the session starts.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"16\"/></svg></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Reminders are set by the host</div>\n          <div><p>Not all webinars include reminder emails. It depends on how the host configured the event. If you don't receive a reminder, check your confirmation email for the join link.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div>\n      <button><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n","text":"Help Center › Joining as a Participant › Registering for a Webinar Joining as a Participant Registering for a Webinar Business Plan Guest &amp; Member 2 min read Updated May 2026 Beginner Some R-Link Studio webinars require registration before you can attend. This article explains how to register, what happens after you submit your details, and the reminder emails you may receive before the session. Registration is optional — set by the host Not all webinars require registration. The host decides when setting up the event. If no registration is required, you'll receive a direct join link instead. Business Plan feature Webinar scheduling and registration is available on the Business Plan . If you received a registration link, the host is on a Business Plan and has enabled registration for their event. HOW TO REGISTER 1 Open the Registration Link The host will share a webinar registration link with you via email, social media, or messaging. Click or paste the link into your browser to open the registration page. Example Registration URL https://studio.r-link.com/webinar/ idxx-aw7s-2swy /event 2 Complete the Registration Form The registration page is customised by the host. It shows the webinar title, date, time, a countdown timer, and a short form asking for your details. Screenshot ↑ An example webinar registration page — the host sets the event image, title, date, and form fields. Fill in your First Name, Last Name, and Email Address, then click Register . 1 Fill in your First Name , Last Name , and Email Address . 2 Click the Register button to submit your registration. 3 Already registered? Click Already registered? Verify your email to join to retrieve your join link. 3 Registration Confirmed — Add to Calendar After clicking Register , the page updates immediately to show a confirmation message. You'll see a countdown to the webinar and an Add to Calendar button. Screenshot ↑ The confirmation page: event details on the left; your event time, registration confirmation, countdown and <strong>Add to Calendar</strong> on the right. Click Add to Calendar to save the event directly to your preferred calendar app: CALENDAR OPTIONS Google Calendar Opens Google Calendar with the event pre-filled. Outlook / Office 365 Opens Outlook or Office 365 calendar. Yahoo Calendar Opens Yahoo Calendar with the event details. Apple Calendar Downloads an .ics file that opens in Apple Calendar. Download .ics Saves a universal calendar file compatible with any calendar app. We recommend adding it to your calendar Adding the webinar to your calendar ensures you get a reminder at the right time and have the event details handy. You won't need to search for the confirmation email when it's time to join. 4 Confirmation Email After registering, what happens next depends on how the host configured the webinar: REGISTRATION APPROVAL TYPES Auto-Approve Your confirmation email with the join link is sent immediately after you register. Manual Approval The host reviews your registration first. Your confirmation email is only sent once the host approves your request. Keep your confirmation email Your confirmation email contains the unique join link for the webinar. Save it — you'll need it to enter the session on the day. 5 Reminder Emails If the host has configured reminders, you will receive automated emails before the webinar starts: REMINDER SCHEDULE 24 Hours Before A reminder email with your join link, sent the day before the webinar. 1 Hour Before A final reminder email with your join link, sent one hour before the session starts. Reminders are set by the host Not all webinars include reminder emails. It depends on how the host configured the event. If you don't receive a reminder, check your confirmation email for the join link. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]},{"id":"art-2","title":"Joining a Webinar as an Attendee","blurb":"Ready to join a webinar? This guide covers how to enter the room from your confirmation email or event page, what happens when a waiting room is active, and what you can do as an attendee.","html":"\n  <nav><a href=\"https://learn.r-link.com\">Help Center</a><span>›</span><a href=\"#elements/art-0\" >Joining as a Participant</a><span>›</span><span>Joining a Webinar as an Attendee</span></nav>\n  <div><span></span>Joining as a Participant</div>\n  <h1>Joining a Webinar as an Attendee</h1>\n  <div>\n    <span><span></span>All Plans</span>\n    <span><span></span>Attendee &amp; Panelist</span>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg>3 min read</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"16\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"2\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"6\"/><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"/></svg>Updated May 2026</span>\n    <span><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polyline points=\"20 6 9 17 4 12\"/></svg>Beginner</span>\n  </div>\n  <p>Ready to join a webinar? This guide covers how to enter the room from your confirmation email or event page, what happens when a waiting room is active, and what you can do as an attendee once you're inside.</p>\n\n  <div>\n    <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"2\" y=\"3\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\"/><line x1=\"8\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"21\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"21\"/></svg></div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Desktop gives you the best experience</div>\n      <div><p>For the best webinar experience, join from a <strong>desktop browser</strong>. You'll have a full view of the presentation, elements, and all content shared by the host throughout the session.</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>HOW TO JOIN</div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Joining When Registration Was Required</div>\n      <p>If the webinar required registration, you have your own <strong>unique join link</strong>. It's created for you when you register and is included in your confirmation and reminder emails.</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>Open your <strong>confirmation email</strong> or a <strong>reminder email</strong> (sent 24 hours or 1 hour before the webinar).</span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>Click the <strong>join link</strong> in the email. This is unique to your registration and will take you directly into the webinar room — no extra steps needed.</span></li>\n      </ol><div class=\"ss\" style=\"margin-top:16px\"><img src=\"assets/img/webinar-confirmation-email.png\" alt=\"Webinar confirmation email with event name, date, time, Join Webinar button and access link\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:460px;border-radius:10px;display:block;margin:0 auto;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The confirmation email. Click <strong>Join Webinar</strong>, or use the access link below it. The link is unique to you.</div></div><p class=\"ov-desc\" style=\"margin-top:16px\"><strong>Using the registration page instead:</strong> if you go back to the webinar's registration link on the same device and browser you registered with, the page recognises you once the webinar has started. It shows <strong>You're Registered!</strong> with your email address and a <strong>Join Webinar Now</strong> button.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/webinar-registered-live.png\" alt=\"Registration page showing This webinar is live now, You're Registered and a Join Webinar Now button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Returning to the registration page after the webinar starts. Click <strong>Join Webinar Now</strong> to enter. If the email shown isn't yours, click <strong>Not you? Register with a different email</strong>.</div></div><div class=\"co gr\"><div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div><div><div class=\"co-h\">Keep Your Link to Yourself</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Your join link is tied to your registration, so don't forward it. Anyone else who wants to attend should register with their own email to get their own link.</p></div></div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>Joining When Registration Is Not Required</div>\n      <p>If the webinar does not require registration, you join directly from the event landing page when the session goes live.</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li><span>1</span><span>Go back to the <strong>webinar event landing page</strong> link that was shared with you.</span></li>\n        <li><span>2</span><span>Once the webinar is live, the page will update to show a <strong>Join Webinar Now</strong> button. Click it to enter the room immediately.</span></li>\n      </ol>\n      <div>\n        <div role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Screenshot\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"21 15 16 10 5 21\"/></svg><span>Screenshot</span></div>\n        <div>↑ When the webinar is live, the event page shows a green <strong>\"This webinar is live now!\"</strong> banner and a <strong>Join Webinar Now</strong> button. Click it to enter the room.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>3</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>If a Waiting Room Is Active</div>\n      <p>The host may have a <strong>Waiting Room</strong> enabled. If so, clicking your join link will place you in the waiting room instead of the live session directly.</p>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><polyline points=\"12 6 12 12 16 14\"/></svg></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Just wait — the host will let you in</div>\n          <div><p>When a waiting room is active, the host controls when attendees are admitted into the session. Stay on the page and you'll be moved into the webinar automatically once the host lets you in.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span></span>\n  <div>\n    <div>4</div>\n    <div>\n      <div>What You Can Do as an Attendee</div>\n      <p>Webinars are a different experience from meetings. As an attendee, you are a <strong>viewer</strong> — the host controls the stage.</p>\n      <table>\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"3\">ATTENDEE CAPABILITIES</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td>Audio &amp; Video</td>\n            <td>❌ Not available by default. Your camera and microphone are off. You can only go on stage if the <strong>host promotes you</strong> as a panelist or speaker.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td>Chat</td>\n            <td>✅ You can send messages in the chat throughout the session.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td>Reactions &amp; Effects</td>\n            <td>✅ You can interact with the host and other attendees using live reactions and effects.</td>\n          </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div>\n        <div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"/><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"7\" r=\"4\"/><path d=\"M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87\"/><path d=\"M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75\"/></svg></div>\n        <div>\n          <div>Getting promoted to the stage</div>\n          <div><p>If the host invites you on stage, you'll be able to turn on your <strong>camera and microphone</strong> and interact as a panelist or presenter. The host manages all stage promotions during the session.</p></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <span>Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div>\n      <button><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n","text":"Help Center › Joining as a Participant › Joining a Webinar as an Attendee Joining as a Participant Joining a Webinar as an Attendee All Plans Attendee &amp; Panelist 3 min read Updated May 2026 Beginner Ready to join a webinar? This guide covers how to enter the room from your confirmation email or event page, what happens when a waiting room is active, and what you can do as an attendee once you're inside. Desktop gives you the best experience For the best webinar experience, join from a desktop browser . You'll have a full view of the presentation, elements, and all content shared by the host throughout the session. HOW TO JOIN 1 Joining When Registration Was Required If the webinar required registration, your entry point is the join link in your confirmation or reminder email. 1 Open your confirmation email or a reminder email (sent 24 hours or 1 hour before the webinar). 2 Click the join link in the email. This is unique to your registration and will take you directly into the webinar room — no extra steps needed. 2 Joining When Registration Is Not Required If the webinar does not require registration, you join directly from the event landing page when the session goes live. 1 Go back to the webinar event landing page link that was shared with you. 2 Once the webinar is live, the page will update to show a Join Webinar Now button. Click it to enter the room immediately. Screenshot ↑ When the webinar is live, the event page shows a green \"This webinar is live now!\" banner and a Join Webinar Now button. Click it to enter the room. 3 If a Waiting Room Is Active The host may have a Waiting Room enabled. If so, clicking your join link will place you in the waiting room instead of the live session directly. Just wait — the host will let you in When a waiting room is active, the host controls when attendees are admitted into the session. Stay on the page and you'll be moved into the webinar automatically once the host lets you in. 4 What You Can Do as an Attendee Webinars are a different experience from meetings. As an attendee, you are a viewer — the host controls the stage. ATTENDEE CAPABILITIES Audio &amp; Video ❌ Not available by default. Your camera and microphone are off. You can only go on stage if the host promotes you as a panelist or speaker. Chat ✅ You can send messages in the chat throughout the session. Reactions &amp; Effects ✅ You can interact with the host and other attendees using live reactions and effects. Getting promoted to the stage If the host invites you on stage, you'll be able to turn on your camera and microphone and interact as a panelist or presenter. The host manages all stage promotions during the session. Was this article helpful? Yes No","headings":[]}],"integrations":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Integrations Overview","blurb":"What the Integrations tab connects, how the groups are organised, and where to find each connector.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What the Integrations Tab Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The Integrations tab connects R-Link Studio to the tools you already use — your CRM, your calendar, your automation stack, your streaming destinations, your payment processor. Connect once in Settings and the integration is available to every session in the workspace.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-overview.png\" alt=\"The Integrations tab in Settings showing the CRM and Calendar groups\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations. The header counts your presets, connected integrations, and current plan.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"ov-cap\">Find it at <strong>Settings → Integrations</strong> in the left sidebar.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">The Groups</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Every connector sits in a group. Available Now holds the live integrations; Developer Tools sits at the bottom of the page.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">INTEGRATION GROUPS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>CRM</td><td><strong>Go High Level</strong> — push contacts and activity into your CRM.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Calendar</td><td><strong>Google Calendar</strong> — sync scheduled meetings to your calendar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Automation</td><td><strong>Operly</strong> and <strong>Zapier</strong> — send session data into workflows.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Live Streaming</td><td><strong>YouTube Live</strong>, <strong>Facebook Live</strong>, <strong>Twitch</strong>, <strong>LinkedIn Live</strong>, <strong>X Live</strong>, and <strong>Custom RTMP</strong>.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Payments</td><td><strong>Stripe</strong> — connect your account for hosted checkout.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Developer Tools</td><td><strong>Webhooks</strong> and <strong>API Keys</strong> for building against the platform.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connecting and Disconnecting</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Each connector is a card with a short description and a <strong>Connect</strong> button. Once connected, the card shows a green <strong>Connected</strong> badge and the button pair changes to <strong>Configure</strong> and <strong>Disconnect</strong>.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-automation.png\" alt=\"The Automation group with Operly connected and Zapier not yet connected\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Operly is connected — note the badge and the Configure / Disconnect buttons. Zapier still shows Connect.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Connect Before You Schedule</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Connect your calendar and streaming destinations before you schedule anything. A destination saved in Settings shows up as a one-click option when you Go Live, rather than something you scramble to paste in mid-session.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What the Integrations Tab Does The Integrations tab connects R-Link Studio to the tools you already use — your CRM, your calendar, your automation stack, your streaming destinations, your payment processor. Connect once in Settings and the integration is available to every session in the workspace. ↑ Settings → Integrations. The header counts your presets, connected integrations, and current plan. Find it at Settings → Integrations in the left sidebar. 2 The Groups Every connector sits in a group. Available Now holds the live integrations; Developer Tools sits at the bottom of the page. INTEGRATION GROUPS CRM Go High Level — push contacts and activity into your CRM. Calendar Google Calendar — sync scheduled meetings to your calendar. Automation Operly and Zapier — send session data into workflows. Live Streaming YouTube Live , Facebook Live , Twitch , LinkedIn Live , X Live , and Custom RTMP . Payments Stripe — connect your account for hosted checkout. Developer Tools Webhooks and API Keys for building against the platform. 3 Connecting and Disconnecting Each connector is a card with a short description and a Connect button. Once connected, the card shows a green Connected badge and the button pair changes to Configure and Disconnect . ↑ Operly is connected — note the badge and the Configure / Disconnect buttons. Zapier still shows Connect. Pro Tip — Connect Before You Schedule Connect your calendar and streaming destinations before you schedule anything. A destination saved in Settings shows up as a one-click option when you Go Live, rather than something you scramble to paste in mid-session. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-1","title":"Go High Level","blurb":"Connect your CRM so R-Link activity flows into your contacts and pipelines — via the CRM card or an inbound webhook.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Go High Level is a full-featured CRM and marketing automation platform. Connecting it lets R-Link pass session activity — registrants, attendees, and leads — into your CRM so follow-up happens where the rest of your pipeline lives.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-crm.png\" alt=\"The CRM group with the Go High Level card\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → CRM.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Option 1 — Connect the CRM Card</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Go High Level card and authorise R-Link against your Go High Level account. Once the authorisation completes, the card shows a green <strong>Connected</strong> badge.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Use the Right Sub-Account</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Go High Level accounts often have multiple sub-accounts or locations. Authorise the one that holds the pipeline you want R-Link data in — switching later means disconnecting and reconnecting.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Option 2 — Connect via Webhook</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">You can also send R-Link events into Go High Level without using the CRM card, by pointing an R-Link webhook at a Go High Level workflow.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">SETTING IT UP</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>1. In Go High Level</td><td>Open <strong>Automations</strong> and create a workflow.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>2. Choose the trigger</td><td>Select <strong>Inbound Webhook</strong> as the workflow trigger.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>3. Copy the URL</td><td>Go High Level generates a custom inbound webhook URL. Copy it and save the trigger.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>4. In R-Link</td><td>Go to <strong>Settings → Integrations → Webhooks</strong>, click <strong>Configure Webhooks</strong>, and paste the URL as the Endpoint URL.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>5. Pick your events</td><td>Switch on the events you want sent to Go High Level, then click <strong>Add Webhook</strong>.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/ghl-inbound-webhook.png\" alt=\"A Go High Level workflow with an Inbound Webhook trigger and its generated URL\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Inbound Webhook trigger in Go High Level. Copy the generated URL into R-Link's webhook configuration.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Inbound Webhook Is a Premium Trigger</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Go High Level charges per execution for inbound webhook triggers, and caps the payload at 1&nbsp;MB. Subscribe only to the events you actually build automation around.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Publish the Workflow</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>A workflow left in <strong>Draft</strong> will not fire. Use <strong>Test workflow</strong> to confirm the payload arrives, then flip it to <strong>Publish</strong>.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">After Connecting</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Use <strong>Configure</strong> on the card to review the connection, and <strong>Disconnect</strong> to revoke it. Disconnecting stops new data flowing; anything already in your CRM stays there.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Go High Level is a full-featured CRM and marketing automation platform. Connecting it lets R-Link pass session activity — registrants, attendees, and leads — into your CRM so follow-up happens where the rest of your pipeline lives. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → CRM. 3 Option 1 — Connect the CRM Card Click Connect on the Go High Level card and authorise R-Link against your Go High Level account. Once the authorisation completes, the card shows a green Connected badge. Use the Right Sub-Account Go High Level accounts often have multiple sub-accounts or locations. Authorise the one that holds the pipeline you want R-Link data in — switching later means disconnecting and reconnecting. 4 Option 2 — Connect via Webhook You can also send R-Link events into Go High Level without using the CRM card, by pointing an R-Link webhook at a Go High Level workflow. SETTING IT UP 1. In Go High Level Open Automations and create a workflow. 2. Choose the trigger Select Inbound Webhook as the workflow trigger. 3. Copy the URL Go High Level generates a custom inbound webhook URL. Copy it and save the trigger. 4. In R-Link Go to Settings → Integrations → Webhooks , click Configure Webhooks , and paste the URL as the Endpoint URL. 5. Pick your events Switch on the events you want sent to Go High Level, then click Add Webhook . ↑ The Inbound Webhook trigger in Go High Level. Copy the generated URL into R-Link's webhook configuration. Inbound Webhook Is a Premium Trigger Go High Level charges per execution for inbound webhook triggers, and caps the payload at 1&nbsp;MB. Subscribe only to the events you actually build automation around. Pro Tip — Publish the Workflow A workflow left in Draft will not fire. Use Test workflow to confirm the payload arrives, then flip it to Publish . 5 After Connecting Use Configure on the card to review the connection, and Disconnect to revoke it. Disconnecting stops new data flowing; anything already in your CRM stays there. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-2","title":"Google Calendar","blurb":"Sync your scheduled meetings to Google Calendar.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Syncing Google Calendar pushes your scheduled R-Link meetings and webinars into the Google Calendar you choose, with the room link attached, so sessions show up where you already look for them.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Scroll to the <strong>Calendar</strong> group and click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Google Calendar card.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/gcal-connect-modal.png\" alt=\"Google Calendar Integration dialog with the Connect Google Calendar button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Google Calendar Integration dialog. Click <strong>Connect Google Calendar</strong> to open Google sign-in.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Choose Your Google Account</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">A Google sign-in window opens. Pick the account that holds your working calendar, or click <strong>Use another account</strong> to sign in with a different one.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/gcal-choose-account.png\" alt=\"Google account chooser to continue to R-Link Studio\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Choose the Google account to connect.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Continue Past the Verification Warning</div>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Google Verification Is Still Pending</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>R-Link Studio is still awaiting Google's app approval, so Google shows a <strong>Google hasn't verified this app</strong> warning. This is expected and safe to continue. Click <strong>Advanced</strong>, then <strong>Go to R-Link Studio (unsafe)</strong>.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/gcal-unverified.png\" alt=\"Google hasn't verified this app warning with the Go to R-Link Studio (unsafe) link\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Click <strong>Advanced</strong>, then <strong>Go to R-Link Studio (unsafe)</strong> at the bottom.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Sign In and Grant Access</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Confirm the account and click <strong>Continue</strong>. On the next screen, tick <strong>Select all</strong> so R-Link Studio can see your calendars and create events on them, then click <strong>Continue</strong>. The same unverified-app notice appears here too, for the same reason.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/gcal-sign-in.png\" alt=\"Sign in to R-Link Studio screen with Cancel and Continue\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Confirm the account and click <strong>Continue</strong>.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/gcal-access.png\" alt=\"Select what R-Link Studio can access with calendar permissions\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Tick <strong>Select all</strong> to grant both calendar permissions, then click <strong>Continue</strong>.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s6\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">6</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Pick a Calendar Destination</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Back in R-Link, the dialog shows <strong>Connected as</strong> with your Google account. Open <strong>Calendar destination</strong> and choose which of your calendars should receive R-Link events.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/gcal-destination.png\" alt=\"Calendar destination dropdown listing the connected account's calendars\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Choose the calendar R-Link events go to.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s7\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">7</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">After Connecting</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">The Google Calendar card now shows <strong>Connected</strong>. New meetings and webinars you schedule in R-Link appear on the chosen calendar. Use <strong>Configure</strong> to change the destination calendar, or <strong>Disconnect</strong> to stop the sync. Events already on the calendar remain.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/gcal-card.png\" alt=\"Google Calendar card showing Connected with Configure and Disconnect\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The connected card with <strong>Configure</strong> and <strong>Disconnect</strong>.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Scheduling Still Lives in R-Link</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Edit the meeting in R-Link, not in Google Calendar. Changes made on the calendar side do not travel back to the session.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Syncing Google Calendar puts your scheduled R-Link meetings on your calendar automatically, with the room link attached — so the session is where you already look for it. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Calendar. 3 Connect It Click Connect , choose the Google account you want to sync with, and grant R-Link calendar access. Pick the account that holds your working calendar, not a personal one you never open. 4 After Connecting New meetings you schedule in R-Link appear on the connected calendar. Use Disconnect to stop the sync — events already on the calendar remain. Pro Tip — Scheduling Still Lives in R-Link Edit the meeting in R-Link, not in Google Calendar. Changes made on the calendar side do not travel back to the session. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-3","title":"Operly","blurb":"Send recordings, transcripts, leads, and registrations into Operly for AI organisation.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Operly takes what comes out of a session — recordings, transcripts, leads, and registrations — and lets its AI organise it into tasks, notes, and reminders. Instead of a recording sitting in a folder, the follow-up work is already written down.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-automation.png\" alt=\"The Automation group showing Operly connected\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Automation. A connected integration shows the green badge and Configure / Disconnect.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Operly card and authorise the connection. When it succeeds, a green <strong>Connected</strong> badge appears next to the name.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Configure What Gets Sent</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Configure</strong> to review what R-Link pushes across. <strong>Disconnect</strong> stops the flow immediately.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Pairs With the Assistant Key</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Operly also appears under Developer Tools as an <strong>Operly Assistant Key</strong> in API Keys — the key used for programmatic access on the Operly side.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Operly takes what comes out of a session — recordings, transcripts, leads, and registrations — and lets its AI organise it into tasks, notes, and reminders. Instead of a recording sitting in a folder, the follow-up work is already written down. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Automation. A connected integration shows the green badge and Configure / Disconnect. 3 Connect It Click Connect on the Operly card and authorise the connection. When it succeeds, a green Connected badge appears next to the name. 4 Configure What Gets Sent Click Configure to review what R-Link pushes across. Disconnect stops the flow immediately. Pro Tip — Pairs With the Assistant Key Operly also appears under Developer Tools as an Operly Assistant Key in API Keys — the key used for programmatic access on the Operly side. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-4","title":"Zapier","blurb":"Trigger Zaps from meetings, webinars, recordings, registrants, and signed contracts.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Zapier connects R-Link to thousands of other apps without code. A session event fires a Zap, and the Zap does the rest — add a row to a sheet, message a channel, create a task, start an email sequence.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What Can Trigger a Zap</div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">AVAILABLE TRIGGERS</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Meetings</td><td>A meeting is scheduled, started, or ended.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Webinars</td><td>A webinar is scheduled or run.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Recordings</td><td>A recording finishes processing.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Registrants</td><td>Someone registers for a webinar.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Signed contracts</td><td>A contract is signed.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-automation.png\" alt=\"The Automation group with the Zapier card\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Automation.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Zapier card and authorise R-Link in Zapier. Then build your Zap in Zapier, choosing R-Link Studio as the trigger app and picking the event you want.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Start With One Zap</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Wire up a single high-value Zap first — new registrant into your email list, say — and confirm it fires on a real session before building a chain of them.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Zapier connects R-Link to thousands of other apps without code. A session event fires a Zap, and the Zap does the rest — add a row to a sheet, message a channel, create a task, start an email sequence. 2 What Can Trigger a Zap AVAILABLE TRIGGERS Meetings A meeting is scheduled, started, or ended. Webinars A webinar is scheduled or run. Recordings A recording finishes processing. Registrants Someone registers for a webinar. Signed contracts A contract is signed. 3 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Automation. 4 Connect It Click Connect on the Zapier card and authorise R-Link in Zapier. Then build your Zap in Zapier, choosing R-Link Studio as the trigger app and picking the event you want. Pro Tip — Start With One Zap Wire up a single high-value Zap first — new registrant into your email list, say — and confirm it fires on a real session before building a chain of them. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-5","title":"YouTube Live","blurb":"Save your YouTube RTMP server and stream key for one-click Go Live.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Stream your R-Link session straight to your YouTube channel. Save the connection once and YouTube becomes a one-click destination every time you go live.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-livestream.png\" alt=\"The Live Streaming group with six RTMP destinations\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Get Your Stream Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">In YouTube Studio, open <strong>Go Live</strong> and choose the stream you are setting up. The <strong>Stream settings</strong> panel shows your <strong>Stream URL</strong> and <strong>Stream key</strong> — copy both.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the YouTube Live card, paste your details, and save.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT YOU PASTE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>RTMP Server URL</td><td>The ingest endpoint from YouTube.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Key</td><td>The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Keep Your Stream Key Private</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Go Live</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once saved, YouTube Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Test It First</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Stream your R-Link session straight to your YouTube channel. Save the connection once and YouTube becomes a one-click destination every time you go live. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming. 3 Get Your Stream Details In YouTube Studio, open Go Live and choose the stream you are setting up. The Stream settings panel shows your Stream URL and Stream key — copy both. 4 Connect It Click Connect on the YouTube Live card, paste your details, and save. WHAT YOU PASTE RTMP Server URL The ingest endpoint from YouTube. Stream Key The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password. Keep Your Stream Key Private Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here. 5 Go Live Once saved, YouTube Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live. Pro Tip — Test It First Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-6","title":"Facebook Live","blurb":"Stream to Facebook pages, profiles, groups, or events with manual RTMP.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Broadcast your session to a Facebook page, profile, group, or event. R-Link uses manual RTMP, so you choose the destination on the Facebook side.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-livestream.png\" alt=\"The Live Streaming group with six RTMP destinations\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Get Your Stream Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">In Facebook's Live Producer, create a live video and pick <strong>Streaming software</strong>. Facebook shows a <strong>Server URL</strong> and a <strong>Stream key</strong>.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Facebook Live card, paste your details, and save.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT YOU PASTE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>RTMP Server URL</td><td>The ingest endpoint from Facebook.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Key</td><td>The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Keep Your Stream Key Private</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Go Live</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once saved, Facebook Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Test It First</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Broadcast your session to a Facebook page, profile, group, or event. R-Link uses manual RTMP, so you choose the destination on the Facebook side. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming. 3 Get Your Stream Details In Facebook's Live Producer, create a live video and pick Streaming software . Facebook shows a Server URL and a Stream key . 4 Connect It Click Connect on the Facebook Live card, paste your details, and save. WHAT YOU PASTE RTMP Server URL The ingest endpoint from Facebook. Stream Key The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password. Keep Your Stream Key Private Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here. 5 Go Live Once saved, Facebook Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live. Pro Tip — Test It First Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-7","title":"Twitch","blurb":"Save your Twitch ingest endpoint and stream key.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Send your session to your Twitch channel. Useful for long-running community sessions and workshops.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-livestream.png\" alt=\"The Live Streaming group with six RTMP destinations\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Get Your Stream Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">In the Twitch Creator Dashboard, go to <strong>Settings → Stream</strong>. Copy your <strong>Primary Stream key</strong>, and pick the ingest endpoint closest to you from Twitch's ingest list.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Twitch card, paste your details, and save.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT YOU PASTE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>RTMP Server URL</td><td>The ingest endpoint from Twitch.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Key</td><td>The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Keep Your Stream Key Private</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Go Live</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once saved, Twitch appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Test It First</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Send your session to your Twitch channel. Useful for long-running community sessions and workshops. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming. 3 Get Your Stream Details In the Twitch Creator Dashboard, go to Settings → Stream . Copy your Primary Stream key , and pick the ingest endpoint closest to you from Twitch's ingest list. 4 Connect It Click Connect on the Twitch card, paste your details, and save. WHAT YOU PASTE RTMP Server URL The ingest endpoint from Twitch. Stream Key The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password. Keep Your Stream Key Private Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here. 5 Go Live Once saved, Twitch appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live. Pro Tip — Test It First Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-8","title":"LinkedIn Live","blurb":"Publish to LinkedIn Live events using their RTMP setup.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Broadcast to your LinkedIn profile, page, or event. Best for professional audiences and registration-backed events.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-livestream.png\" alt=\"The Live Streaming group with six RTMP destinations\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Get Your Stream Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Create your LinkedIn Live event and choose a third-party streaming tool. LinkedIn issues an <strong>RTMP server URL</strong> and a <strong>stream key</strong> for that specific event.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the LinkedIn Live card, paste your details, and save.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT YOU PASTE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>RTMP Server URL</td><td>The ingest endpoint from LinkedIn.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Key</td><td>The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Keep Your Stream Key Private</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Go Live</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once saved, LinkedIn Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Keys Are Per-Event</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>LinkedIn issues a new stream key for each event. Update the connection in R-Link before each broadcast rather than assuming the saved key still works.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Broadcast to your LinkedIn profile, page, or event. Best for professional audiences and registration-backed events. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming. 3 Get Your Stream Details Create your LinkedIn Live event and choose a third-party streaming tool. LinkedIn issues an RTMP server URL and a stream key for that specific event. 4 Connect It Click Connect on the LinkedIn Live card, paste your details, and save. WHAT YOU PASTE RTMP Server URL The ingest endpoint from LinkedIn. Stream Key The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password. Keep Your Stream Key Private Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here. 5 Go Live Once saved, LinkedIn Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live. Keys Are Per-Event LinkedIn issues a new stream key for each event. Update the connection in R-Link before each broadcast rather than assuming the saved key still works. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-9","title":"X Live","blurb":"Save an X live producer RTMP destination.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Stream your session to X. The connection uses X's live producer RTMP destination.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-livestream.png\" alt=\"The Live Streaming group with six RTMP destinations\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Get Your Stream Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">In X's live producer, create a broadcast and open its source settings. Copy the <strong>RTMP URL</strong> and <strong>stream key</strong> it issues.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the X Live card, paste your details, and save.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT YOU PASTE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>RTMP Server URL</td><td>The ingest endpoint from X.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Key</td><td>The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Keep Your Stream Key Private</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Go Live</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once saved, X Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Test It First</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Stream your session to X. The connection uses X's live producer RTMP destination. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming. 3 Get Your Stream Details In X's live producer, create a broadcast and open its source settings. Copy the RTMP URL and stream key it issues. 4 Connect It Click Connect on the X Live card, paste your details, and save. WHAT YOU PASTE RTMP Server URL The ingest endpoint from X. Stream Key The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password. Keep Your Stream Key Private Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here. 5 Go Live Once saved, X Live appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live. Pro Tip — Test It First Run a short private session and check that the stream lands on the right channel before your real event. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-10","title":"Custom RTMP","blurb":"Add any RTMP or RTMPS destination from a third-party provider.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Stream to any platform that accepts RTMP or RTMPS — a restreaming service, an internal media server, a regional platform, or a client's own infrastructure.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-livestream.png\" alt=\"The Live Streaming group with six RTMP destinations\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Get Your Stream Details</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Ask your provider for the <strong>ingest URL</strong> and <strong>stream key</strong>. RTMPS endpoints are supported as well as plain RTMP.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Custom RTMP card, paste your details, and save.</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">WHAT YOU PASTE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>RTMP Server URL</td><td>The ingest endpoint from Custom RTMP.</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Stream Key</td><td>The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Keep Your Stream Key Private</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Go Live</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Once saved, Custom RTMP appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Use a Restreamer for Multiple Destinations</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>If you need several platforms at once, point Custom RTMP at a restreaming service and let it fan the stream out, rather than managing each destination separately.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Stream to any platform that accepts RTMP or RTMPS — a restreaming service, an internal media server, a regional platform, or a client's own infrastructure. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Live Streaming. 3 Get Your Stream Details Ask your provider for the ingest URL and stream key . RTMPS endpoints are supported as well as plain RTMP. 4 Connect It Click Connect on the Custom RTMP card, paste your details, and save. WHAT YOU PASTE RTMP Server URL The ingest endpoint from Custom RTMP. Stream Key The private key for your stream. Treat it like a password. Keep Your Stream Key Private Anyone with your stream key can broadcast to your channel. Never share it in chat or on screen. If it leaks, reset it from your streaming platform and reconnect here. 5 Go Live Once saved, Custom RTMP appears as a destination in the studio. Select it before you start, and R-Link pushes your stream there as soon as you Go Live. Pro Tip — Use a Restreamer for Multiple Destinations If you need several platforms at once, point Custom RTMP at a restreaming service and let it fan the stream out, rather than managing each destination separately. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-11","title":"Stripe","blurb":"Connect your Stripe account so R-Link can route hosted checkout flows to your workspace.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What This Connection Does</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Connecting Stripe lets R-Link route future hosted checkout flows to your own Stripe account, so payments taken around your sessions land directly in your workspace.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find the Connector</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Open the left sidebar, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then the <strong>Integrations</strong> tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-payments.png\" alt=\"The Payments group with the Stripe card\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Payments.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Connect It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Connect</strong> on the Stripe card and complete the Stripe authorisation. You will need an existing Stripe account with payouts enabled.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">This Is Not Your R-Link Subscription</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Connecting Stripe here is about money you collect from your audience. Your own R-Link plan and payment method live in <strong>Billing &amp; Usage</strong>, and the two are unrelated.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What This Connection Does Connecting Stripe lets R-Link route future hosted checkout flows to your own Stripe account, so payments taken around your sessions land directly in your workspace. 2 Find the Connector Open the left sidebar, go to Settings , then the Integrations tab. Integrations are grouped by what they do — scroll to the group below, or use the counter in the header to see how many you have connected. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Payments. 3 Connect It Click Connect on the Stripe card and complete the Stripe authorisation. You will need an existing Stripe account with payouts enabled. This Is Not Your R-Link Subscription Connecting Stripe here is about money you collect from your audience. Your own R-Link plan and payment method live in Billing &amp; Usage , and the two are unrelated. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-12","title":"Webhooks","blurb":"Receive real-time event notifications as signed HTTP callbacks.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What Webhooks Do</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Webhooks send HTTP callbacks to a URL you control when something happens in R-Link — room creation, recording completion, participant joins, registrations, and more. Each request is signed with <strong>HMAC-SHA256</strong> so you can verify it came from R-Link.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Find It</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Webhooks sit under <strong>Developer Tools</strong> at the bottom of the Integrations tab.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-webhooks.png\" alt=\"The Webhooks panel showing one active webhook endpoint\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Developer Tools. Active endpoints are listed on the right.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Add an Endpoint</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Configure Webhooks</strong> to open the Webhook Configuration dialog. Paste your <strong>Endpoint URL</strong>, switch on the events you want, and click <strong>Add Webhook</strong>.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-webhook-config.png\" alt=\"The Webhook Configuration dialog with an endpoint URL field and fifteen event toggles\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:560px;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Webhook Configuration. All events are on by default — switch off what you do not need.</div></div>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">EVENTS TO SUBSCRIBE</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Meeting Scheduled</td><td>When a meeting is scheduled</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Webinar Scheduled</td><td>When a webinar is scheduled</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Room Created</td><td>When a new room is created</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Room Started</td><td>When a room session starts</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Room Ended</td><td>When a room session ends</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Participant Joined</td><td>When someone joins a room</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Participant Left</td><td>When someone leaves a room</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Recording Started</td><td>When recording begins</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Recording Completed</td><td>When recording is ready</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Registration Created</td><td>When someone registers</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Meeting Registrant Created</td><td>Production-compatible meeting registrant webhook</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Webinar Registrant Created</td><td>Production-compatible webinar registrant webhook</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Attendance Recorded</td><td>When attendee lifecycle state is recorded</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Replay Viewed</td><td>When an attendee accesses event replay</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Engagement Updated</td><td>When attendee engagement metrics change</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Subscribe Narrowly</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Leaving every event on means your endpoint handles traffic it will ignore. Turn on only the events you act on — you can come back and add more later.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Verify the Signature</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Every request includes an <code>X-RLink-Signature</code> HMAC-SHA256 header. Verify it on your side before acting on the payload — it is the only thing that proves the callback is genuinely from R-Link.</p>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Respond Quickly</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Your endpoint should acknowledge the callback fast and do the real work asynchronously. Slow endpoints cause retries and duplicate processing.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What Webhooks Do Webhooks send HTTP callbacks to a URL you control when something happens in R-Link — room creation, recording completion, participant joins, registrations, and more. Each request is signed with HMAC-SHA256 so you can verify it came from R-Link. 2 Find It Webhooks sit under Developer Tools at the bottom of the Integrations tab. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Developer Tools. Active endpoints are listed on the right. 3 Add an Endpoint Click Configure Webhooks to open the Webhook Configuration dialog. Paste your Endpoint URL , switch on the events you want, and click Add Webhook . ↑ Webhook Configuration. All events are on by default — switch off what you do not need. EVENTS TO SUBSCRIBE Meeting Scheduled When a meeting is scheduled Webinar Scheduled When a webinar is scheduled Room Created When a new room is created Room Started When a room session starts Room Ended When a room session ends Participant Joined When someone joins a room Participant Left When someone leaves a room Recording Started When recording begins Recording Completed When recording is ready Registration Created When someone registers Meeting Registrant Created Production-compatible meeting registrant webhook Webinar Registrant Created Production-compatible webinar registrant webhook Attendance Recorded When attendee lifecycle state is recorded Replay Viewed When an attendee accesses event replay Engagement Updated When attendee engagement metrics change Pro Tip — Subscribe Narrowly Leaving every event on means your endpoint handles traffic it will ignore. Turn on only the events you act on — you can come back and add more later. 4 Verify the Signature Every request includes an X-RLink-Signature HMAC-SHA256 header. Verify it on your side before acting on the payload — it is the only thing that proves the callback is genuinely from R-Link. Respond Quickly Your endpoint should acknowledge the callback fast and do the real work asynchronously. Slow endpoints cause retries and duplicate processing. Was this article helpful? Yes No"},{"id":"art-13","title":"API Keys","blurb":"Create and manage keys for programmatic access to the public API.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">What API Keys Are For</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">An API key lets your own software make programmatic requests against the R-Link public API. Keys are managed under <strong>Developer Tools</strong> at the bottom of the Integrations tab.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Create a Key</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Create New Key</strong>. The key is shown once, at creation — copy it then and store it somewhere safe.</p>\n      <div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/int-apikeys.png\" alt=\"The API Keys panel with no keys yet and the Create New Key button\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Settings → Integrations → Developer Tools → API Keys.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"co am\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Shown in Full Only Once</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>If you lose a key you cannot recover it. Create a replacement and update whatever was using the old one.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">Use the Key</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\">Pass the key as a Bearer token on every request:</p>\n      <table class=\"dt\">\n        <thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"dt-head\">AUTHORISATION HEADER</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Header</td><td><code>Authorization: Bearer rlink_live_…</code></td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span>\n  <div class=\"ov-sec\">\n    <div class=\"ov-num\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"ov-body\">\n      <div class=\"ov-title\">The Operly Assistant Key</div>\n      <p class=\"ov-desc\"><strong>Operly Assistant Key</strong> sits beside Create New Key. It issues the key Operly uses for programmatic access, so you do not have to create and paste one by hand.</p>\n      <div class=\"co gr\">\n        <div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div>\n        <div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — One Key per System</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Give each system its own key. When something needs to be revoked you can kill that one key without breaking everything else you have built.</p></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fb-row\">\n    <span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span>\n    <div class=\"fb-btns\">\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button>\n      <button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\">        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner OVERVIEW 1 What API Keys Are For An API key lets your own software make programmatic requests against the R-Link public API. Keys are managed under Developer Tools at the bottom of the Integrations tab. 2 Create a Key Click Create New Key . The key is shown once, at creation — copy it then and store it somewhere safe. ↑ Settings → Integrations → Developer Tools → API Keys. Shown in Full Only Once If you lose a key you cannot recover it. Create a replacement and update whatever was using the old one. 3 Use the Key Pass the key as a Bearer token on every request: AUTHORISATION HEADER Header Authorization: Bearer rlink_live_… 4 The Operly Assistant Key Operly Assistant Key sits beside Create New Key. It issues the key Operly uses for programmatic access, so you do not have to create and paste one by hand. Pro Tip — One Key per System Give each system its own key. When something needs to be revoked you can kill that one key without breaking everything else you have built. Was this article helpful? Yes No"}],"affiliate":[{"id":"art-0","title":"Joining the Affiliate Program","blurb":"Where to find the Affiliate page and what's on it.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n<span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">1</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Who Can Join</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Anyone with an active R-Link Studio subscription is automatically part of the Affiliate Program. There is nothing to apply for: your affiliate link is created for you.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">2</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Open the Affiliate Page</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">In the <strong>Admin Portal</strong>, click <strong>Affiliate</strong> under <strong>Grow</strong> in the left sidebar. Your referral link is already there, ready to share.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/aff-overview.png\" alt=\"Affiliate page with the Referrals header, Overview/Conversions/Payouts tabs and the referral link card\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Affiliate page. Your referral link sits on the <strong>Overview</strong> tab.</div></div></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">3</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">The Three Tabs</div><p class=\"ov-desc\"><strong>Overview</strong> holds your referral link, your stats, a performance chart, and recent activity. <strong>Conversions</strong> lists the people who signed up through your link. <strong>Payouts</strong> shows what you've been paid.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">4</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">White Label Partners</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">The Referrals header also covers the White Label Program. If you refer a White Label partner, use the White Label Program link shown on the same page.</p></div></div><div class=\"fb-row\"><span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span><div class=\"fb-btns\"><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button></div></div>","text":"All Plans 2 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner  OVERVIEW 1 Who Can Join Anyone with an active R-Link Studio subscription is automatically part of the Affiliate Program. There is nothing to apply for: your affiliate link is created for you. 2 Open the Affiliate Page In the Admin Portal , click Affiliate under Grow in the left sidebar. Your referral link is already there, ready to share. ↑ The Affiliate page. Your referral link sits on the Overview tab. 3 The Three Tabs Overview holds your referral link, your stats, a performance chart, and recent activity. Conversions lists the people who signed up through your link. Payouts shows what you've been paid. 4 White Label Partners The Referrals header also covers the White Label Program. If you refer a White Label partner, use the White Label Program link shown on the same page. Was this article helpful? Yes No "},{"id":"art-1","title":"Getting Your Referral Link","blurb":"Copy, rename, and share your personal referral link.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">STEP-BY-STEP</div>\n<span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">1</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Find Your Link</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Open <strong>Affiliate</strong> and stay on the <strong>Overview</strong> tab. The <strong>Your R-Link Studio Referral Link</strong> card shows your tracked link. The badge in the top-right corner is your referral code.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/aff-overview.png\" alt=\"Affiliate page with the Referrals header, Overview/Conversions/Payouts tabs and the referral link card\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Affiliate page. Your referral link sits on the <strong>Overview</strong> tab.</div></div></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">2</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Copy It</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Copy</strong> to put the link on your clipboard. Anyone who signs up through it is credited to you automatically.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">3</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Rename It</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Rename</strong> to change the end of the link to something easier to remember, such as your business name.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">4</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Share It</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Use the buttons below the link to share straight to <strong>X</strong>, <strong>LinkedIn</strong>, <strong>Facebook</strong>, or <strong>Email</strong>. Click <strong>QR Code</strong> to get a scannable code for slides, print, or in-person events.</p><div class=\"co gr\"><div class=\"co-ico\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><polygon points=\"12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2\"/></svg></div><div><div class=\"co-h\">Pro Tip — Share It in Your Sessions</div><div class=\"co-t\"><p>Put the QR code on a slide or drop the link in chat during your own webinars. Attendees see R-Link Studio in action right before they see the link.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"fb-row\"><span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span><div class=\"fb-btns\"><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button></div></div>","text":"All Plans 2 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner  STEP-BY-STEP 1 Find Your Link Open Affiliate and stay on the Overview tab. The Your R-Link Studio Referral Link card shows your tracked link. The badge in the top-right corner is your referral code. ↑ The Affiliate page. Your referral link sits on the Overview tab. 2 Copy It Click Copy to put the link on your clipboard. Anyone who signs up through it is credited to you automatically. 3 Rename It Click Rename to change the end of the link to something easier to remember, such as your business name. 4 Share It Use the buttons below the link to share straight to X , LinkedIn , Facebook , or Email . Click QR Code to get a scannable code for slides, print, or in-person events. Pro Tip — Share It in Your Sessions Put the QR code on a slide or drop the link in chat during your own webinars. Attendees see R-Link Studio in action right before they see the link. Was this article helpful? Yes No "},{"id":"art-2","title":"Your Affiliate Dashboard","blurb":"Track clicks, conversions, balance, and recent activity.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n<span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">1</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Summary Cards</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Scroll down the <strong>Overview</strong> tab to four cards: <strong>Clicks</strong> on your link, <strong>Conversions</strong> with the number of active subscribers, <strong>Conv. Rate</strong> (conversions divided by clicks), and <strong>Pending Balance</strong> with your lifetime earnings underneath.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/aff-stats.png\" alt=\"Clicks, Conversions, Conv. Rate and Pending Balance cards above the Payout Progress bar and Performance chart\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Summary cards, payout progress, and the Performance chart.</div></div></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">2</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Payout Progress</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">The bar shows how close your pending balance is to <strong>$100.00</strong>, the minimum for a payout request.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">3</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Performance</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">The chart plots your activity over time. Switch between <strong>7d</strong>, <strong>30d</strong>, and <strong>90d</strong> in the top-right corner. It reads <em>No activity in this period</em> when nothing happened in the selected range.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">4</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Recent Activity</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">At the bottom of the page, every event is listed with how long ago it happened and a status badge, such as <strong>tracked</strong> for a recorded click. Filter the list with <strong>All Activity</strong>, <strong>Clicks</strong>, <strong>Conversions</strong>, or <strong>Payouts</strong>.</p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/aff-activity.png\" alt=\"Recent Activity list of referral link clicks with tracked badges and filter buttons\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ Recent Activity with its filters.</div></div></div></div><span id=\"f-s5\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">5</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Conversions Tab</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Click <strong>Conversions</strong> to see everyone who signed up through your link. Each card shows the account name, its plan, and a status badge such as <strong>active</strong>. The progress bar tracks how many of the 12 commission months have been paid, with the start date on the right. Click the arrow to expand a card. Until your first referral subscribes, the tab reads <em>No conversions yet. Share your link to start earning.</em></p><div class=\"ss\"><img src=\"assets/img/aff-conversions.png\" alt=\"Conversions tab listing referred accounts with plan, status and months paid\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;border-radius:10px;display:block;\"/><div class=\"ss-cap\">↑ The Conversions tab with three referred accounts.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"fb-row\"><span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span><div class=\"fb-btns\"><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button></div></div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner  OVERVIEW 1 Summary Cards Scroll down the Overview tab to four cards: Clicks on your link, Conversions with the number of active subscribers, Conv. Rate (conversions divided by clicks), and Pending Balance with your lifetime earnings underneath. ↑ Summary cards, payout progress, and the Performance chart. 2 Payout Progress The bar shows how close your pending balance is to the $100.00 payout threshold. 3 Performance The chart plots your activity over time. Switch between 7d , 30d , and 90d in the top-right corner. It reads No activity in this period when nothing happened in the selected range. 4 Recent Activity At the bottom of the page, every event is listed with how long ago it happened and a status badge, such as tracked for a recorded click. Filter the list with All Activity , Clicks , Conversions , or Payouts . ↑ Recent Activity with its filters. Was this article helpful? Yes No  Conversions Tab Click Conversions to see everyone who signed up through your link."},{"id":"art-3","title":"Commissions & Payout Schedule","blurb":"How commissions are calculated and when they're paid.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">OVERVIEW</div>\n<span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">1</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">How Commissions Work</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">You earn <strong>10%</strong> of each referred customer's subscription payment for the first <strong>12 months</strong> of their subscription. The <strong>Conversions</strong> tab shows how many of those months have been paid for each account. New earnings appear in <strong>Pending Balance</strong> on the Overview tab.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">2</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Payout Threshold</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Once your pending balance reaches <strong>$100.00</strong>, you can send a payout request from the <strong>Payouts</strong> tab. The <strong>Payout Progress</strong> bar on the Overview tab shows how close you are. Balances below $100 carry over until you reach it.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">3</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Requesting a Payout</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Payouts aren't sent automatically. When you're over the threshold, request a payout on the <strong>Payouts</strong> tab. Requested and completed payouts are listed there.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">4</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Refunds and Cancellations</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">If a referred customer is refunded, the commission for that payment is removed. If they cancel, you keep commissions already earned, and they stop counting as an active subscriber.</p></div></div><div class=\"fb-row\"><span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span><div class=\"fb-btns\"><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button></div></div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner  OVERVIEW 1 How Commissions Work You earn  of each referred customer's subscription payment for  . New earnings appear in Pending Balance on the Overview tab. 2 Payout Threshold A payout is sent once your pending balance reaches $100.00 . The Payout Progress bar tracks this. Balances below the threshold carry over until you reach it. 3 Payout Schedule Payouts are sent  . Completed payouts are listed on the Payouts tab.  Payouts tab 4 Refunds and Cancellations If a referred customer is refunded, the commission for that payment is removed. If they cancel, you keep commissions already earned, and they stop counting as an active subscriber.  Was this article helpful? Yes No "},{"id":"art-4","title":"Payout Methods & Tax Info","blurb":"Set up how you get paid and submit the tax details required for payouts.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">STEP-BY-STEP</div>\n<span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">1</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Open the Payouts Tab</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">On the Affiliate page, click <strong>Payouts</strong>.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">2</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Choose a Payout Method</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Select your payout method and enter your account details. Click <strong>Save</strong>.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">3</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Submit Tax Information</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Payouts can't be sent until your tax form is on file.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s4\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">4</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Check Payout Status</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Past payouts are listed with their date, amount, and status. If a payout fails, check that your payout details are correct and complete.</p></div></div><div class=\"fb-row\"><span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span><div class=\"fb-btns\"><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button></div></div>","text":"All Plans 3 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner  STEP-BY-STEP 1 Open the Payouts Tab On the Affiliate page, click Payouts .  Payouts tab with payout settings 2 Choose a Payout Method Select  and enter your account details, for example you@yourbusiness.com for PayPal. Click Save . 3 Submit Tax Information Payouts can't be sent until your tax form is on file.  4 Check Payout Status Past payouts are listed with their date, amount, and status. If a payout fails, check that your payout details are correct and complete. Was this article helpful? Yes No "},{"id":"art-5","title":"Program Terms & FAQ","blurb":"The rules of the program and answers to common questions.","html":"<div class=\"ov-label\">FAQ</div>\n<span id=\"f-s1\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">1</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Why don't my clicks show as conversions?</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">A click becomes a conversion only when that person creates an account and subscribes through your link. If they sign up on a different device or clear their cookies first, the referral may not be tracked.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s2\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">2</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Can I refer myself or my own team?</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">No. Self-referrals and referrals of accounts you own or manage don't earn commissions.</p></div></div>\n<span id=\"f-s3\" style=\"display:block;visibility:hidden;height:0\"></span><div class=\"ov-sec\"><div class=\"ov-num\">3</div><div class=\"ov-body\"><div class=\"ov-title\">Who do I contact with questions?</div><p class=\"ov-desc\">Reach out through <strong>Support</strong> in the Admin Portal sidebar.</p></div></div><div class=\"fb-row\"><span class=\"fb-label\">Was this article helpful?</span><div class=\"fb-btns\"><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='👍 Thanks!'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3H14z\"/><path d=\"M7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3\"/></svg>Yes</button><button class=\"fb-btn\" onclick=\"this.innerHTML='Thanks for letting us know'\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3H10z\"/><path d=\"M17 2h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17\"/></svg>No</button></div></div>","text":"All Plans 4 min read Updated September 2026 ✓ Beginner  FAQ 1 Why don't my clicks show as conversions? A click becomes a conversion only when that person creates an account and subscribes through your link. If they sign up on a different device or clear their cookies first, the referral may not be tracked.  2 Can I refer myself or my own team? No. Self-referrals and referrals of accounts you own or manage don't earn commissions.  3 Who do I contact with questions? Reach out through Support in the Admin Portal sidebar. Was this article helpful? Yes No "}]};
